        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7071> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1144689>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q207849> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/chaos_script>,
        <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1026.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Li Bai’s 'Drink Alone Under the Moon'; 'Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Sky' (《月下独酌》,《把酒问月》)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of two iconic poems by Li Bai 李白 (701–762): \"Drink Alone Under the Moon\" (Yue xia duzhuo 月下独酌) and \"Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Moon\" (Ba jiu wen yue 把酒问月). Wang Dongling uses bright red acylic on a six-fold screen of gold leaf to render both texts in his distinctive Chaos Script (luanshu 乱书), a radical, gestural style that abstracts the traditional strokes of Chinese characters into dynamic, expressive forms.  The result is almost illegible, flowing lines interwining and overlapping, evoking both the exuberance  and the spiritual freedom of Li Bai's verses."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q897> ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon true ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing",
        "Set of signs (illegible)" ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/1026_HR.jpg> ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1025> ;
    ns1:madeUsingTool <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q614467> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 182 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """A pot of wine among the flowers.\r
I drink alone, no friend with me.\r
I raise my cup to invite the moon.\r
He and my shadow and I make three.\r
The moon does not know how to drink;\r
My shadow mimes my capering;\r
But I'll make merry with them both -\r
And soon enough it will be Spring.\r
I sing - the moon moves to and fro.\r
I dance - my shadow leaps and sways.\r
Still sober, we exchange our joys.\r
Drunk - and we'll go our separate ways.\r
Let's pledge - beyond human ties - to be friends,\r
And meet where the Silver River ends.\r
(translation by Vikram Seth)"""@en,
        """How long has the bright moon graced the sky?\r
Tonight I set down my cup and ask.\r
Man may strive to reach the radiant moon, yet fail;\r
Still, she moves on, silently following us below.\r
\r
She shines, pure as a flying mirror over crimson halls,\r
The green mists vanish, and her clear light pours forth.\r
At night, I see her rising from the sea’s horizon;\r
Who knows where she sinks at dawn among the clouds?\r
\r
The white rabbit pounds the elixir, autumn after spring;\r
Chang’e dwells alone—who shares her lonely home?\r
We of today cannot see the moon of ages past,\r
Yet this same moon once shone on people long ago.\r
\r
Ancient and modern pass like flowing water;\r
But all gaze at the same bright moon alike.\r
Would that as I sing and lift my wine,\r
Her light might forever shine into my golden cup.\r
(translation by Xu Yuanzhong)"""@en,
        """《把酒問月》\r
青天有月來幾時？我今停杯一問之。\r
人攀明月不可得，月行卻與人相隨。\r
皎如飛鏡臨丹闕，綠煙滅盡清輝發。\r
但見宵從海上來，寧知曉向雲間沒。\r
白兔搗藥秋復春，嫦娥孤棲與誰鄰？\r
今人不見古時月，今月曾經照古人。\r
古人今人若流水，共看明月皆如此。\r
唯願當歌對酒時，月光長照金樽裡。"""@zh,
        """《把酒问月》\r
青天有月来几时？我今停杯一问之。\r
人攀明月不可得，月行却与人相随。\r
皎如飞镜临丹阙，绿烟灭尽清辉发。\r
但见宵从海上来，宁知晓向云间没。\r
白兔捣药秋复春，嫦娥孤栖与谁邻？\r
今人不见古时月，今月曾经照古人。\r
古人今人若流水，共看明月皆如此。\r
唯愿当歌对酒时，月光长照金樽里。"""@zh,
        """《月下独酌》\r
花间一壶酒，独酌无相亲。\r
举杯邀明月，对影成三人。 \r
月既不解饮，影徒随我身。 \r
暂伴月将影，行乐须及春。 \r
我歌月徘徊，我舞影零乱。 \r
醒时同交欢，醉后各分散。 \r
永结无情游，相期邈云汉。"""@zh,
        """《月下獨酌》\r
花間一壺酒，獨酌無相親。\r
舉杯邀明月，對影成三人。\r
月既不解飲，影徒隨我身。\r
暫伴月將影，行樂須及春。\r
我歌月徘徊，我舞影零亂。\r
醒時同交歡，醉後各分散。\r
永結無情遊，相期邈雲漢。"""@zh,
        """“Bǎ jiǔ wèn yuè”\r
Qīng tiān yǒu yuè lái jǐ shí? Wǒ jīn tíng bēi yī wèn zhī.\r
Rén pān míng yuè bù kě dé, yuè xíng què yǔ rén xiāng suí.\r
Jiǎo rú fēi jìng lín dān què, lǜ yān miè jìn qīng huī fā.\r
Dàn jiàn xiāo cóng hǎi shàng lái, níng zhī xiǎo xiàng yún jiān mò.\r
Bái tù dǎo yào qiū fù chūn, Cháng’é gū qī yǔ shuí lín?\r
Jīn rén bú jiàn gǔ shí yuè, jīn yuè céng jīng zhào gǔ rén.\r
Gǔ rén jīn rén ruò liú shuǐ, gòng kàn míng yuè jiē rú cǐ.\r
Wéi yuàn dāng gē duì jiǔ shí, yuè guāng cháng zhào jīn zūn lǐ."""@zh-Latn,
        """“Yuè xià dúzhuó“\r
Huā jiān yī hú jiǔ, dú zhuó wú xiāng qīn.\r
Jǔ bēi yāo míng yuè, duì yǐng chéng sān rén.\r
Yuè jì bù jiě yǐn, yǐng tú suí wǒ shēn.\r
Zàn bàn yuè jiāng yǐng, xíng lè xū jí chūn.\r
Wǒ gē yuè pái huái, wǒ wǔ yǐng líng luàn.\r
Xǐng shí tóng jiāo huān, zuì hòu gè fēn sàn.\r
Yǒng jié wú qíng yóu, xiāng qī miǎo yún hàn."""@zh-Latn .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1027> a ns3:Q7725634 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Drink Alone with the Moon (月下独酌)"@en,
        "月下独酌"@zh,
        "Yuè xià dúzhuó"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P1480 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5727902> ;
    ns2:P50 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7071> ;
    ns2:P571 "0744"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "\"Drink Alone Under the Moon\" (月下独酌) is a renowned poem by Li Bai 李白 (701-762), acclaimed as one of China’s best-loved poets of the Tang dynasty (618–907) and in Chinese history as a whole. This lyrical masterpiece was composed during the third year of Emperor Xuanzong's Tianbao reign (744), while Li Bai was residing in the capital city of Chang'an. The poem reflects a period of deep frustration for the poet, as his ambitions remained unfulfilled within the rigid confines of officialdom. In response, he turned to wine and the quiet company of the moon and his own shadow, seeking solace and spiritual liberation in the act of drinking alone under the serene night sky."@en ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """(1) \r
A pot of wine among the flowers.\r
I drink alone, no friend with me.\r
I raise my cup to invite the moon.\r
He and my shadow and I make three.\r
The moon does not know how to drink;\r
My shadow mimes my capering;\r
But I'll make merry with them both -\r
And soon enough it will be Spring.\r
I sing - the moon moves to and fro.\r
I dance - my shadow leaps and sways.\r
Still sober, we exchange our joys.\r
Drunk - and we'll go our separate ways.\r
Let's pledge - beyond human ties - to be friends,\r
And meet where the Silver River ends.\r
(translation by Vikram Seth)"""@en,
        """(1) \r
Amid the flowers, from a pot of wine\r
I drink alone beneath the bright moonshine.\r
I raise my cup to invite the Moon who blends\r
Her light with my Shadow and we're three friends.\r
The Moon does not know how to drink her share;\r
In vain my Shadow follows me here and there.\r
Together with them for the time I stay\r
And make merry before spring's spent away.\r
I sing and the Moon lingers to hear my song;\r
My Shadow's a mess while I dance along.\r
Sober, we three remain cheerful and gay;\r
Drunken, we part and each may go his way.\r
Our friendship will outshine all earthly love,\r
Next time we'll meet beyond the stars above.\r
(Translation by Xu Yuanzhong)"""@en,
        """(1) \r
花间一壶酒，独酌无相亲。\r
举杯邀明月，对影成三人。\r
月既不解饮，影徒随我身。\r
暂伴月将影，行乐须及春。\r
我歌月徘徊，我舞影零乱。\r
醒时相交欢，醉后各分散。\r
永结无情游，相期邈云汉。\r
\r
(2) \r
天若不爱酒，酒星不在天。\r
地若不爱酒，地应无酒泉。\r
天地既爱酒，爱酒不愧天。\r
已闻清比圣，复道浊如贤。\r
贤圣既已饮，何必求神仙。\r
三杯通大道，一斗合自然。\r
但得酒中趣，勿为醒者传。\r
\r
(3) \r
三月咸阳城，千花昼如锦。\r
谁能春独愁，对此径须饮。\r
穷通与修短，造化夙所禀。\r
一樽齐死生，万事固难审。\r
醉後失天地，兀然就孤枕。\r
不知有吾身，此乐最为甚。\r
\r
(4) \r
穷愁千万端，美酒三百杯。\r
愁多酒虽少，酒倾愁不来。\r
所以知酒圣，酒酣心自开。\r
辞粟卧首阳，屡空饥颜回。\r
当代不乐饮，虚名安用哉。\r
蟹螯即金液，糟丘是蓬莱。\r
且须饮美酒，乘月醉高台。"""@zh,
        """(1) \r
Huā jiān yī hú jiǔ, dúzhuó wū xiāngqīn.\r
Jǔ bēi yāo míngyuè, duì yǐng chéng sān rén.\r
Yuè jì bù jiě yǐn, yǐng tú suí wǒ shēn.\r
Zàn bàn yuè jiāng yǐng, xínglè xū jí chūn.\r
Wǒ gē yuè páihuái, wǒ wǔ yǐng língluàn.\r
Xǐng shí xiàng jiāohuān, zuì hòu gè fēnsàn.\r
Yǒng jié wúqíng yóu, xiāng qī miǎo yúnhàn.\r
\r
(2) \r
Tiān ruò bù ài jiǔ, jiǔ xīng bùzài tiān.\r
De ruò bù ài jiǔ, dì yìng wú jiǔquán.\r
Tiāndì jì ài jiǔ, ài jiǔ bùkuì tiān.\r
Yǐ wén qīng bǐ shèng, fù dào zhuó rú xián.\r
Xián shèng jì yǐ yǐn, hébì qiú shénxiān.\r
Sān bēi tōng dàdào, yī dòu hé zìrán.\r
Dàn dé jiǔ zhōng qù, wù wèi xǐng zhě chuán.\r
\r
(3) \r
Sān yuè xiányáng chéng, qiānhuā zhòu rú jǐn.\r
Shéi néng chūn dú chóu, duì cǐ jìng xū yǐn.\r
Qióng tōng yǔ xiū duǎn, zàohuà sù suǒ bǐng.\r
Yī zūn qí sǐshēng, wànshì gù nán shěn.\r
Zuì hòu shī tiāndì, wù rán jiù gū zhěn.\r
Bùzhī yǒu wú shēn, cǐ lè zuìwéi shén.\r
\r
(4)\r
Qióngchóu qiān wàn duān, měijiǔ sānbǎi bēi.\r
Chóu duō jiǔ suī shǎo, jiǔ qīng chóu bù lái.\r
Suǒyǐ zhī jiǔ shèng, jiǔ hān xīn zì kāi.\r
Cí sù wò shǒu yáng, lǚ kōng jī yán huí.\r
Dāngdài bù lè yǐn, xūmíng ān yòng zāi.\r
Xiè áo jíjīn yè, zāo qiū shì pénglái.\r
Qiě xū yǐn měijiǔ, chéng yuè zuì gāotái."""@zh-Latn .

