        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42519> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Facsimile Wang Xizhi (lines)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of repeated character components/linesets arranged sequentially to create intricate ink patterns in the artwork \"Facsimile Wang Xizhi\" by Chen Guangwu. The brush is saturated with ink and ample water, allowing the ink to spread within the composition and produce a highly imaginative visual effect. A continuous line, unbroken from the start to the finish of the composition, mimics the cursive style of Chinese characters. Sinuous and illusionary curve lines and bold connections evokes traditional calligraphy, but it is entirely a product of imagination and does not correspond to reality of the script."@en ;
