    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1155.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Peace (和气)" ;
    ns1:description """The Calli-Writing Unit is composed of two Chinese characters: Heqi 和气. Nat used a blue marker to write, in wildstyle and 3D style, the two characters on a white porcelain plate, with arrows and zigzagging lines that perfectly combine a traditional approach with contemporary execution. \r
The choice of Heqi 和气 characters stemmed from the fact that decorative motifs in Chinese artistic handicrafts are always linked to auspicious and good luck messages, so they chose to focus the piece on these two characters. Indeed, they are present in a chengyu used as a wish of happiness, which reads "Heqi shengcai 和气生财" (Amiability begets riches). He adds in the piece also some Chinese traditional elements: the decorative “clouds pattern” (yunwen), and the motif of the “turbulent ocean waves” (ping shui) within the central part. Nestled between the lines there are the tags: kwanyin clan, nato and the logo/seal guanyin 观音."""@en ;
