    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Please no graffiti (请勿涂鸦)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of four Chinese characters \"Qingwu tuya 请勿涂鸦\", that stand for \"Please no graffiti\", made in 2020 by Li Qiuqiu and Corw in Jingmi Road, Beijing. This is an act of artistic rebellion, a protest against government buffing. After the buffing of the Jingmi Road hall of fame, the government painted a black stencil inscription \"Qingwu tuya 请勿涂鸦 (No graffiti)\". So, Li Qiuqiu and Corw decided to paint the same text, but using bright colours and fun animations so as to brighten the blank wall that had once been the heart of a shared creativity."@en ;
