    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1208.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU My way of playing basketball is born in the street (我的篮球由街头打造 + tags + NIKE)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is the inscription in Chinese characters in the top section of the piece and stands as its title: Wo de lanqiu you jietou dazao 我的篮球由街头打造 (My way of playing basketball is born in the street). It recalls the underground street culture of New York’s inner city and of Chinese cities, where playing basketball is a way to hang out with friends. The inscription sets out to connect the place where graffiti art was born, the USA, to the place where it is now developing, China, while obviously referencing the sport that is the subject of the commercial advertising requested by Nike. The characters are written in 3D style, the fill-in color is red with beige inlays, decorations and underlines, and the outline is white with dark green depths. This triumph of colors and decorations underlines the sense of light-heartedness with which the piece is imbued. The writing style is rounded and playful, calling to mind the idea of leisure associated with the theme of the graffiti. Inside one of the buds, right in the center of the work, stands the inscription “Nike” and, below it, the three tags of the authors of the piece (0528, Soos and More) and that of BJPZ."@en ;
