    ns1:attributedTitle """CWU Raising Hope (托起希望 + tags)\r
""" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of four Chinese characters \"Tuoqixiwang 托起希望\" (Raising Hope). This Calli-Writing Unit is a wild style renderings of the four characters of the title inspired by a chengyu \"Raising Hope\". The writing style is very edgy and basic, consisting of one or two fill-in colors spread evenly, a single outline, and only occasionally a hint of 3D. The result is somewhat “rigid” and reveals the embryonic state of ANDC personal stylistic research, centered on the attempt to reshape Chinese writing by imitating American styles. The artwork was produced in memory of the Sichuan earthquake of 12 May 2008, which claimed approximately seventy thousand victims. Around the main piece there are 3 orange tags and the year of the execution \"2009\"."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Modern" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42519> ;
