<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1320> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1260> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Atlas: Harmony in Diversity (Venice Biennale 2024 - China Pavillion)"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q641> ;
    ns2:P580 "2024-04-20"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2024-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.labiennale.org/it> ;
    ns1:description """The "Atlas: Harmony in Diversity" exhibition at the Venice Biennale 2024 - China Pavilion was featured by China's National Participation and co-curated by Professor Wang Xiaosong from Zhejiang University and independent curator Jiang Jun. The exhibition connects the past and present art of a country with a rich and ancient tradition.  The exhibition is set in the large spaces of the cisterns, divided into two sections: Union and Heritage.\r
- Union: This section displays documents and images from  "A Comprehensive Collection of Ancient Chinese Paintings". It features 100 paintings from various past dynasties, which are  found overseas. These works are shown in cabinets and on LED screens. "A Comprehensive Collection of Ancient Chinese Paintings" is a project that took almost 19 years to complete, gathering 12,405 pieces of ancient Chinese paintings, including over 3,000 pieces from institutions outside China. Hence the name Atlas for the exhibition, signifying a comprehensive collection. As an anthology of art, cultural relics, and knowledge, this exhibition emphasizes the global convergence of diversity: identities, races, beliefs, concepts, purposes, media, backgrounds, and cultures.\r
- Heritage: This section highlights the work of seven contemporary Chinese artists: Che Jianquan, Jiao Xingtao, Shi Hui, Qiu Zhenzhong, Wang Shaoqiang, Wang Zhenghong, and Zhu Jinshi. These artists created new works inspired by the ancient collection, using various elements like architecture, landscapes, figures, flowers, and birds. Their creations form a harmony between old and new art, blending the past with contemporary styles.\r
Overall, the exhibition showcases how ancient Chinese art continues to influence and inspire modern artists, creating a dialogue between history and present-day creativity.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1321> .

