        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4022>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7797997>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7860>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8502> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11472>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q127418> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/running_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU A Poem by Li Bai (Through the Yangze Gorge) (早发白帝城）" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is composed of two lines of the poem "Through the Yangze Gorge" (Zao fa bai di cheng 早发白帝城) by the famous Tang poet Li Bai (701-762). The poem describes the poet's journey back home across the Yangtze River after a period of exile. The disposition of the characters of the poems are very pictorial in their composition, shaping a typical Chinese landscape painting. The first eight characters for the river banks, the monkey, and their calling are aligned along an incline and are drawn unevenly, as if they really are on the far bank of the river. The small characters appear suspended in the distance, mimicking a location deep in far mountains. The three characters of "ten thousand mountains" (萬重山) stand firm and upright in the foreground, as if on the near bank. The other three characters which mean "my boat has already sped" (舟已過) are written much smaller and placed between the two river banks, like boats loawing quickly and unimpeded on the Yangze River. Thus, the image, essentially pictorial in structure, is organically united with that of the poem.\r
"""@en ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns1:hasBigCharactersCalligraphy false ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon true ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing" ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/133> ;
    ns1:madeUsingTool <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q614467> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 14 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """While the monkeys vainly hail me from both banks,\r
My boat has already sped ten thousand mountains away. \r
(Translated by Zhang Yiguo and Harry Miller)"""@en,
        """两岸猿声啼不住，\r
轻舟已过万重山。"""@zh,
