    ns1:attributedTitle """CWU Blackism No. 1 (signs)\r
""" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the  large black lines executed with a flat brush on white paper. The strokes intersect dynamically, evoking the tension between writing and abstraction. Although the composition derives from a Chinese character, Luo Qi disrupts the stroke order, making it unreadable. This deliberate distortion transforms the work from calligraphic to abstract. The loss of legibility dissolves meaning and highlights the expressive autonomy of the line." ;
