    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1408.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Godbird 07-30 (鸟) " ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of a stylized depiction of a bird that is a reminiscence of the pictographic forms of the character niao 鸟 (bird). Compared to the previous works of the "Godbird Series" it belongs to, there is no longer a strong analogy with the pictographic forms of the character, and the compositions of lines only faintly suggest the shapes of a bird.  In this work, as in the other works of the series, Luo Qi created a childish, archaic drawing writing, in which the characters have been heavily reshaped and contaminated with simple figurative elements. For example, the beak is rendered in red, similar to a seal impression, while green is used for the bird's plumage. This coloration gives the bird an almost fish-like form, evoking connections to the 'Flying Fish Series' by the same artist. The colophon consists of the signature of the artist, "Luo Qi 洛齐", with the two Chinese characters of his name written in cursive. This non-formalized 'writing' is no longer linguistically readable, but visually appreciable, opening itself to universal aesthetic enjoyment. \r
""" ;
