    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Rubbing Drought (lines)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of black ink lines imprinted on paper through the rubbing process used in Wang Nanming's artwork \"Rubbing Drought\". The fragmented ink surfaces, marked by fissures, are not pictorial abstractions, but capture the cracks in the dry ground of Xiliu Lake in Zhengzhou in a tangible, physical way. These lines document a pressing social and ecological issue." ;
