    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU The Story of the Mirror (痛贯心肝、痛当奈何...)"@en ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the chatacters written by Li Xinmo during the performance \"The Story of the Mirror\" (Jingzi de gushi 镜子的故事) realized by Li Xinmo at the exhibition opening at the \"House of Inciting Passion\" of Vienna on November, 10 2023 in occasion of the “Vienna Art Week”. Li Xinmo uses red ink (cinnabar ink) to write characters related to pain which came from ancient Chinese inscriptions on the gauze and after on the mattress, i.e. “Pain penetrates the heart and liver, pain should be helpless” (Tong guan xingan, tong dang naihe 痛贯心肝、痛当奈何) in Wang Xizhi's “Sangluan Tie” 丧乱贴 and “Sadness and pain are destroyed” (Aitong cui bo 哀痛摧剥) in Wang Xizhi’s “Auntie” (Yimu tie 姨母帖). She wrote these words in traditional Chinese characters."@en ;
