<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1479> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q127418> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Book from the Sky (signs)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU constists of thousands of completely invented characters realized  by Xu Bing between 1987 and 1991 for the four books and the installation that constitute the work "Book from the Sky".  Each character was meticulously designed by the artist in a Song-style font that had been standardized by artisans during the Ming dynasty (1368-1644), but although they resemble real Chinese characters, they are entirely meaningless and illegible: Xu Bing actually uses some real components and some that are invented in combinations that are entirely new, creating characters that are looks extremely familiar to who can read Chinese. These "false" characters were hand-carveded on a set of over four thousand moveable type printing woodblocks used to produce a four-volume treatise of 604 pages. Characters were then printed to produce a hundred books, which were neatly arranged at the center of the installation, and were also printed on long scrolls, hanging from the ceiling and mounted on the walls.\r
""" ;
