    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Flute Melodies,  Flowing Water, Writing Calligraphy (负情石上...)" ;
    ns1:description "The poem \"Flute Melodies,  Flowing Water, Writing Calligraphy\" (箫声 ·  流 水 · 书写) is written by Zhu Qingsheng  in traditional characters (cursive-running script). It describes the flowing water that breaks on the rocks, an image combined with the passage of time that runs away, leaving no trace of itself. As well as a part of the characters of the composition that are washed away by the water and of which only traces of soaked ink remain."@en ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns1:hasBigCharactersCalligraphy false ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon false ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing" ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/152> ;
    ns1:madeUsingTool <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q614467> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 36 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """Lively, on the rocks\r
The water breaks.\r
It washes away the autumns...\r
Unrelenting.\r
Unaware of time,\r
it flows away.\r
Spring winds recall...\r
The years passed by.\r
No more trace, no more essence...\r
What has been, is gone.\r
So be it."""@en,
        """負情石上快樂水\r
洗清秋\r
翻然不知時候\r
東風妄憶\r
西風正過\r
只一襲凋零意\r
還不肯\r
就乾休"""@zh,
        """负情石上快乐水\r
洗清秋\r
翻然不知时候\r
东风妄忆\r
西风正过\r
只一袭凋零意\r
还不肯\r
就干休"""@zh,
        """Fù qíng shíshàng kuài lè shuǐ \r
xǐ qīngqiū\r
fānrán bùzhī shíhòu\r
dōngfēng wàng yì \r
xīfēng zhèngguò \r
zhǐ yī xí diāolíng yì  \r
hái bù kěn\r
jiù gàn xiū"""@zh-Latn ;
    ns1:vectorisedOrDigitised false .

