    ns1:attributedTitle """CWU United Nations - Babel of the Millennium (signs)\r
""" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of illegible texts based on Chinese, English, Arabic and Hindi that are included in Gu Wenda's installation \"United Nations - Babel of the Millennium\" exhibited at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art in 1999.  The Chinese characters seems to be written in seal script, but in fact all of them are unreadable. There are also fragments of English language words but none of them could be read, and texts actually don't make full sense.  The texts are made of human hair collected from 325 barber shops and hair salons from 18 countries from every continent. They are arranged in panels that are installed to create a tower. This is an echo of the biblical story of the Tower of Babel from the Genesis that meant to explain the existence of different languages and the difficulty of understanding between peoples.  " ;
