<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1663> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42948> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1088>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q373058> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/running_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1663.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Iron (鐵)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit prominently features Iron's tag along with a coral motif. The vibrant red tones and fluid lines in the piece create a sense of movement, while the contrasting blue highlights add depth and texture.\r
It is interesting how coral, a natural element typically red in color, is rendered in blue, while the charactering of the tag "Iron," a mineral element, is instead depicted in bright red using a "Modern Gothichinese Calligraffiti style". This creates a curious juxtaposition of elements rendered inversely, evoking a reminiscence of yin and yang and the interplay of opposites.\r
Regarding this, within the piece, a taijitu 太极图 can be observed, commonly represented by the yin-yang symbol in Daoism. The yin-yang symbol consists of a circle divided into two interlocking halves—one black (yin) and one white (yang)—each containing a small dot of the opposite color. This imagery symbolizes the duality and interconnectedness of opposites in the universe, embodying the principles of balance, harmony, and perpetual transformation, which are foundational to the concept of Tao. This is a recurring motif (leit motif) that Iron frequently incorporates into his works; however, in this instance, rather than using the traditional black and white, the symbol adopts the colors of the artwork, blending red and blue.\r
The overall composition blends elements of natural forms with stylized graffiti charactering, creating a striking visual impact."""@en ;
