        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q9598> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script>,
        <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/wild_cursive_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU XL: S 05 (《道士步虚词·其六 》/ signs)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is based on the opening section (four columns, 22 characters) of \"Four Ancient Poems Calligraphy\" (Gu shi si tie 古诗四帖), a renowned Tang dynasty calligraphy model by Zhang Xu 张旭 (685–759). The text is organized according to the traditional Chinese format, written from right to left in vertical columns. On the right side of the panel are pixelated representations of the original seals by emperors and collectors included in the calligraphic model. Calligraphic brushstrokes are fragmented and reduced to pixel-like forms, while seals appear as pixel-based visual codes similar to QR codes. As a result, the text becomes nearly illegible. Despite the visual abstraction and new syntax derived by this extreme digital reduction, the artist preserves the aesthetic rhythm, form, and expressive depth of the original model, conveying its essence and spirit (shenyun 神韵). This approach highlights the continuity between past and present, showing how traditional aesthetics can be reimagined through the lens of technology and digital minimalism.  " ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3133>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42519>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q47071> ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine false ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon false ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing",
        "Set of signs (illegible)" ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1425> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 22 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """In Eastern Brilliance, a Nine Mushroom Canopy [carriage];  \r
In Northern Illumination, a Five Cloud chariot.\r
Soaring off into Inverted Luminescence;\r
Emerging and disappearing, ascending to the hazy auroras.\r
Spring fountains [...]\r
(Translated by Feezell Tyler, 2022:  154-55)"""@en,
        "东明九芝盖，北烛五云车。飘飖入倒景，出没上烟霞。春泉"@zh,
        "東明九芝蓋，北燭五雲車。飄飖入倒景，出沒上煙霞。春泉"@zh,
        """Dōngmíng jiǔ zhī gài, běi zhú wǔ yún chē. Piāo yáo rù dào jǐng, chūmò shàng yānxiá. Chūn quán\r
"""@zh-Latn ;
    ns1:vectorisedOrDigitised true .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1735> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
