    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1735.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU East and West, past and present (东西今古)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of four large characters in the middle of he calligraphic work. Their meaning is "East and West, past and present" (dong xi jin gu 东西今古) combining together spatial and temporal axes. The characters are written in traditional script. The format follows the classical vertical order. The text is arranged from top to bottom, and from right to left.\r
In the lower part, below the four large central characters, the colophon is reported in ten vertical columns that are read from top to bottom and from right to left: the artist writes the date of execution of the work "er 0 ersi nian si yue ba ri 二0二四年四月八日" (April 8, 2024), and the place of creation “Zhongguo meishu xueyuan Xianghu guoxueyuan zhengshi ruzhu Lao Ai shu yu hu shang le fu ya lou 中国美术学院湘湖国学院正式入驻老爱书於湖上乐夫雅楼” (Chinese Academy of China Academy of Art officially settled in Lao Aishu’s Lefuya Building on the lake).\r
""" ;
