    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/small_seal_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1737.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Insect-Eroded Wood: Dot and Stroke Imagery Series No. 1  (signs)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of dots and brushstrokes that evoke Chinese characters, as seen in Zhang Aiguo’s Image of Dots and Calligraphic Brushstroke. Like much of his work, it arranges characters in a tightly interwoven manner, resembling a seal and achieving a true calligraphic seal effect. Moving toward pure abstraction, it aligns with Zhang Aiguo’s concept of "moving from introspection to outward expression" (you nei er wai 由内而外).\r
Following the style of small seal script with uniform brushstrokes, Insect-Eroded Wood takes a deconstructive approach to Chinese characters, offering a fresh reinterpretation of classical Han Dynasty inscriptions. By utilizing the Yuan An Stele’s delicate, fluid, and vigorous lines, the work enhances its modern aesthetic. The meandering strokes obscure the original character structures, raising the question of whether modern calligraphy can exist independently of Chinese characters.\r
As an extension of the Grand Open Passage Impression Series, this piece emphasizes the quality and texture of calligraphic dots and strokes rather than an overall meaning of the content.""" ;
