    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1396399>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42519> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Digital No08-CH01, CH02 (Set of signs)" ;
    ns1:description """The CWU consists exclusively of the visual organization of brush-written Chinese characters and marks made by the cigarette. It is composed of vertically arranged columns of calligraphic marks executed with black ink and with burn marks on xuan paper, following the traditional Chinese writing direction from top to bottom and right to left. Although the characters retain the formal appearance and structural conventions of Chinese calligraphy, they do not convey identifiable linguistic content. \r
As in the other works of the Digital series, the characters are intentionally devoid of specific linguistic meaning. The title Digital does not indicate the use of digital technology. Instead, it refers to the visual distortion and fragmentation of the Chinese characters. Their fragmented appearance recalls the visual effects of digital images.""" ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
