    ns2:P569 "1941-05-04"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1792> ;
    ns1:description "Roger Mason is an English geologist who is best known as the discoverer of the original type fossil, Charnia masoni, of a Precambrian (more than 340 million years old) organism that is part of the Ediacaran biota. He is now a professor at the China University of Geosciences in Wuhan, China. He took part in the concert event \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells\" (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会) held in London in 2012, where he collaborated with calligrapher Li Binquan for the creation of a calligraphic writing that reads “Yingguo Zhongguo youyi wangguchangqing 英国中国友谊万古长青” (Britain-China Friendship will Last Forever)." ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Not present"@en ;
    ns1:hasWikidataResource <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q9004982> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1802> a ns3:Q7725634 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Prelude to Water Melody (水调歌头)"@en,
        "水调歌头"@zh,
        "Shuǐ diào gē tóu"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P1480 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5727902> ;
    ns2:P50 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36020> ;
    ns2:P571 "1076"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "The poem “Prelude to Water Melody” (Shui diao ge tou · mingyue jishi you 水调歌头 · 明月几时有) is composed by the Song dynasty poet Su Shi (1036-1101), who wrote these lyrics while he was drunk and missing his younger brother (Su Zhe) on the Mid-Autumn Festival of the year Bingzhen (1076)."@en ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """How long will the full moon appear?\r
Wine cup in hand, I ask the sky.\r
I do not know what time of the year\r
It would be tonight in the palace on high.\r
Riding the wind, there I would fly,\r
Yet I'm afraid the crystalline palace would be\r
Too high and cold for me.\r
I rise and dance, with my shadow I play.\r
On high as on earth, would it be as gay?\r
The moon goes round the mansions red\r
Through gauze-draped window soft to shed\r
Her light upon the sleepless bed.\r
Why then when people part, is the oft full and bright?\r
Men have sorrow and joy; they part or meet again;\r
The moon is bright or dim and she may wax or wane.\r
There has been nothing perfect since the olden days.\r
So let us wish that man\r
Will live long as he can!\r
Though miles apart, we'll share the beauty she displays."""@en,
        """明月几时有？把酒问青天。\r
不知天上宫阙，今夕是何年？\r
我欲乘风归去，又恐琼楼玉宇，高处不胜寒。\r
起舞弄清影，何似在人间？\r
转朱阁，低绮户，照无眠。\r
不应有恨，何事长向别时圆？\r
人有悲欢离合，月有阴晴圆缺，此事古难全。\r
但愿人长久，千里共婵娟。"""@zh,
        """míng yuè jǐ shí yǒu? bǎ jiǔ wèn qīng tiān.\r
bùzhī tiān shàng gōng què, jīn xī shì hé nián?\r
wǒ yù chéng fēng guī qù, yòu kǒng qióng lóu yù yǔ, gāo chùbù shèng hán.\r
qǐ wǔ nòng qīng yǐng, hé sì zài rén jiān?\r
zhuǎn zhū gé, dī qǐ hù, zhào wú mián.\r
bù yīng yǒu hèn, hé shìcháng xiàng bié shí yuán?\r
rén yǒu bēi huān lí hé, yuè yǒu yīn qíng yuán quē, cǐ shì gǔ nán quán.\r
dàn yuàn rén cháng jiǔ, qiān lǐ gòng chán juān."""@zh-Latn .

