    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Landscript: Revisit n. 2 (水，石 ，土, ...)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of a set of Chinese characters that Xu Bing uses as pictorial elements to arrange the landscape of "Landscript: Revisit n. 2" (2002). In this work, written characters function as visual components of the scene. In this way, the character for 'stone' (shi 石) forms the rocks along the riverbanks; the character for 'water' (shui 水) makes up the waves of the river, the charater for ‘tree' (mu 木）becomes the trees that populate the landscape; and so on. Through this method, individual characters are arranged and repeated to build the entire composition. \r
The artist draws on different styles of Chinese writing, from regular and cursive scripts to simplified forms. Anyway, archaic forms such as bronze scripts and oracle-bone scripts are the ones he uses the most due to their pictographic value.\r
The colophon in the lower right of the work features the artist's signature rendered in idiosyncratic Roman letters reading "Xu Bing" and the title of the work in four Chinese characters (chongyou ling er 零二 重游). The work includes the artist's circular, red, relief seal, also inscribed with "Xu Bing" in idiosyncratic Roman letters.""" ;
