    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Kwanyin (觀音)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is composed of the two characters of the word "Guanyin 觀音", that is Chinese name of the Kwanyin Clan - the author of this tag. The regular thickness of their lines reproduces the typical thickness of the calligraphic “great seal style” (dazhuan shu 大篆书). The two characters are written reshaping their pictographic forms: the right part of the first character "Guan 觀" is tranformed into a face with two big eyes – the meaning of the character is, in fact, “look at, watch, observe”, and the lower part of the second character yin 音 into an open mouth – the meaning of the character is, in fact, “phone, sound”.\r
The two characters "Guanyin 观 音" explicitly refers to the Bodhisattva Guanyin (Guanyin Pusa 观音菩萨) associated with compassion and usually known as Avalokiteśvara. """ ;
