    ns2:P1476 "INK Art Week"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q641> ;
    ns2:P580 "2018-04-17"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2018-04-20"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P664 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1546906>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q338505>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q834650> ;
    ns1:description """The INK Art Week, which took place in Venice from April 17 to 20, 2018, was an event dedicated to contemporary Chinese ink arts (ink painting and calligraphy). The goal was to explore and promote the new trends in these artistic forms and their impact on the contemporary art scene.\r
The event featured a group exhibition called Ink Riders, which opened on April 17 at the Academy of Fine Arts in Venice, showcasing works by fourteen prominent Chinese artists, including Gu Gan, Zhang Dawo, Fan	 Bingnan,	 Liu Gang, Pu Lieping,	 Zhang	 Qiang	& Lia Wei, etc. who have contributed to modernizing calligraphy over the past thirty years.\r
Additionally, three days of conferences and discussions were held at Ca’ Foscari University, with the participation of artists, scholars, and curators from both China and Europe. Topics ranged from art theory, to the calligraphic gesture, and the role of ink arts in the contemporary context.""" .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1891> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/100> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Brushes with Surprise: The Art of Calligraphy in Modern China Exhibition"@en,
        "惊人之笔—现代中国书法展"@zh,
        "Jīngrén zhī bǐ—xiàndài Zhōngguó shūfǎ zhǎn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q84> ;
    ns2:P580 "2002-01-31"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2002-05-19"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P664 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6373> ;
    ns1:description """This exhibition explores the evolution and dynamism of "modern Chinese calligraphy", a form of art that has changed more in the past 50 years than in the previous 1,500 years. Inspired by Picasso's remark that, had he been born Chinese, he would have been a calligrapher, the exhibition presents nearly fifty significant pieces from the museum's collection, highlighting a unique and unmatched collection of modern Chinese calligraphy.\r
The exhibition offers a vibrant and unexpected glimpse into both the art and people of modern China. It showcases a variety of styles, from classical to modern, neo-classical, and avant-garde, with striking techniques that range from elegant to dramatic. The content of the works has become more accessible, with modern Chinese calligraphy serving as a dynamic medium for personal expression. The calligraphy often conveys emotions more directly than in previous centuries.\r
The exhibition also reflects how Chinese calligraphy has evolved as a form of social commentary and satire. Among the featured works are contributions from leading Chinese calligraphers of the past half-century, including Mao Zedong, who was also a talented calligrapher, and Gu Gan, the first Chinese artist invited to create a label for the prestigious wine Château Mouton Rothschild, following in the footsteps of Picasso and Matisse."""@en .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1892> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/100> ;
    ns2:P1476 "The Divine Brush Comes to Jingde - Zhang Qiang's New Ceramic Aesthetics and Art Document Exhibition"@en,
        "神来景德之笔 — 张强陶瓷新美学与艺术文献展"@zh,
        "Shén lái Jǐngdé zhī bǐ - Zhāng Qiáng táocí xīn měixué yǔ yìshù wénxiàn zhǎn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q34405> ;
    ns2:P580 "2019-01-19"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2019-01-29"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """This exhibition took place from January 19 to 29, 2019 at the Sanbaopeng Ceramic Art Base of Jingdezhen (Jingdezhen sanbao peng yishu juluo 景德镇三宝蓬艺术聚落). \r
During this exhibition, several performances took place in which Zhang Qiang painted on ceramics, collaborating with some female counterparts. These performances, part of his artistic research, focused on a process of "blinded calligraphy" (mangshu 盲书),  where Zhang Qiang and his female collaborators engaged in a creative dialogue, bringing together the art of ceramics and a collective sensory experience.""" .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1905> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/585> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Territori - Ibiza Performance Art Festival (3rd edition)"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q52631> ;
    ns2:P580 "2023-09-17"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2023-09-25"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P856 <https://territorifestival.com/> ;
    ns1:description """The third edition of "Territori - Ibiza Performance Art Festival" took place from 17 to 25 September, 2022 in Ibiza (Spain). \r
Territori Ibiza is an international gathering specialized in performance art. Since 2020, the island has brought together an extraordinary selection of artists from around the world who work with body art, live arts, and action. Territori is a space for committed creation, open to new processes and emerging local talents.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/607> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1906> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/585> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Love, Celebration and the Road Ahead Festival"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q84> ;
    ns2:P580 "2022-09-29"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2022-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """"Love, Celebration and the Road Ahead" is a three-day festival which took place from September, 29 -to October, 1st, 2022 to mark the launch of Hettie Judah's book entitled "How Not To Exclude Artist Mothers (and other parents)". In this book Hettie Judah explains that for too long, artists have been told that they can't have both motherhood and a successful career. In this polemical volume, critic and campaigner Hettie Judah argues that a paradigm shift is needed within the art world to take account of the needs of artist mothers (and other parents: artist fathers, parents who don't identify with the term "mother", and parents in other sectors of the art world). The festival included a mix of exhibitions, discussions, performances, and other related activities, all meant to elevate the voices of parent-artists, while also addressing the systemic challenges they face. \r
For this occasion the artist Echo Morgan decides to realize a performance entitled "Woman 女+ Horse 马 = Mother 妈".""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/615> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1907> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/585> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Performance Festival THE NON-FUNGIBLE BODY?"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41329> ;
    ns2:P580 "2022-06-17"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2022-06-19"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.ooekultur.at/> ;
    ns1:description """The Performance Festival THE NON-FUNGIBLE BODY was held took place from June 17 to 19, 2022 in Linz and was dedicated to the latest developments in performance art. Each year, the festival explores a specific theme, and this year it focused on the intersection of performance and digitalization. Artists whose work explores the intersection between body and archive, using live performance and documentation, as well as performance in relation to internet cultures and NFTs (Non-Fungible Tokens), were invited to participate.\r
The festival was organized by OÖ Landes-Kultur GmbH in cooperation with Landestheater Linz and its new dance director, Roma Janus. For three days, more than 20 international artists presented their performances. Some of the performances took place on the roof and in the voestalpine open space.\r
The festival title, "Non-Fungible Body", referenced the idea of a body that cannot be copied, substituted, or subdivided, highlighting the importance of the physical meeting between performers and audience as an essential quality of performance. The title also invited reflections on NFTs, which, especially in the last two years, have triggered a shift in the paradigm of art production, sales, and collection. While initially this digital format seemed disconnected from performance art, the festival explored how NFTs and blockchain technologies can influence and transform performance. It also reflected on the online self-dramatization characteristic of the social media age, which has broadened the horizons of artistic performance.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/623> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1911> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/643>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/648> ;
    ns2:P1476 "The 55th Venice Biennale Parallel Exhibition, Independent Chinese Art Exhibition: Voice of the Unseen"@en,
        "第55届威尼斯双年展平行展中国独立艺术展 - 未曾呈现的声音"@zh,
        "Dì 55 jiè Wēinísī shuāng nián zhǎn píngxíng zhǎn zhōngguó dúlì yìshù zhǎn - wèicéng chéngxiàn de shēngyīn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q641> ;
    ns2:P580 "2013-05-29"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2013-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """The "5th Venice Biennale Parallel Exhibition, Independent Chinese Art Exhibition: Voice of the Unseen" exhibition took place in Venice from May 29 to November 4, 2013. The exhibition highlighted the history of Chinese art, from the Post-Avant-Garde movement of the '80s and '90s to the present day. It showcased works by 188 artists and groups who have been part of the independent, unofficial art movement in China, many of whom had never been exhibited outside of China.\r
The exhibition also reflected on the evolution of the Chinese independent art movement, which began in 1979 with the Xidan Democracy Wall event in Beijing. With its vast space and significance, the exhibition represented a key moment for Chinese art, reflecting the profound transformation the country was undergoing.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/655> .

