    ns1:description "Lei Liang was born in Tianjin (China) on November 28, 1972. He received his earliest musical training in Beijing, where he lived until he was seventeen years old. He then moved to the United States, where he completed his college and graduate education in Boston. He studied composition with Harrison Birtwistle (1934-2022), Chaya Czernowin (b. 1957), Joshua Fineberg (b.1969), and Mario Davidovsky (1934-2019), and received degrees from the New England Conservatory of Music and Harvard University. Actually, he is Chancellor’s Distinguished Professor of Music at the University of California San Diego (UCSD). " ;
