<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1957> a ns3:Q1400264 ;
    ns2:P2561 "TENG Ensamble 鼟" ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q334> ;
    ns2:P453 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1959> ;
    ns2:P571 "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.thetengcompany.com/> ;
    ns1:description "TENG is a leading not-for-profit Singaporean arts company that re-imagines the possibilities of Chinese music. Founded in 2004, The TENG Ensemble is a critically acclaimed Singaporean Chinese fusion music group that imbues musical influences from the East, West, traditional and contemporary. Its members comprise nineteen among music educators, scholars, and award-winning instrumentalists.  The Chinese word “teng 鼟”– one of the most complex characters in the Chinese language – is an ancient Chinese representation for the sound of a “drum”.  This character is a symbol of TENG’s aspiration to bring cultures together and nurture future generations of musicians and audiences in Chinese music.  One of the most significant performances from a calligraphic point of view realized by this musical group is the digital performance of music and calligraphy entitled “Heaven, Earth, Mankind and Unity” (Tian di ren he 天地人合) realized in 2021 together with the Chinese female calligrapher Grace Chen Liang 陈亮 (b.1974) (see the archive). " .

