    ns2:P2561 "Zhang Yiguo 张以国" ;
    ns2:P569 "1960"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q60>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8646>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns1:description "Zhang Yiguo (b. 1960) is a renowned Chinese calligraphy and painting connoisseur. He graduated from Nankai University’s Department of Philosophy in 1983, where he served as the president of the university’s calligraphy society. In the late 1980s, he went to the United States for further studies and earned a Ph.D. in Art History and Archaeology from Columbia University in 2001. Zhang Yiguo has held research positions at prestigious institutions, including the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York and the Museum of Fine Arts in Boston.  He currently holds the positions of Director of the Chinese Painting and Calligraphy Department at Beijing Poly International Auction and Senior Consultant at Poly Auction Hong Kong. He is the author of several books on calligraphy: and is an accomplished calligrapher himself. " ;
    ns1:isCuratorOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1401> .

