    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/great_seal_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2058.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Inquiry of Heaven (《天问》)" ;
    ns1:description """CWU Inquiry of Heaven (Tianwen 天問) consists of the complete transcription of Qu Yuan's Questions to Heaven rendered in a seal script (zhuanshu) inspired by the script forms of the ancient state of Chu. Rather than adopting the standardized Small Seal Script (xiaozhuan) of the Qin dynasty, Huang Yeda draws on earlier large seal script traditions (dazhuan), evoking the historical and cultural context associated with Qu Yuan and the Chu ci tradition. The text comprises 1,553 traditional Chinese characters written in red cinnabar on a black background, reproducing the chromatic scheme of the installation Inquiry of Heaven.\r
The writing is arranged according to the traditional Chinese format of vertical columns read from top to bottom and from right to left. Executed with brush, ink, and cinnabar on wooden panels, the work transforms the literary text into a monumental calligraphic composition. Through its script style, materiality, and visual presentation, the CWU establishes a direct connection to early Chinese traditions of writing, ritual, and cosmological inquiry.""" ;
