    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Writing Music - Silent Melodies: \"Turandot\"(signs) " ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is composed of Luo Qi's original transcription of an aria from the Italian opera "Turandot". The artist employs a series of signs inspired by the "Dunhuang Musical Score System" (Dunhuang qupu / yuepu 敦煌曲谱/乐谱). This ancient music notation system consists of 20 tablature-signs, which represented the tablature notations for the four-stringed Tang dynasty pipa (Chinese lute), indicating finger positions and their corresponding pitches. These simbols are simple characters (six are Chinese numerals), radicals or character components/parts. As in the Dunhunag musical pieces, these symbols in this CWU are transcribed one below the other from right to left, to form columns, and are accompanied by two other symbols (a dot · and a mouth 口 ) that denote rhythm and meter. \r
In this CWU, the echo of the Italian opera resonates through pipa notes that compose an unreadable rhytmic text. """ ;
