    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Zhuangzi – On the equality of things / Tangerine (《庄子—齐物论》)" ;
    ns1:description "Chu Chu wrote parts of the chapter from the \"Zhuangzi\" entitled “Discourse on the Equality of All Things”  (Qiwulun 齐物论) in small characters and in a particular form of cursive script called zhangcao 章草, and placed them vertically on the paper. By looking at the work closely, you will be able to identify the characters and read the content of the text, losing sight of the depicted image, which will instead emerge as you move away. This effect is the result of different concentration of ink. The characters serve the textual function, but they also act as micro components of the image. " ;
