<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2130> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2076> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Wu wu fei shi: Chu Chu Art Solo Exhibition (物无非是——储楚艺术个展 )"@en,
        "物无非是——储楚艺术个展 "@zh,
        "Wù wú fēi shì —— Chǔ Chǔ yìshù gèzhǎn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4970> ;
    ns2:P580 "2016-05-29"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2016-07-12"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """"Wu Wu Fei Shi" is a solo exhibition by the female artist Chu Chu, held in 2016 at the Jianghong Art Museum in Hangzhou. The exhibition presents a selection of her works from the past decade, including pieces from the series "Material Immaterial" (Wu Fei Wu 物非物),  "Equality of things - Fruit" (Qi Wu - Guoshi 齐物-果实), "Shu Shan Shui" (书山水), "Tree Whisper" (Shu Yu 树语), and "Dream of the West Lake Series" (Xihu meng xun 西湖梦寻)". \r
The title of this exhibition, "Wu Wu Fei Shi", is inspired by Zhuangzi's "Discourse on the Equality of All Things" (Qiqulun 齐物论), reflecting Chu Chu's philosophical exploration into the nature and essence of objects. The exhibition introduces her artistic approach to calligraphy known as "Hidden Characters" (cang zi 藏字), which she began exploring in 2012. This technique involves embedding Chinese characters within layered compositions, inviting the viewer to uncover them through careful observation. By deconstructing and reassembling images and text through photography,  calligraphy and painting, Chu Chu reconstructs the spirit of objects, creating a dialogue between Western contemporary visual art and classical Chinese traditions.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2077>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2081>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2083> .

