    ns2:P1476 "China/Avant-Garde Art Exhibition (中国现代艺术展)"@en,
        "中国现代艺术展"@zh,
        "Zhōngguó xiàndài yìshù zhǎn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns2:P580 "1989-02-05"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "1989-02-19"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """"China/Avant-Garde Art Exhibition" was held at the National Art Museum of China in Beijing from 5, to 19 February 1989. It was the first large-scale exhibition dedicated to experimental art in China.  Key participants included Gu Wenda, Xu Bing, and Wu Shanzhuan.\r
Gu Wenda presented paintings and drawings produced during his two-year stay (1987-1989) in the United States, including his works with pseudo-characters.\r
Xu Bing contributed with a section of his installation entitled "Book from the Sky" (Tianshu 天书). Wu Shanzhuan staged a performance titled “Big Business – Selling Shrimps in China/Avant-Garde Art Exhibition” (Da Shengyi 大生意 ), part of his Red Humor series. During the opening, he sold 30 kilograms of shrimp, which he had transported from Zhoushan to Beijing.\r
Another participant was Yan Binghui, the only artist in the group who had also taken part in the First Exhibition of Chinese Modern Calligraphy. He later played a leading role in the modernization of ink painting.\r
\r
""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1478>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2211>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/235> .

