<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2222> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P1476 "China: Through the Looking Glass (中国 : 镜花水月)"@en,
        "中国 : 镜花水月"@zh,
        "Zhōngguó: Jìng huā shuǐ yuè"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q160236>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q60> ;
    ns2:P580 "2015-05-07"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2015-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """The exhibition "China: Through the Looking Glass" was held at the Metropolitan Museum of Art from May 7 to September 7, 2015. It explored the historical influence of Chinese aesthetics on Western fashion. It examined how China inspired centuries of fashion imagination and fantasy. The Costume Institute collaborated with the Department of Asian Art to present a dialogue between haute couture and traditional Chinese garments, paintings, porcelain, and other art forms, including cinema.\r
Since the 16th century, the West had been fascinated by the mysterious and elusive beauty of Chinese objects and imagery. Designers such as Paul Poiret and Yves Saint Laurent drew inspiration from this fascination, creating works imbued with fantasy, romance, and nostalgia. Fashion served as a lens through which these designers reinterpreted and hybridized Chinese aesthetic and cultural elements.\r
The exhibition featured over 140 haute couture and avant-garde designs, displayed within immersive environments inspired by classical Chinese art. Throughout the exhibition, cinematic representations of China were also included to show how popular culture shaped Western perceptions of China and to highlight film’s unique role in understanding Chinese history.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2221> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2294> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P144 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2295> ;
