        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q9683> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q37681> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2294.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU  \"Quiproquo\" Cocktail Dress (肚痛帖)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the outfit created by Christian Dior in 1951 called \" 'Quiproquo' Cocktail Dress\" (鸡尾酒裙). It features a calligraphic print of the poem by Zhang Xu Zhang Xu 张旭 (c. 675 CE – 750 CE), known as “Letter about a Stomachache” (Du Tong Tie 肚痛帖).  Rather than appearing as a single, legible inscription, the calligraphy is multiplied across the surface of the dress, turning the script into a rhythmic decorative pattern that emphasizes visual impact over textual readability. The original text has been lost, but a stone inscription copy from the year 1058 CE (Song dynasty period) is preserved at the Beilin Museum in Xi’an. This piece is not a poem in the strict sense, but rather a short letter/calligraphy in cursive script written by Zhang Xu during a moment of physical pain, as he was suffering from a severe stomachache (or abdominal pain). In the text, Zhang Xu briefly describes his condition, his confusion about the cause of the pain (whether from cold or heat), and his decision to take a rhubarb-based medicine to relieve the discomfort. The cursive-script text is extremely concise, consisting of only six lines and around 30 characters." ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns1:hasBigCharactersCalligraphy false ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon true ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing" ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/2294.jpg> ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2221> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 30 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """Suddenly stricken with unbearable stomach pain,\r
Unsure whether it was caused by heat or cold.\r
I thought of taking a decoction of rhubarb,\r
Beneficial in either case—hot or cold alike.\r
But what should I do?\r
This isn’t a clinical setting."""@en,
        """忽肚痛不可堪,                                       \r
不知是冷热所致，                                                    \r
欲服大黄汤，                                                                 \r
冷热俱有益。                                                                   \r
如何为计,\r
非临床”。"""@zh,
        """忽肚痛不可堪，\r
不知是冷熱所致，\r
欲服大黃湯，\r
冷熱俱有益。\r
如何為計，\r
非臨床”。"""@zh,
        """Hū dù tòng bù kě kān,\r
bù zhī shì lěng rè suǒ zhì,\r
yù fú dà huáng tāng,\r
lěng rè jù yǒu yì.\r
Rú hé wéi jì,\r
fēi lín chuáng."""@zh-Latn .

