        <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/ugly_calligraphy> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU I can’t take it anymore (受的好累)" ;
    ns1:description "The \"CWU I can’t take it anymore (受的好累)\" consists of four Chinese characters: \"shou de hao 受的好\", rendered in red spray paint, followed by \"lei 累 (fatigue)\", executed in black. The chromatic contrast between red and black is visually and symbolically significant: the red conveys intensity, emotional agitation, and perhaps internalized pain, while the black character \"lei 累 (fatigue)\" isolates and emphasizes the core sentiment of exhaustion."@en ;
