    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU In Hong Kong, if you are sick, you don't see a doctor; you look at your wallet (在香港地,有病不是看醫生,是看看自己個銀包)" ;
    ns1:description "The \"CWU In Hong Kong, if you are sick, you don't see a doctor; you look at your wallet (在香港地,有病不是看醫生,是看看自己個銀包)\" is written in traditional Chinese characters and employs Cantonese vernacular syntax, reinforcing its local specificity and immediacy. Formally, the text is rendered in black, likely applied with a marker, on a tiled wall, with each character carefully positioned within the boundaries of a single tile. This strict alignment produces a grid-like visual order that contrasts with the critical and emotionally charged content of the message, a strategy frequently observed in text-based urban interventions."@en ;
