<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2539> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P144 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2318> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11024>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q16358629>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q185961> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1860> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/square_word_calligraphy> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Specially Designed Calligraphy Set Box in “Square Word Calligraphy”/ Specially Designed Four Treasures of the Study Box Realized in “Square Word Calligraphy” (在古代)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the \"Specially Designed Calligraphy Set Box in 'Square Word Calligraphy'/ Specially Designed Four Treasures of the Study Box Realized in 'Square Word Calligraphy' \" realized by the contemporary Chinese artist Xu Bing. Xu Bing took the text of the poem “In Ancient Days” (Zai gudai 在古代, 2004) by Zhai Yongming, translated it into English, and converted each word into a “square unit” following the Square Word Calligraphy method. Each unit functions as a self-contained micro-character: it incorporates the letters of the original word arranged in a compact, balanced structure, similar to a traditional Chinese character. The result is a writing system that combines legibility with visual form, turning the poetic text into a mosaic of square symbols where calligraphy becomes both language and artistic expression." ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q47071> ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasColophon true ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing" ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2314> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 292 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """In ancient days, I’d only\r
write letters, not knowing\r
where we’d meet.\r
\r
Now I flood your email,\r
my characters like stars\r
chasing after you.\r
I care little where they land.\r
In ancient days, mountains were green facts.\r
Blue water at our feet,\r
we’d simply clasp fists, keeping faith\r
we’d meet again.\r
\r
Now you fly this place and that,\r
my small stars trailing through the sky,\r
reaching out as to a sore spot,\r
countless tries to patch\r
the blue screen, though not hysterical.\r
\r
In ancient days, how many poems\r
to be a Lao Shan Taoist, to slip into\r
a cup of bamboo-leaf tea,\r
stride on air, pass through brick walls\r
and seize you. Or\r
beat one’s head bloody.\r
\r
Now, you thumb a phone\r
that wafts ten thousand scents,\r
the fragrance of a distant body.\r
One part trembles and a whole world shakes.\r
\r
Ancient days weren’t like this.\r
We spurred the horses then, side by side,\r
covering a few miles.\r
My earrings clinked, a grin showed on your face.\r
We kept ours heads down, and rode.\r
\r
© D. Shi e G. O’Connell"""@en,
        """Nel tempo antico, potevo soltanto\r
scriverti lettere, senza sapere\r
in qual parte del mondo\r
ci saremmo rincontrati. \r
\r
Ora inondo la tua casella di posta:\r
i miei caratteri, simili a stelle, \r
ti inseguono senza tregua\r
e più non curo ove si posino. \r
\r
Nel tempo antico, i monti erano presenze quiete\r
e l’acqua azzurra riposava ai loro piedi.\r
Bastava un gesto delle mani\r
per confidare nel nostro ritrovarci. \r
\r
Ora tu attraversi il cielo senza posa, \r
e le mie piccole stelle ti inseguono\r
Ovunque.\r
Quando ti sfiorano, è come toccare una ferita sottile. \r
Ripetono il gesto del ricucire,\r
in silenzio, \r
uno schermo azzurro. \r
\r
Nel tempo antico, quante poesie\r
occorrevano per farsi taoista di Laoshan, \r
per scivolare entro una tazza di tè\r
alle foglie di bambù,\r
camminare nell’aria, trapassare muri di mattoni  \r
e raggiungerti.  \r
Oppure cadere al suolo, feriti. \r
\r
Ora sfiori un telefono\r
che reca con sé mille profumi lontani,  \r
il respiro d’un corpo assente.  \r
E quando un punto trema,  \r
trema il mondo intero. \r
\r
Nel tempo antico non era così.  \r
Si cavalcava fianco a fianco  \r
per poche miglia soltanto.  \r
Un tintinnio d’orecchini nel vento,  \r
un sorriso appena sorto sul tuo volto,  \r
poi gli occhi si chinavano.  \r
E si seguitava a cavalcare. \r
\r
© M. Merenda"""@it,
        """在古代，我只能这样\r
给你写信 并不知道\r
我们下一次\r
会在哪里见面\r
\r
现在 我往你的邮箱\r
灌满了群星 它们都是五笔字形\r
它们站起来 为你奔跑\r
它们停泊在天上的某处\r
我并不关心\r
\r
在古代 青山严格地存在\r
当绿水醉倒在他的脚下\r
我们只不过抱一抱拳 彼此\r
就知道后会有期\r
\r
现在，你在天上飞来飞去\r
群星满天跑 碰到你就像碰到疼处\r
它们像无数的补丁 去堵截\r
一个蓝色屏幕 它们并不歇斯底里\r
\r
在古代 人们要写多少首诗？\r
才能变成嶗山道士 穿过墙\r
穿过空气 再穿过一杯竹叶青\r
抓住你 更多的时候\r
他们头破血流 倒地不起\r
\r
现在 你正拨一个手机号码\r
它发送上万种味道\r
它灌入了某个人的体香\r
当某个部位颤抖 全世界都颤抖\r
\r
在古代 我们并不这样\r
我们只是并肩策马 走几十里地\r
当耳环玎璫作响 你微微一笑\r
低头间 我们又走了几十里地"""@zh,
        """在古代，我只能這樣\r
給你寫信 並不知道\r
我們下一次\r
會在哪裡見面\r
\r
現在 我往你的郵箱\r
灌滿了群星 它們都是五筆字形\r
它們站起來 為你奔跑\r
它們停泊在天上的某處\r
我並不關心\r
\r
在古代 青山嚴格地存在\r
當綠水醉倒在他的腳下\r
我們只不過抱一抱拳 彼此\r
就知道後會有期\r
\r
現在，你在天上飛來飛去\r
群星滿天跑 碰到你就像碰到疼處\r
它們像無數的補丁 去堵截\r
一個藍色屏幕 它們並不歇斯底里\r
\r
在古代 人們要寫多少首詩？\r
才能變成嶗山道士 穿過牆\r
穿過空氣 再穿過一杯竹葉青\r
抓住你 更多的時候\r
他們頭破血流 倒地不起\r
\r
現在 你正撥一個手機號碼\r
它發送上萬種味道\r
它灌入了某個人的體香\r
當某個部位顫抖 全世界都顫抖\r
\r
在古代 我們並不這樣\r
我們只是並肩策馬 走幾十里地\r
當耳環玎璫作響 你微微一笑\r
低頭間 我們又走了幾十里地"""@zh .

