    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Meditation (泉鸣起韵的松间...)" ;
    ns1:description """The calligraphic text written in Meditation (Chensi 沉思, 2021) translates the emotional atmosphere of Jules Massenet’s musical intermezzo into poetic language. The selected phrases evoke natural and contemplative imagery, such as “the murmuring spring threading a melodic rhythm” (quan ming qi yun 泉鸣起韵), “the poignant beauty born of sorrow” (beishang niang chu de qimei 悲伤酿出的凄美), “a thousand paper cranes soaring into the distance” (fei xiang yuanfang de qian zhihe 飞向远方的千纸鹤), "endless drifting threads” (yong wu zhijing de yousi  永无止境的游丝), “floating into the cosmos” (piao xiang taikong  飘向太空), and “the emotion of torn silk” (lie bo zhi qing 裂帛之情).\r
These poetic fragments transform musical sensation into visual language. The imagery of flowing water, drifting threads, and quiet landscapes reflects the contemplative character evoked by the violin melody. Extremely pale ink washes represent the thoughts spreading into the cosmos, their boundless elegance subtly tinged with faint hints of red, green, and blue. Alternating light and dark ink and richer variations in brushwork, represents the interplay of the violin and orchestra, as well as the performers’ pure and graceful visual presence, Through these textual elements, the artwork integrates poetic imagery with calligraphic rhythm, creating a synesthetic correspondence between musical emotion and written form.""" ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
