    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2580.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Earth Script – Dust (薼)" ;
    ns1:description """\r
"Dust" is part of Song Chen’s series titled "Earth Script", realized in 2018. The work presents a graphic variant of the character for 'dust' (chen 尘), rendered in the rare form 薼. The content implied by this character is influenced by Buddhist thought and reflects on the essence of existence: “life emerges from soil and ultimately returns to it, dust to dust, earth to earth” (artist's interview 2025). The medium foregrounds ‘dust’ as both substance and concept/message of transience and impermanence. The character derives from the archaic forms depicting running deer raising dust and earth. It is explicitly linked to Buddhist notions of dissolution and disappearance, as it links the idea of dust to cycles of decay and renewal. """ ;
