    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2586.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Emptiness (無)"@en ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the dress entitled \"Emptiness (Wu 無)\" designed by Tsai Yifen in occasion of the \"From Ink to Apparel III\" exhibition held in Taipei in 2018. Inspired by Tong Yang-tze’s fourteen calligraphic styles of Wu, the CWU transforms the brushstrokes into textile form. Lace, corded details, and beaded embroidery trace the flowing, rhythmic gestures of the character, turning it into a three-dimensional, wearable symbol of emptiness. Through its structure and texture, the CWU embodies both the visual energy of calligraphy and the philosophical concept of “wu”—limitless space, potential, and void—within the garment."@en ;
