    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Left/Right: Deviation from the Centre (左、右)" ;
    ns1:description "The two characters \"左\" (left) and \"右\" (right) and the two words \"left\" and \"right\" are engraved on the sole of the performer's shoes. The performer is blindfolded and he tries to find the exit on the other side of a narrow hallway. On the floor, between the performance starting point and the exit, there is a line made of ink. If the performer walks straight, he reaches the exit without leaving any shoe prints behind. If he trails from the path, the words \"left\" and \"right\" will be imprinted to the surrounding floor, and he might run into the wall. The performance continues until the performer finally walks out of the exit."@en ;
