    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/278.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Bright Snow (晴雪)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the work entitled \"Bright Snow (晴雪)\" executed in 1985 by Shao Yan.  There are two characters and a lower-left little inscription. The two characters qing 晴 (“bright”), whose edges look like carved wood signs, and xue 雪 (“snow”), fat and thick with a firm central part, represent a surprising contrast just like the sunlight that spreads with roar over the silent snow. For both characters, Shao Yan adopts the “flying white” (feibai飞白) technique, which means using the half-dry brush, in order to represent the wild landscape of Northern China struck by violent snowstorms. The little inscription is written with brushstrokes full of ink and it has an angular shape, balancing the entire calligraphy. "@en ;
