    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Peach blossoms fall in a chaotic rain of red dust (桃花乱落红尘雨)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the work “Peach blossoms fall in a chaotic rain of red dust”. This is an "artwork with more characters” (duozishu chuangzuo 多字数创作) executed by Shao Yan in 1995.  It is characterised by a huge variation in the thickness of the lines and by words that seem to radiate from the centre of the work and to continue beyond the paper’s edge. The words are executed in an original cursive form, achieved by frequently changing the speed and direction of the brush until the characters become almost unreadable, in order to emphasise the harmony and movement of the lines. \r
Shao Yan executed the characters taohua luanluo hongchengyu 桃花乱落红尘雨 in cursive style and placed them vertically on the paper to call to the viewer's mind the poetic image of the falling peach blossom and they are composed by horizontal lines and dots that cover the work and recall the lines of a score embellished with musical notes. This creates a perfect union between the spatial structure of Chinese characters and the temporal rhythm, which reminds of the crackling red rain.\r
Shao Yan borrowed from the poem “Invitation to Wine” (Jiangjinjiu 将进酒) by Li He 李贺 (790-816) the expression "like red rain" (ruhongyu 如红雨) and transformed it into "rain of red dust" (hongchenyu 红尘雨), inserting the character chen 尘 ("dust" ) between the character hong 红 ("red") and yu 雨 ("rain"), whose structure is made of a continuous motion of inextricable lines to balance the work. The characters "chen" and "yu" work in concert with the characters hua 花 (“flower”) and luan 乱 ("chaotic”) to mirror the scene of peach blossoms sliding down like rainwater.\r
The characters are executed not only with a usual brush but also with doubi 斗笔 (a large brush with the tip mounted on the final part of the bucket-shaped handle). \r
With this artwork, Shao Yan does not want to reproduce the meaningful forms of the characters but wants to convey to the observer the feeling evoked by the poetic verses. \r
\r
"""@en ;
