    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Chaos (lines)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the work “Chaos” (混沌) executed in 2011 by Shao Yan combining the technique of ink “washed” in water (shui de “chongxi” 水的 “冲洗”) with the use of a syringe. The artist added water to the ink in the syringe and then injected it on the paper allowing it to flow strong and free. \r
Shao Yan decided to limit the work beauty by only executing solid lines. The initial buzzing sound emitted by the ink escaping from the syringe, gradually fades into silence and it could represent the flowing blood that, when stopping, puts an end to life."""@en ;
