    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Desolation (幽)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the work “Desolation” executed in 2008 by Shao Yan who was inspired by the Sichuan earthquake disaster (May 12, 2008).\r
Shao Yan uses a paibi 排笔 brush (composed of small brushes joined together) and a long-tipped brush. The concave bottom of the character "you", should be intact and smooth but appears instead as a shaking groove. The bottom left corner tilts out of the work while the top right corner leaps in mid-air, filling the work with an enormous sense of instability like mountains collapsing as the earth quakes. The central part of the work is executed with a dry brush that creates the shapes of the cracks. Both '幺' elements of the character tilt and succumb together with the entire structure. The work is criss-crossed by dots and ink splashes that look like a crowd scattering in different directions but, there is no possibility to escape because it is impossible to elude natural disasters."""@en ;
