    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q46> ;
    ns1:description "Isabelle Giovacchini was born in Nice in 1982. She lives and works between Paris and the Mediterranean, according to her projects. She first attended the École nationale supérieure de la Photographie in Arles and subsequently obtained a Master's degree in literary creation at the Université Jean-Jaurès in Toulouse. A rare and singular figure in French photography, Isabelle has presented her work particularly in cities such as Marseille, Montpellier, Reims, Nice, Tours, Paris and Berlin. She was able to develop her research during stays in France (Paris, Metz) and abroad (in countries such as Brazil, Germany and Italy). In 2020 Isabelle won the Epkhrasis scholarship, which takes the form of a critical text that appeared in Le Quotidien de l'Art. She is currently developing a project relating to the archaeological finds of Lake Nemi, near Rome."@en ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Not present"@en ;
