    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/438.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/B 50 (Sophia) Model - performance/installation: plaster's geometric shapes (lines)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the performance \"Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/B 50 (Sofia) Model - performance/installation: plaster's geometric shapes [张强踪迹学报告A/B50 (索非亚) 模型 - 行为/ 装置：石膏几何体]\". In this performance, Zhang Qiang writes on sheets of paper and on geometric shapes made of white chalk. The artist is seen from behind and never looks at where he paints, while the female British counterpart named Sophia Huist conveys the artist's movements. She moves the paper or objects on which Zhang Qiang is working, thus shattering, or deconstructing his work. The paper sheets and the plaster's geometric shapes are full of black ink traces (lines and spots). After being used for the performance, these geometric shapes will be also used for an installation." ;
