    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/449.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Watching the Sea and Listening to the Waves (观海听涛)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the artwork “Watching the sea and listening to the waves” (Guan hai ting tao 观海听涛) executed in 2015 by Shao Yan. \r
Shao Yan wrote the four characters on the surface of  a cylindrical “maotong” (帽筒) vase in white porcelain. \r
Shao Yan engraved the four characters on the surface of the vessel and then filled in the blue color. The four characters recall the "bird seal script" (niao zhuan 鸟篆), a kind of artistic script in common use during the late Warring States period (475-221 BC). This script is characterized by gently and intricated curved lines decorated with bird designs. In this work, Shao Yan re-elaborates this script drawing birds and fishes in a naïf style, recalling the acquatic scene evoked by the four characters. The style of the characters reflected a modern taste, still maintaining the essence of archaic Chinese characters."""@en ;
