    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/C 24 (Chi Wu) Model (lines)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the performance  Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/C 24 (Chi Wu) Model [张强踪迹学报告 A/C 24 (赤乌) 模型]. The body of  the female counterpart Chi Wu 赤乌 is full of \"ink traces\" leaved  by Zhang Qiang through the brush. After being \"traced\" by Zhang Qiang, the performer Chi Wu (whose real name is Ma Yuanyuan 马媛媛) performs the \"sword dance\" (jianwu 剑舞), one of the four classical dances used in Chinese opera. While holding the sword, Chi Wu has two red Chinese knots tied to her wrist. Chi Wu's lips are also red, but painted only in the middle, not completely."@en ;
