    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Dream (做梦)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of two characters 做梦 (DREAM!) made with a red duct tape. The sentence is meant to be the Chinese equivalent of a command with the verb in the imperative mode (Dream!). Since the new slogan had changed from Hu Jingtao’s ‘Harmonious society’ to Xi Jingping’s ‘Chinese Dream’, this action was thought to send a provocative message about the contradiction between the continuity of the unresolved precarity between the government change. The choice of red is obviously linked to the Chinese tradition of writing with red ink (and even blood) to convey and something urgent and aggressive. "@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Modern" ;
