    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Lanting Xu Stones (《兰亭序》)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the artwork "Lanting Xu Stones", made by Luo Qi for the performance "Luo Qi and Collegium Musicum Almae Matris - Musicalligraphy Performance (Luo Qi yu Boluoniya daxue yuedui - shufa yinyue biaoyan 洛齐与博洛尼亚大学乐队 - 书法音乐表演)". Luo Qi writes characters from the "Orchid Pavilion Preface" (Lanting Xu 兰亭序) on twelve Carrara marble stones with black ink.  \r
The characters inscribed on these twelve stones are: 茂林 (màolín, “luxuriant woods”), 曲水 (qǔshuǐ, “winding stream”), 游目骋怀 (yóu mù chěng huái, “to let the eyes wander and the mind expand”), 和畅 (héchàng, “harmonious and pleasant”), 仰观 (yǎngguān, “to gaze upward”), 俯察品类 (fǔchá pǐnlèi, “to observe all things below”), 崇山 (chóngshān, “lofty mountains”), 一觞一咏 (yī shāng yī yǒng, “one cup, one poem”), etc."""@en ;
