        <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/625_2.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Chinese Knot - Chapter Three : She/Her (奸、奻 、姦、妖...)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the performance \"Chinese Knots - Chapter Three : She/Her (结 - 第三章 : 她)\" which takes place in Linz (Austria) in 2022 in occasion of the \"Performance Festival: Non-fungible Body?\" (June, 16 - 19). The artist Echo Morgan, after colouring her body white, writes Chinese characters in red ink all over her body. She writes the character \"ta 她\"(she/her) on her face and her body becomes a scroll of \"patriarchal text\". The artist decides to cover her body with some derogatory and insulting words associated with the character \"nü 女\" (female), such as: \"jian 奸\" (rape); \"nuan 奻\" (stupid); \"jian 姦\" (evil); \"yao 妖\" (demon); \"biao 婊\"(bitch); \"piao 嫖\"(brothe); \"pin 姘\"(mistress); \"chang 娼\"(whore); \"ji 妓\"(prostitute); \"nu 奴\"(slave); \"shua 耍\"(play); \"lan 婪\"(greed); \"ning 佞\"(insincerity); \"wang 妄\" (foolish); \"yu 娱\"(entertainment); \"xian 嫌\"(fedup); \"fang 妨\"(harm); \"ji 嫉\" (envy) ; \"du 妒\" (jealous); \"bi 妣\" (dead mother); \"ban 姅\" (miscarriage). She also covers her body with famous Chinese saying such as: “Three Obediences and Four Virtues” (san cong si de 三从四德); “A woman's virtue is to have no talent\" (nuzi wu cai bian shi de 女子无才便是德); \"Men are superior and women are inferior” (nan zun nu bei 男尊女卑); \"Beauty leads to disaster/femme fatale” (hongyanhuoshui 红颜祸水)."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Free" ;
