    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Rubbing script, I am who I am, change me no one can (我有我在...)" ;
    ns1:description "In this Calli-Writing Unit, Fung MIng Chip wrote the sentence: wǒ yǒu wǒ zài, xī shén wúnài \"我有我在, 息神无奈\", whose meaning is \"I am who I am, Change me no one can\".  The big characters are written vertically in only one column. In this work, the artist plays with different dilutions of ink in water, creating stratified effects. The \"script type\" he creates in this work is \"rubbing script\" (ta zi 拓字) that reproduces the effect of rubbing tehnique. The artist wrote the characters on xuan paper with water and put the piece of paper into a pool of ink. The traces of writing instantly revealed themselves. "@en ;
