    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU A Love Poem Written in Water (我在水中...)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the performance \"A Love Poem Written in Water (写在水中的爱情诗)\". Li Xinmo starts rewriting a love poem written by herself using a classical lyric form (ci 词) using vermilion ink on a silk cloth. The characters are spreading outward in the water and all that remained on the white silk cloth are stained spots that resembled tears. As the artists specified: \" It's a poem that I created before the performance. It was a writing of my feelings about a love that I had experienced, an intimate inner experience. I put a long strip of white yarn in the water and then wrote the poem in vermillion ink, the writing dispersing as I wrote. The poem eventually dissolved in the water. The process of this performance is also an interpretation of love, that it is fickle, sad, uncertain, and impossible to keep. With this work I may be saying goodbye to the love I have experienced before, and to the person I once was\"."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Unidentifiable" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1396399>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
