    ns1:description "The \"Shuowen Jiezi 说文解字\" is an ancient Chinese dictionary from the Eastern Han dynasty composed by Xu Shen (c. 58 – c. 148 CE). It was the first dictionary to analyze the structure of the characters and to give the rationale behind them, as well as the first to use the principle of organization by sections with shared components called radicals (bushou 部首)."@en ;
    ns1:hasWikidataResource <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1072348> .

