    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/chaos_script>,
        <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/773.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Filling the World with Love (《让世界充满爱》)" ;
    ns1:description """The content of this CWU is the song "Let the World Be Full of Love" (Rang shijie chongman ai 让世界充满爱) by the Chinese composer Guo Feng 郭峰 (b. 1962).  This song was composed in response to Michael Jackson's "We are the World" and to other American pop songs. It is in fact a hymn to peace, fraternity and universal love. It was first presented to the public at a charity concert held at the Beijing Workers' Stadium on May 9, 1986 in commemoration of the International Year of Peace. This concert involved more than one hundred Chinese singers. The show caused a huge sensation in mainland China, and the theme song "Let the World Be Full of Love" became a hit. The performance greatly promoted the development of Chinese original pop music and became one of the milestones in the history of Chinese pop music, and Guo Feng was later hailed by the Chinese official media as "the first person to launch Chinese original pop music" (Chinaedunet.com). The influence of "Let the World Be Full of Love" continues to this day, as it was used as one of the theme songs for the opening ceremony of the Beijing Winter Olympics in 2022.\r
Wang Dongling wrote the text of this song in 'Chaos Script' (luanshu 乱书), his personal illegible cursive script, using an Apple pencil on an iPad screen. The color of calligraphy is a vivid violet, which evokes the graffiti style. The background features a detail from arguably the most famous portrait in the world, Leonardo da Vinci's "Mona Lisa".\r
"""@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q208045>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q47071> ;
    ns1:hasBigCharactersCalligraphy false ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasCharacterForm <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178528> ;
    ns1:hasColophon false ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing",
        "Set of signs (illegible)" ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/773_HR.png> ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/769> ;
    ns1:madeUsingTool <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q20962515> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 130 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """Tenderly holding you face\r
To wipe away you tears\r
My heart always belong to you\r
Tell me you’ll never be alone\r
Looking deeply into you eyes\r
No need to say another word\r
Holding tightly onto your hands\r
This warmth will never ever change\r
Together we share joy\r
We share same sorrow\r
And we have the same aspiration\r
Together we strive\r
Together we dream\r
We treasure the same love in our hearts\r
No matter if we know each other\r
No matter if you’re here or faraway\r
Let us pray with sincerity\r
To wish you peace and happiness."""@en,
        """轻轻地捧起你的脸\r
为你把眼泪擦干\r
这颗心永远属于你\r
告诉我不再孤单\r
深深地凝望你的眼\r
不需要更多的语言\r
紧紧地握住你的手\r
这温暖依旧未改变\r
我们同欢乐\r
我们同忍受\r
我们怀着同样的期待\r
我们共风雨\r
我们共追求\r
我们珍存同一样的爱\r
无论你我可曾相识\r
无论在眼前在天边\r
真心的为你祝愿\r
祝愿你幸福平安\r
\r
"""@zh,
        """Qīng qīng de pěng qǐ nǐ de liǎn\r
wèi nǐ bǎ yǎnlèi cā gān\r
zhè kē xīn yǒngyuǎn shǔyú nǐ\r
gàosù wǒ bù zài gūdān\r
shēn shēn de níngwàng nǐ de yǎn\r
bù xūyào gèng duō de yǔyán\r
jǐn jǐn de wò zhù nǐ de shǒu\r
zhè wēnnuǎn yījiù wèi gǎibiàn\r
wǒmen tóng huānlè\r
wǒmen tóng rěnshòu\r
wǒmen huáizhe tóngyàng de qídài\r
wǒmen gòng fēngyǔ\r
wǒmen gòng zhuīqiú\r
wǒmen zhēn cún tóng yīyàng de ài\r
wúlùn nǐ wǒ kě céng xiāngshí\r
wúlùn zài yǎnqián zài tiānbiān\r
zhēnxīn de wèi nǐ zhùyuàn\r
zhùyuàn nǐ xìngfú píng'ān"""@zh-Latn ;
    ns1:vectorisedOrDigitised true .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/776> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
