    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/cursive_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/776.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU View from Heaven (泰山成砥砺...)" ;
    ns1:description """ This CWU is part of the artwork "View from Heaven" (泰山成砥砺, 黄河为裳带). It represents ten huge characters of different dimensions. The content is a transcription of two lines from the 48th poem included in the collection entitled "Singing My Cares" (Yong huai 咏怀) by the poet Ruan Ji (210-263) . (Reference of the collection is the Fan Qin/Chen Dewen edition).  In the visual result given by the ten monumental characters of "View from Heaven", and in particular in the last character of the verse (dai 带), projected onto the entire surface of the final panel, we see the influence of a Japanese calligraphic current, known as the Few-characters current (shao zi pai 少字派). In particular, the work recalls the style by Inoue Yuichi (井上有一, 1916-1985) and its impact on Wang Dongling's art, who began producing monumental characters in his studio in 1985. As declared by Gao (2021: xi) , "The work gives the viewers an impression as if they were facing gigantic pieces of cliff inscriptions on the northern mountains. The ten huge characters in Cursive Script exhibit a remarkable vigorand innate solidity and exuberance as if they travelled through eternity, with a cosmic solitude facing heaven and earth alone, as well as a mountain-moving and ocean-filling power”.\r
"""@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns1:hasBigCharactersCalligraphy true ;
