    ns1:description "Chen Yeung-ping is a Hong Kong composer. He received degrees from Hong Kong Baptist University, the Hong Kong Academy for Performing Arts, and the University of California, San Diego (UCSD). From 2013 to 2014, he worked as an assistant researcher for Professor Lei Liang at the Qualcomm Institute, focusing on Chinese music materials. His creative work has been featured in the New York Times and the South China Morning Post. Chen's compositions are published by Universal Edition (Austria) and PARMA Records (USA). He has been a composer-fellow for various prestigious institutions, including the Darmstadt Ensemble Project, the International Ensemble Modern Academy, and others. Currently, he is an Associate Professor of Music at South China Normal University, Director of the Hong Kong Composers’ Guild, and a member of the Executive Committee of the Hong Kong Jockey Club Music and Dance Fund Awardee Association."@en ;
