<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1115> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1095> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Minimal Oriental oder Das grosse Lernen"@de,
        "Minimal Oriental or The Great Learning"@en ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q64> ;
    ns2:P580 "2009-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2009-02-21"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description "The \"Minimal Oriental  or The Great Learning\" exhibition was  held at the Alexander Ochs Galleries  in Berlin from the 24th January to the 21st February 2009. It showcased innovative approach to calligraphic artworks, paintings and sculptures by  the Beijing-based conceptual artist Chen Guangwu. Through meticulous techniques, such as reproducing texts from Confucian classics only to dissolve them into sculptures of paper pulps, Chen explores themes of cultural transformation and loss, and he offers a unique perspective on a culture he believes is eroding. Central to his work is the recognition of calligraphy as a performance art, with each brushstroke embodying the calligrapher's gestures and intentions. Chen's minimalist compositions blend tradition with modernity, inviting viewers to contemplate the intricate balance between past and present in contemporary Chinese art."@en ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1113>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1120> .

