    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/119.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 New Style (KYGS)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is a lettering piece \"KYGS\" written in a very complex wildstyle, with lots of 3D effects, that seems to reproduce the knottiness of the bamboos. The interlocking letters involved in the piece KYGS are an acronym of  \"KwanYin Graffiti Studio\", and also their colors (from light green to very dark green) are very similar to bamboos. The use of green recalls the tradition of Western realism, based on a steadfast devotion to color truth. At the same time, the various shades of green also remind the greenish patina of ancient \"Chinese bronze vessels\" (qingtongqi 青铜器). According to EricTin: \"The source of inspiration of New Style is ancient Chinese bronze ware\" (EricTin 2008). This is evident not only in the choice of colors, but also in the \"angularity\" of the lettering piece \"patterned with ridges\" that replaces the typical ribbed surface of bronze vessels."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Modern" ;
