    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Society (社会)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit, on the right-hand corner of the piece, is composed of two characters Shehui 社会 (Society). Shehui 社会 is the name of the brand  linked to the world of skateboarding that Li Qiuqiu founded in 2001 with other friends. The purpose of the brand was promoting events, activities and products connected with spreading this sport in China along with its related cultural industry. \r
The two Chinese characters on the right stand out on a background of blue bubbles, the same colour as the tag: the fill-in is light blue, the outline is white, and the depths are blue. The writing style used for the Chinese characters is geometric and reminiscent of “regular script” (kaishu 楷书), an easily intelligible calligraphic style where each stroke is distinct and discernible. All elements are reminiscent of aquatic settings. Thus, through the marine atmosphere, Li Qiuqiu seems to disclose a world in which everything – waves, bubbles, architecture, walls, street art – is fluid and fleeting, while also granting a touch of liveliness to the composition, as we occasionally find in his graffiti."""@en ;
