    ns2:P664 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/130> ;
    ns1:description "The \"First Exhibition of Chinese Modern Calligraphy\" was held in 1985 at the National Art Museum of China and marks the birth of modern Chinese calligraphy and the modernist movement. It features a total of 72 works by 26 artists from the \"Chinese Modern Calligraphy and Painting Association\" (Zhongguo xiandai shuhua xuehui 中国现代书画学会) founded in October 1985. Among the most important artists featured in the exhibition are Huang Miaozi 黄苗子 (1913-2012), Zhang Ding 张仃 (1917-2010), and Li Luogong 李骆公 (1917-1992), together with other artists such as Gu Gan 古干 (1942-2020), Wang Xuezhong 王学仲 (1925–2013), Ma Chengxiang 马承祥 (b. 1937), and Dai Shanqing 戴山青 (1944-2004), who were also the promoters and organizers of the exhibition. Other notable artists are Wang Naizhuang 王乃壮 (1928-2024), Zhu Naizheng 朱乃正 (1935-2013), Su Yuanzhang 苏元章 (1924-2002), Xie Shengpei 谢盛培 (1929-2021), Zuo Hanchao 左汉桥 (b. 1946), Deng Yuanchang 邓元昌 (b. 1939), Xu Futong 许福同 (b. 1944), Yan Binghui 阎秉会 (b. 1956), and Lin Xinchen 林信成 (b. 1952). Other artists participating in the exhibition are Peng Shiqiang 彭世强, Xie Deping 谢德萍, Gao Mang 高莽, Yu Ren 于人, Wang Ding 王宁, Du Zhongxin 杜中信, Wu Chuanlin 吴传麟, Zhang Hu 张虎, Gao Shouquan 高寿荃, and Hou Dechang 侯德昌."@en ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/127>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/133> .

