    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU1 Living Word (鸟）" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of a series of plexiglass cutouts of the various forms of the character niao 鸟 (bird), from the most ancient forms, such as “oracle bone script” (jiaguwen 甲骨文) and seal style (zhuanshu 篆书) to the modern standard, in which each form is rendered with a different color. Rising into the air, the character gradually changes from its simplified modern form to non-simplified traditional forms written in different calligraphic styles and finally to the ancient Chinese pictograph for “bird”."@en ;
