    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 The Invisible Words: A GPS Calligraphy Project (世)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the Chinese characters created through GPS tracking on the roads of Beijing, as Part 1 of the Running Script - GPS Calligraphy Project. In this phase, Feng Mengbo created characters in Regular Script, such as shì 世 (world), driving along the long streets within the urban landscape of Beijing. The process involves detailed study and planning of the characters, including the marking of waypoints and mapping the path to form the blueprint for the driving route. This route, meticously programmed into a GPS navigation system, guides the driver along the path designated by the artist. Simultaneously, the artist employs a separate GPS device to record and collect data on the vehicle's trajectory, capturing the creation of each character in real-time."@en ;
