    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 The Invisible Words: A GPS Calligraphy Project (太平)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the Chinese characters created through GPS tracking on the water of the bay of Brisbane, Australia, as Part 2 of the Running Script - GPS Calligraphy Project. In this phase, Feng Mengbo created characters in Running/Cursive Script, navigating with a motorboat along the bay in Brisbane. The process involves detailed study and planning of the characters, including the marking of waypoints and mapping the path to form the blueprint for the navigation route. The path, meticously programmed into a GPS navigation system, guides the boat driver along the path designated by the artist. Simultaneously, the artist employs a separate GPS device to record and collect data on the boat's trajectory, capturing the creation of each character in real-time."@en ;
