    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Overturning the Mountains (山摧)" ;
    ns1:description "Thic CWU consists of two large characters as foreground text: “山” (shan) meaning \"mountain\" in the upper left-hand corner a large character and “摧” (cui) meaning \"destruction\" or \"overturning.\" The visual arrangement suggests a dynamic interaction between the two, with  \"mountain\" (shan 山) looked as if it were being overturned by the force of the other main character \"overturning\" (cui 摧).  These two characters are part of a poem by Li Bai 李白 (701-762) entitled Shu dao nan 蜀道難 (The Hard Road to Sichuan), partially written around the big character \"山\" in a very free composition. The characters \"山摧\" appear in the first of these two verses.  "@en ;
