    ns1:description """The exhibition "WORDS & SILENCE, Poetry and Philosophy in Calligraphy, QIU Zhenzhong" (Yu · Mo / Qiu Zhenzhong: Shuxie zhong de shi yu zhexue 语·默 / 邱振中：书写中的诗与哲学) marks the debut of Qiu Zhenzhong's large-scale installation piece "Void - Flow" measuring 6×2.5×1.2 meters. The uniqueness of the piece lies in the deflection of its components, which creates a twist between lines and surfaces, setting it apart in both structural principle and visual effect from existing works. It explores spatial continuity and the twisting of lines, offering an innovative experience.\r
"Void·Flow" can be seen as an interpretation of the artist's handwriting. Through this visual language, the artist not only conveys their creative concept but also invites the audience to contemplate the relationship between space, lines, and artistic expression. The work's innovation lies in its ability to merge these elements into a cohesive and thought-provoking installation.\r
\r
""" ;
