    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Elvis (黄祸)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit features the characters \"Huanghuo 黃禍\" (Yellow Peril) in the upper left corner. These characters are rendered in non-simplified characters, with certain indexing components written in small seal script (xiaozhuan 小篆), a style commonly used in ancient China for formal inscriptions and seals. The positioning of the characters evokes the appearance of a colophon, similar to an artist’s signature, as often found in large-character calligraphic works (dazi 大字). This placement, typical in traditional Chinese calligraphy, emphasizes the artistic and cultural significance of the characters, further blending art with written language."@en ;
