    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Cursive/Wild Grass (lines)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU (\"Cursive/Wild Grass\") is part of the solo performance-installation by Yin Mei, realized on February 25, 2006, at the Vision Festival in New York. Dressed in black and positioned on a large white paper sheet, Yin Mei begins to move in slow, serpentine patterns. In a subsequent phase, her body—now soaked in black ink—continues these gestures, leaving marks on the surface through direct contact. These imprints, made with her limbs and entire body, evoke calligraphic brushstrokes, particularly referencing the expressive and unrestrained energy of \"wild cursive\" script. The resulting composition consists solely of calligraphic lines and ink traces produced by the motion of the body." ;
