    ns2:P571 "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1650.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """The artwork titled "Please Describe Graffiti to a Blind Person" (qing xiang mangren miaoshu tuya 请向盲人描述涂鸦) was created in Guangzhou in 2023.\r
Zeit 時間 used spray paint in his straight, large charactering to write the title phrase. The piece features a white outline and a multicolored fill (mainly pastel colors)and includes also various tags in white, such as STH, 2G, and FEK (his crews), as well as the name "Zeit" in traditional characters "時間," possibly the names Oreone and Leven (two potential crewmates) and the same characters of the piece above in white.\r
In an interview (Bisceglia 2024), Zeit states: "This is a place full of graffiti, and people come here to take photos. I wrote ‘Please describe graffiti to the blind’ because I hope that after taking a picture, people will realize that sharing color with others is more meaningful." While, on his Instagram post, hedescribes the work as follows: "The culture of graffiti has entered the public's field of vision because of its conspicuous colors and its occupation of public space. We also call it a part of ‘visual art.’ But have we, as writers, ever thought about how to describe graffiti to a blind person? Give it a try, I look forward to seeing your responses in the comments."\r
Zeit 時間's decision to paint the phrase "Please Describe Graffiti to the Blind" reflects a profound exploration of the intersection between visual art and accessibility. By inviting viewers, especially those who might not experience color or visual aesthetics, to engage with graffiti in a different way, he emphasizes the need for inclusivity and encourages a broader understanding of art that transcends traditional boundaries.\r
This phrase challenges the norm that art is solely a visual experience, prompting people to consider how the essence of graffiti can be communicated beyond visual elements. It also serves as a cultural commentary, recognizing the limitations of visual art for some audiences while inviting discussion about the role of public art in society and its impact on different communities.\r
Through his focus on sharing color, Zeit highlights the importance of community and collective experiences, encouraging viewers to think about how to convey the essence of graffiti to someone who cannot see it. In doing so, he emphasizes the social aspect of art and the connections it can create. Overall, Zeit 時間’s piece acts as a thought-provoking commentary on accessibility, the nature of art, and the significance of community engagement in creative expression."""@en ;
