<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1673> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42948> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q9186> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1088>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q208045>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1673.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Jiangxi Graffiti (赣塗)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of the Chinese characters "Gantu 赣塗," where "gan" signifies Jiangxi Province, often abbreviated in this way in local discourse, and "tu" denotes painting or coating, often associated with the act of graffiti. Together, the characters could be translated as "Jiangxi Graffiti," symbolizing an artistic homage to the region.\r
The style of the Chinese characters combines regular script (kaishu 楷书) with an ignorant style, characterized by a spontaneous, raw execution that emphasizes expression over refinement. This juxtaposition of traditional calligraphic form with modern graffiti technique creates a dynamic visual contrast, highlighting Beer1ne's ability to integrate cultural heritage within contemporary street art. The regular script provides a sense of formality and structure, while the ignorant style adds an element of unrestrained creativity, evoking the spontaneity that defines graffiti.\r
The use of stars, dots, and LED-inspired light patterns in the surrounding environment adds an additional layer of energy and modernity to the artwork. These elements create a vibrant atmosphere that complements the boldness of the characters. The left panel, rendered in a striking yellow and red color scheme, draws attention to the textual elements, while the right panel, dominated by cooler tones of blue and green, balances the composition with abstract forms and expressive graffiti lettering.\r
Within the character "gan 赣," specifically in the radical "li 立 (stand)," there are two characters "yishi 意實 (意实)," meaning “real”: “yi 意” is rendered in Jiaguwen (oracle bone script), while “shi 實” is written in Xiaozhuan (seal script). Both characters are rendered in a golden hue, evoking the appearance of LED lights and dots.\r
In its entirety, "Jiangxi Painting" reflects a nuanced dialogue between traditional Chinese calligraphy and modern graffiti culture. It underscores the artist’s regional roots in Jiangxi Province while exploring the broader possibilities of contemporary urban art. The interplay between structured calligraphy and spontaneous graffiti emphasizes both continuity with the past and innovation, making it a standout piece in Beer1ne’s artistic repertoire."""@en ;
