    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1770.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Inky Strings: Old Friends from Mountains and Rivers (山河故人)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the performance realized by Echo Morgan held on October 29, 2023, at the International Museum and Library of Music in Bologna, as part of the collateral events related to the exhibition “Sounds of Ink: Luo Qi and 30 Years of Calligraphyism”. It consists of the four Chinese characters “Shan he gu ren 山河故人” (Old friends from mountains and rivers) that she shaped on her face. These characters are the original title of Jia Zhangke’s 2015 film, internationally known as "Mountains May Depart". It is a drama exploring memory, affection, and the social transformations of contemporary China. Set across three distinct periods, the film follows the 25-year-old shopkeeper Tao and the choices that separate her from both the men in her life and her son, Daole/Dollar. Through the growing geographical and emotional distance between mother and son, Jia reflects on globalization, cultural displacement, and the fragility of family bonds.\r
Literally, the phrase "Shan he gu ren 山河故人" can be read as “mountains, rivers, and old friends”, evoking a sense of enduring landscapes set against the fragility of human relationships and time. Jia Zhangke’s choice of title reflects the film’s central concern with change, memory, and the passage of generations: the permanence of nature contrasts with the impermanence of human bonds and personal destinies. Echo inscribed these characters on her face by following the same iconographic style as the film’s official poster, thereby creating a visual and symbolic bridge between cinema and performance art. By appropriating Jia Zhangke’s cinematic language and re-situating it within her own body art practice, she reactivates the poetic resonance of "Shan he gu ren" in a new context marked by ecological urgency."""@en ;
