    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/941> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork was realized during the performance by Wang Dongling held the 31st of October, 2011 at the Zhejiang Art Museum of Hangzhou. The content of the calligraphy realized by Wang Dongling is one of the two poems entitled “Drinking on West Lake First Shine After the Rain” (Yin hu shang chu qing hou yu 饮湖上初晴后雨) by Su Shi 苏轼 (1037-1101, better known as Su Dongpo 苏东坡), an eminent poet of the Song dynasty (960-1279). The poem describes the beauty of West Lake in Hangzhou, China, after a rain. It evokes vivid images of nature, highlighting the scenic beauty of the lake and its surroundings and reflecting on the interaction between man and nature. Characters are written in cursive script (cao shu) and praise the beauty of West Lake (Xihu 西湖)." ;
