    ns1:description "In this artwork, Gu Gan reimagines the character  mǎ 马 (horse) using its ancient pictographic forms. The character is repeated across the paper, creating the impression of a moving herd of horses.  Making use of the pictographic nature of Chinese writing, 'Horses' exemplifies \"pictorial/pictographic calligraphy\", where Chinese characters transforms into \"pictorial images,\" resembling stylized and primitive representations of their meaning. Even if viewers do not recognize them as Chinese characters, they can still appreciate the naïf charm and primal vitality of the imagery." ;
