        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q39338>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q47071>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P571 "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """The work 'Deer crying' was realized by the artist Gu Gan in 1990. The artist reiterated the pictographic versions of the two characters of the title lu 鹿 ('deer') and ming 鸣 ('cry') to recreate the din of a herd of wailing deer. The addition of colors, such as brown, orange and yellow, accentuate the pictorial charge of the representation.\r
The style is reminiscent of Joan Miró, and in fact Gu Gan was deeply influenced by this artist together with Kandinsky and Klee. The increasingly thinner brush strokes used by Gu Gan, the use of a line that seeks to hoard and manifest the beauty of form in all its splendor, the adoption of a “childish” language, the isolation of single element/character repeated and arranged in deliberate composition are all references to these Western avant-gardists. \r
In November 1998, this work was featured in the European edition of Time magazine, as a testament to Gu Gan’s growing international recognition.""" ;
