    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5816> ;
    ns1:description "\"Art for the People\" is a monumental red banner.  It consists of four big signs in the middle which appears as Chinese script, but on the contrary they are written with English letters.  Xu Bing writes the  phrase 'Art for the People' using  his \"Square Word Calligraphy\", a writing system he designed to adapts the English alphabet to the stroke-based calligraphic structure forms of Chinese writing. The expression 'Art for the People' was used by Chairman Mao Zedong, while the red banner and the yellow brushstrokes reflect the visual aesthetics of mass mobilization." ;
