        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8646> ;
    ns1:description "Vivienne Tam is an internationally acclaimed fashion designer celebrated for blending Eastern and Western aesthetics and for her innovative collaborations that bridge fashion and technology. Recognized by Forbes and People for her influence and beauty, Tam’s work has been featured in major museums like the MET, V&A, and the Andy Warhol Museum. She authored the award-winning book \"China Chic\", and her designs, including iconic gowns from her \"Buddha collection\", were prominently featured in the MET’s exhibition \"China: Through the Looking Glass\" and the documentary \"The First Monday in May\". Honored with the \"China Fashion Award – International Designer of the Year 2017\", she returned to China in 2018 to debut her Spring/Summer 2019 show at Beijing’s Bird’s Nest Stadium. Her evening gowns are favored by global celebrities and public figures, including Lady Gaga, Gong Li, and members of the U.S. First Family." ;
