    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Love (愛)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of a dress designed by Vivienne Tam for her Fall-Winter 2013 \"Ready-to-Wear\" collection and presented at New York Fashion Week in 2013. It consists of the Chinese character \"ai 愛\" (love) at the heart—both literally and symbolically—of its composition. Written in non-simplified characters and positioned at chest level, the character becomes the focal point of the garment. Particularly striking is the use of red for the radical xin 心 (heart), visually isolating and elevating this element in line with traditional Chinese color symbolism, where red signifies vitality, emotion, and good fortune. The rest of the character \"ai 愛\" is rendered in white, creating a layered reading of love not just as a linguistic sign, but as a conceptual and emotional structure anchored in the body. The typical colors of calligraphy (black, white, and red) are reversed in their use: the backgroud color is black and the colors of characters is white, with the radical higlighted in red.  " ;
