    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/ugly_calligraphy> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 I am sick (我爱你)" ;
    ns1:description "The \"CWU 2 I am sick (我爱你)\" consists of the words \"wo ai ni (我爱你, “I love you”)\", which differ from the earlier black inscriptions. They appear in blue in the bottom right corner, written at the end of the repeated phrase \"wo you bing (我有病, “I am sick”)\", following a “wo” that would have marked the thirty-fifth repetition. This addition was likely made later by another emotional graffiti writer, perhaps as a gesture of consolation toward the original author."@en ;
