    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2345.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Ode of Eight Thousand Verses: Fortune n. 1 (signs)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of the Sanskrit parts in black.  The Sanskrit parts are extracts from the Sutra of the Perfection of Wisdom (Prajñāpāramitā Sutra) in 8,000 Lines, also called Transcendental Knowledge Sutra, which is a collection of Buddhist texts fundamental for the creation of Mahāyāna Buddhism. The main theme of Prajñāpāramitā Sutra literature is the achievement of the ‘perfection of wisdom’, which corresponds to ‘emptiness’ (Śūnyatā), that is the state of consciousness which understands the real nature of things, that is, the insubstantiality of phenomena as impermanent and interdependent, and which is capable of realizing Buddhahood and enlightenment. The graphs inspired to this text are no longer understandable due to the artistic rielaboration.\r
""" ;
