<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2348> a ns3:Q43229 ;
    ns2:P2561 "Minaxdo 米丈堂木作" ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8686> ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2470> ;
    ns2:P856 <http://en.minaxdo.com/index.shtml> ;
    ns1:description """Minaxdo is a distinguished participant in China’s refined material culture, dedicated to evolving into a leading brand that embodies a sophisticated and tasteful lifestyle. Rooted in the cultural heritage of the Southern Yangtze region, the brand draws inspiration from traditional Chinese architecture and furniture, imbuing each wooden artwork with rich cultural significance and enduring beauty. Through the seamless integration of elegant forms, meticulous craftsmanship, and contemporary design elements, Minaxdo’s creations exemplify both aesthetic refinement and modern sensibilities.\r
\r
Each piece is thoughtfully conceptualized and handcrafted from premium timber, reflecting a commitment to artistry and authenticity. Guided by a sincere, simple, and pure ethos, Minaxdo is devoted to offering culturally discerning and aesthetically sophisticated clientele bespoke artworks and personalized services of the highest excellence.""" ;
    ns1:hasOrganisationType <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6881511> ;
    ns1:isDesignerOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/124> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2358> a ns3:Q215627 ;
    ns2:P103 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P19 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q187136> ;
    ns2:P21 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6581072> ;
    ns2:P2561 "Song Chen 宋陈" ;
    ns2:P27 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148> ;
    ns2:P569 "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2577>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2578> ;
    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8686> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2358.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """Song Chen was born in Luoyang.  She is a contemporary eco-artist who uses earth and soil as both material and metaphor for her art.  \r
She is the founder of several projects, exhibitions, and festivals dedicated to ecological practices and soil healing, such as the "Soil Ecological Art Program" Art Public Education Project and the "World Soil Day Series Art Public Education Project". \r
Song Chen's practice reflects a deep attachment to her native land and a persistent inquiry into the ultimate destiny of humankind. In her hands, earth becomes more than material; it turns into a vessel of memory and vitality, bridging spiritual and physical realms, ancient and contemporary times.\r
Through a quiet, meditative process, Song Chen cultivates an artistic world rooted in ritual, emotion, and endurance. \r
Her works have been exhibited at major international art fairs, including Art Basel Hong Kong, the Hong Kong Art Fair, the Shanghai Art Fair, ART021 Shanghai Contemporary Art Fair, and the West Bund Art & Design.""" ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/2358_HR.jpg> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2380> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
