<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2393> a ns3:Q17514 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Freedom (自由)"@en,
        "自由 "@zh,
        "Zìyóu"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2390> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2979> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q104969796>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "2022"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """A representative example of the series "Chinese Emotional Graffiti - (Aspiration for) Freedom," is the graffito "Freedom (自由)" published online in April 2022, maybe created the same year.\r
This piece conveys significant meaning through its interaction with the surrounding environment. The two characters "ziyou 自由 (freedom)" are spray-painted in red on a weathered gray surface and appear visually enclosed within a metal cage. \r
The composition intensifies the socio-political resonance of the work: the act of inscribing “freedom” directly onto an urban infrastructure, only to have it visually confined by fencing, may be read as an implicit commentary on the restrictions placed upon individual liberties in the public sphere. \r
Interesting is the fact that the inscription is vertically arranged, written from top to bottom, recalling the traditional orientation of Chinese calligraphy while asserting its presence within a contemporary graffiti context."""@en ;
