<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2403> a ns3:Q17514 ;
    ns2:P1476 "I feel lonely (我感到孤单)"@en,
        "我感到孤单"@zh,
        "wǒ gǎndào gūdān"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2401> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1274479>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q223270> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q127418>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42948> ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q490> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P571 "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """This graffiti work presents a striking repetition of the pronoun "wo 我 (I)" sixteen times, followed by the phrase "wo gan dao gu dan 感到孤单 (I feel lonely)." The visual and linguistic accumulation of wo 我 intensifies the self-referential tone, evoking a sense of obsessive introspection and emotional isolation. The piece exemplifies how written language, particularly Chinese characters, can function as a direct medium of affect in contemporary urban expression.\r
Created outside of China, this work carries additional cultural resonance. Beyond its immediate reflection on solitude, likely amplified by the psychological aftermath of the COVID-19 lockdowns, it can be interpreted as a manifestation of the alienation experienced by Chinese individuals living abroad. The repetition of the pronoun "wo 我" may signify both an assertion of identity and an expression of displacement, as the artist’s voice echoes through an unfamiliar linguistic and cultural environment.\r
Through its minimalist structure and emotionally charged text, this graffito exemplifies the intersection of language, identity, and emotion within the framework of Chinese Emotional Graffiti, translating private sentiment into a universal visual statement on loneliness and belonging."""@en ;
