<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2432> a ns3:Q17514 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Covid lasts longer than any of your love (肺炎在的时间比你任何一场爱还久)"@en,
        "肺炎在的时间比你任何一场爱还久"@zh,
        "肺炎在的時間比你任何一場愛還久"@zh,
        "Fèiyán zài de shíjiān bǐ nǐ rènhé yī chǎng ài hái jiǔ"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2429> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q316>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81068910>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q84263196> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1432769>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935> ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q181557> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P571 "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P6375 "MRT Houyi station, Kaohsiung (Taiwan)."@en ;
    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81068910> ;
    ns1:description """The graffiti “Covid lasts longer than any of your love (肺炎在的時間比你任何一場愛還久)" was published online in 2023 and executed at MRT Houyi Station in Kaohsiung, Taiwan. The inscription, rendered in traditional Chinese characters, is painted in black on a corrugated galvanized steel panel.\r
The phrase encapsulates the prolonged sense of loneliness and emotional disconnection that marked those difficult pandemic years.\r
The work exemplifies the emotionally charged irony characteristic of Chinese Emotional Graffiti, where the language of affection and illness intertwines to expose the fragility of human connection in times of crisis. It engages deeply with themes of unspoken emotion, communicative breakdown, and the inner tension between expression and restraint. Through its abstract wordplay, the statement of despair transforms into a poetic meditation on endurance and loss. By merging traditional Chinese script with contemporary urban aesthetics, the graffiti bridges cultural symbolism and shared human experience, inviting reflection on the complexities of love, isolation, and the modern condition."""@en ;
