<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2494> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41670> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1860> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2494.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 WRITE Logo (R-I-T-E)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the WRITE Logo. It consists of the combination of the Latin letters \"R-I-T-E\". These letters are not merely typographic symbols but are conceptually and visually integrated with the upper part of the Chinese character xie 写. The initial “W” is derived from the brushstrokes of the calligraphic character, while the remaining letters “R‑I‑T‑E” are rendered in a digital font. Notably, the final “E” is stylized as a rotated “3”, referencing a non‑linguistic communicative system and emphasizing the logo’s experimental and multimodal nature. This fusion creates a hybrid linguistic sign in which traditional calligraphic gestures and modern Latin script coexist, allowing the word to function both as a readable English text and as a visual extension of the calligraphic form." ;
