    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2550.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork is an ink-and-color calligraphic painting realized by Pu Lieping in 2021. It is inspired by the symphonic intermezzo “Meditation” from the opera Thaïs by Jules Massenet. The artwork translates the emotional atmosphere and melodic structure of the violin into visual form through the language of Chinese calligraphy.\r
The composition is characterized by thin, drifting brushstrokes that resemble floating threads, echoing the lyrical movement of the violin melody. Pale ink washes spread across the surface of the paper, creating a spacious atmosphere and emphasizing the contrast between emptiness and presence. Richer ink tones and thicker strokes introduce rhythmic variation and suggest the deeper resonance of the orchestral accompaniment.\r
Subtle touches of color, including faint tones of red, blue, and green, enhance the visual atmosphere while maintaining the restrained aesthetics of ink painting. Through this synesthetic translation of sound/music into calligraphic gesture, the work expresses a contemplative emotional state and demonstrates the expressive potential of the ink-based art of Chinese characters (hanzi shuimo yishu 汉字水墨艺术).""" ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3305213> ;
    ns1:hasColophon true ;
