<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/263> a ns3:Q184485 ;
    ns2:P1132 1 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Left/Right: Deviation from the Centre (左右：偏离正中)"@en,
        "左右：偏离正中"@zh,
        "Zuǒyòu: piānlí zhèngzhòng"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P175 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/249> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q107>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q10874>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1895873>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2562511>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3058834>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5004679> ;
    ns2:P186 ns3:Q127418 ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q585> ;
    ns2:P585 "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """This public performance by Qiu Zhijie takes place in a museum of Oslo. The performer wears special shoes with the words "right" and "left" engraved to the sole both in Chinese characters and in latin letters. The performer is blindfolded and he tries to find the exit on the other side of a narrow hallway. On the floor, between the performance starting point and the exit, there is a line made of ink. If the performer walks straight, he reaches the exit without leaving any shoe prints behind. If he trails from the path, the words "left" and "right" will be imprinted to the surrounding floor, and he might run into the wall. The performance continues until the performer finally walks out of the exit.\r
Through this performance, Qiu Zhijie overturns the concept of "space", inverting its main terms (left/right). The space becomes a concealed place of dishorientation. The experience felt by the performer is emblematic of the condition of contemporary people, that have lost their certainties and their straight path. \r
\r
In 2002, Qiu Zhijie does a similar performance, entitled "The Long March: Left / Right"(长征 : 左右). In this performance, Qiu Zhijie becomes the performer. Qiu Zhijie wears a pair of special shoes during the road trip.  Beneath the left shoe there is a stamp depicting the character 右 (right) and the word "right", while beneath the right shoe there is the character 左 (left) and the word "left". In this manner, Qiu Zhijie leaves imprints of "left" and "right" during his journey. Most of the time the imprints remain invisible, and they exist unconsciously. These imprints are only visible when Qiu Zhijie walks across mud (on a soft soil) or when the shoe soils are wet after raining.  \r
This performance takes place in different locations, e.g. Lugu Lake in Yunnan , "Flying Tigers" airport in Lijiang, the site of Zunyi Meeting (in Guizhou), and the Luding Bridge in Sichuan.\r
These performances are part of the art project entitled "Long March - A Walking Visual Display". During this project, Qiu Zhijie and his partner Lu Jie, accompanied by over 250 people from China and abroad (artists, curators, writers, scholars), visited 12 of the 20 historical sites of China’s Long March. Working with local communities along the road in a renegotiation of the past and its multifaceted remembering, artworks were realised, performances enacted and affairs debated concerning a diverse array of issues, such as the question of authorship, place as a site of memory, and the meaning of social exchange through mobility.\r
"""@en ;
