    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P571 "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """“Sea” (海), executed in 2001 by Shao Yan, is the second version of the work also called “Sea” carried out in 1995 by the author himself.\r
Influenced by the painters Liu Guosong  刘国松 (1932 -) and Zhou Shaohua 周韶华 (1929 -), in 2001 the artist introduces a new technique consisting of the repeated execution of strokes on the paper which will later be washed in water. After the washing process, the path taken by the tip of the brush shines clearly on the paper, there is a large amount of ink and various intense gradiations. Shao Yan pays particular attention to the spacial order and the composition of the artwork but, introducing the element of water, he adds the concept of time to the construction of calligraphic space. He thus emphasises the instantaneous and unrepeatable nature of artistic creation.\r
Compared to “Sea” executed in 1995, this artwork is characterised by three-dimensional lines and better reproduces the blue-green color of the sea, its illusory and calm appearance and the abstract aesthetic beauty of form until the work reaches the perfect union of form and content."""@en ;
