    ns2:P571 "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P6375 "Moganshan Road, Shanghai"@en ;
    ns1:description """The artwork “Demolition (Chai 拆)” was painted in 2008 as a reaction to the city’s rapid dismantling and a protest against the demolition of historic, old buildings. De facto, the character “chai 拆” means “to demolish a building and relocate the inhabitants” and is basically used to mark an old building that had been scheduled for demolition. It is usually painted in red on house walls. In this piece, Dezio portrays his protest against the demolition of old buildings by personifying the “chai 拆” character: on the left, the radical “hand 扌” becomes a hand holding a hammer and “hitting” the radical “jin 斤” (on the right side), depicted as an old Chinese house in the process of demolition. The personified “chai 拆” is painted with a white fill-in and a black outline and is bombed with lots of original Chinese “chai 拆” character, marked in red and circled. On the left side, there is the tag “dezione”, on the right side there is the year of the creation”2008”. The “Chai 拆” character has two different backgrounds: the first is a yellow burning star with a red outline, the second is the black wall.\r
"""@en ;
