<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/398> a ns3:Q7725310 ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Shao Yan White and Blue Porcelain – Calligraphy and Ink Shooting Series (邵岩书法与射墨的青花瓷系列)"@en,
        "邵岩书法与射墨的青花瓷系列"@zh,
        "Shào Yán shūfǎ yǔ shè mò de qīnghuācí xìliè"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/277> ;
    ns2:P580 "2022"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/398.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "This series of works is executed by Shao Yan in September 2022. Inspired by Ming “blue and white porcelain” (Qinghuaci青花瓷), the series is composed of several white vases of different shapes and types (“bottle” vase, “plum” vase, “gourd” vase, “pear shaped” vase, “cylinder” vase etc.) , which are carried out using two distinct tools and techniques: for some of them, Shao Yan writes the characters with a brush  while he holds the vase steady with his free hand or he gets help from his assistants (e.g. \"Ruyi\" 如意, \"Feng\" 凤, \"Hai\" 海, \"Ma\" 马, \"Dong nan xi bei si hai ren\" 东南西北四海人, etc. ). For other works, he uses a syringe to inject the blue ink on the vessels that are located on a rotating base. For the entire collection, Shao Yan writes auspicious words carrying a good-luck meaning and he aims to combine the structure of Chinese characters or the lines and marks formed by the ink jet with the shapes of porcelain vases."@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/398.jpg> ;
    ns1:includesArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/396> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/404> a ns3:Q7725310 ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Shao Yan Black and White Ceramics – Calligraphy and Ink Shooting Series (邵岩书法与射墨的百黑瓷器系列)"@en,
        "邵岩书法与射墨的百黑瓷器系列"@zh,
        "Shào Yán shūfǎ yǔ shè mò de bǎi hēi cíqì xìliè"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/277> ;
    ns2:P580 "2022"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/404.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "This series is executed in August 2022 by Shao Yan. The series is composed of several white dishes and vases of different shapes and types (“bottle” vase, “plum” vase, “gourd” vase, “pear shaped” vase, “cylinder” vase etc.), which are carried out using two distinct tools and techniques: for some of them, Shao Yan writes the characters with a brush while he holds the vase steady with his free hand or he gets help from his assistants (\"Shou\" 寿，\"Hai\" 海, \"Qingshan si shi ru hua\" 青山四时如画, etc.). For other works, he uses a syringe to inject the ink on the vessels that are located on a rotating base. For the entire series, he wants to combine the structure of Chinese characters or the lines and marks formed by the ink jet with the shapes of pottery vases. "@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/404.jpg> ;
    ns1:includesArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/402> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/410> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q201662>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q33753>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q345844>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q715162> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1348059>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/410.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Landscape Painting PIC (观音+tags)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit is the first inscription in the center of the scroll. It is written in "big characters" (dazi 大字) and in regular script (kaishu 楷书). It is composed of two traditional Chinese characters, GuanYin 觀音, the Chinese name of the crew. As it is usual in Chinese calligraphic work, they are written vertically (from top to bottom).\r
In the two big characters, the variation of the width of the strokes produced by a skillful use of the spray-painting is a contemporary expedient to create the illusion of being in front of a classical calligraphy written with the ink brush. Furthermore, if we look at the arrangement of this written section, we will notice that it also reproduces a traditional calligraphic pattern: the main text (the two big characters) is in the center of the work, occupying a commanding position, while the inscriptions with the name of the artists are written on the sides in smaller size (even if horizontally and in alphabetic letters).\r
Below the two characters, we can see the tags representing all the members of the crew: Quan, EricTin, Yumi, Apart, Jer, Nato, and Scar on the left; Joey, Keno, Pluto, Viga, Ctn, and Kwanyin on the right. Unlike the two characters "Guan Yin", these tags are written horizontally from left to right in the Latin alphabet, reflecting the Euro-American graffiti tradition. This hybridization of ‘lettering’ and ‘charactering’ is a recurring theme in Kwanyin Clan’s work. It exemplifies the creative fusion of intermixed elements that are both Chinese (vertical Chinese characters) and Western (horizontal Latin script), both traditional (calligraphy) and modern (graffiti tags)."""@en ;
