    ns2:P571 "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "In this artwork Fung Ming Chip made calligraphy by using diluted ink on a landscape background (specifically a background in which he represents a hill with some trees). The image shaped in the artwork is the representation of the text written in the calligraphy, entitled “Landscape B”. The poetic sentiments expressed in this poem are shaped with characters rendered nearly solid in form. Compositionally, the work suggests the fragility and sense of renewal implied by the poem. Fung Ming Chip called this type of script “Black on black Script”, because the black characters are written on a black background."@en ;
