    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/597.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "Born in Pavia on 18th April 1971, living and working in Beijing from 2002 to 2020 and currently based in Bern (Switzerland). He studied Chemistry, History of Art, Experimental Theatre and Film-making. He is as a multimedia and performance artist, director, curator, researcher, writer and lecturer. His work focuses on social intervention and relational dynamics to expand the notion of art practice beyond existing structures, spaces and hierarchies and engage directly with reality in multiple ways.  When he was living in Beijing, he started to practice calligraphy thanks to the acquaintance of his Chinese artist friends and he began to create experimental works inspired by Chinese calligraphy. He is the founder and director of the Social Sensibility R&D Department at Bernard Controls Industries in Beijing (2010-ongoing) and Paris/Gonesse (2016-ongoing) and a founding partner of the Social Sensibility Research Institute (SoSense). His work has been shown in solo, group shows, lectures and presentations all over the world."@en ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Self-Taught"@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/597.jpg> .

