    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Ⅰ (婊子、老处女、绿茶婊、贤妻良母...)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the artwork \"I (Wo 我)\". It consists of the characters written by Wu Xixia inside an inflatable hermetic sphere during the performance that took place in 2020. In this performance, Wu Xixia carries out a reflection on women and herself, writing the labels of society’s goodwill and malice towards women in red paint, such as \"whore\" (biao zi 婊子) \"old maid\" (lao chunu 老处女), \"good wife and loving mother\" (xian qiliang mu 贤妻良母), \"green tea bitch (lucha biao 绿茶婊), \"teenage girl\" (yunu 玉女), \"white lotus\" (bailian hua 白莲花) etc. She answers questions such as: \"Who are women? And who am I? Is my gender determined by birth or is it given by society? There is a womb here, but where is the \"mother\"?\" Having been rejected by her family at the time of her birth as a female, she has been questioning her gender throughout her formative years, and the social labels she writes about are an attempt to reconcile herself with her gender identity."@en ;
