        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q614467> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 324 ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """It is the ninth year of Emperor Mu of Jin's Yonghe era\r
The year of the Yin Water Ox,\r
At the beginning of the third lunar month,\r
We are all gathered at the orchid pavilion in Shanyin County, Guiji Commandery,\r
For the Spring Purification Festival.\r
All of the prominent people have arrived,\r
From old to young.\r
This is an area of high mountains and lofty peaks,\r
With an exuberant growth of trees and bamboos,\r
It also has clear rushing water,\r
Reflecting the sunlight as it flows past either side of the pavilion.\r
The guests are seated side by side to play the drinking game where a wine cup is floated down the stream and the first person sitting in front of the cup when it stops must drink.\r
Although we lack the boisterousness of a live orchestra,\r
With a cup of wine here and a reciting of poetry there, it is sufficient to allow for a pleasant exchange of cordial conversations.\r
Today, the sky is bright and the air is clear,\r
With a gentle breeze that is blowing freely. When looking up, one can see the vastness of the heavens,\r
And when looking down, one can observe the abundance of things. The contentment of allowing one’s eyes to wander,\r
Is enough to reach the heights of delight for the sight and sound. What a joy.\r
Now all people live in this world together,\r
Some will take all of their aspirations, and share them in private with a friend;\r
Still others will abandon themselves to reckless pursuits.\r
Even though everyone makes different choices in life, some thoughtful and some rash,\r
When a person meets with joy, he will temporarily be pleased,\r
And will feel content, but he is not mindful that old age will soon overtake him.\r
Wait until that person becomes weary, or has a change of heart about something,\r
And will thus be filled with regrets.\r
The happiness of the past, in the blink of an eye,\r
Will have already become a distant memory, and this cannot but cause one to sigh;\r
In any case, the length of a man’s life is determined by the Creator, and we will all turn to dust in the end.\r
The ancients have said, "Birth and Death are both momentous occasions."\r
Isn’t that sad!\r
Every time I consider the reasons for why the people of old had regrets,\r
I am always moved to sadness by their writings,\r
And I can not explain why I am saddened.\r
I most certainly know that it is false and absurd to treat life and death as one and the same,\r
And it is equally absurd to think of dying at an old age as being the same as dying at a young age.\r
When future generations look back to my time, it will probably be similar to how I now think of the past.\r
What a shame! Therefore, when I list out the people that were here,\r
And record their musings, even though times and circumstances will change,\r
As for the things that we regret, they are the same.\r
For the people who read this in future generations, perhaps you will likewise be moved by these words."""@en,
        """永和九年，\r
岁在癸丑，\r
暮春之初，\r
会于会稽山阴之兰亭，\r
修禊事也。\r
群贤毕至，\r
少长咸集。\r
此地有崇山峻领，\r
茂林修竹，\r
又有清流激湍，\r
映带左右。\r
引以为流觞曲水，列坐其次；\r
虽无丝竹管弦之盛，\r
一觞一咏，亦足以畅叙幽情。\r
是日也，天朗气清，\r
惠风和畅，仰观宇宙之大，\r
俯察品类之盛，所以游目骋怀，\r
足以极视听之娱，信可乐也。\r
夫人之相与俯仰一世，\r
或取诸怀抱，晤言一室之内；\r
或因寄所托，放浪形骸之外。\r
虽趣舍万殊，静躁不同，\r
当其欣于所遇，暂得于己，\r
快然自足，不知老之将至。\r
及其所之既倦，情随事迁，\r
感慨系之矣。\r
向之所欣，俛仰之间，\r
已为陈迹，犹不能不以之兴怀；\r
况修短随化，终期于尽。\r
古人云﹕「死生亦大矣。」\r
岂不痛哉！\r
每揽昔人兴感之由，\r
若合一契，未尝不临文嗟悼，\r
不能喻之于怀。\r
固知一死生为虚诞，\r
齐彭殇为妄作。\r
后之视今，亦由今之视昔。\r
悲夫！故列叙时人，\r
录其所述，虽世殊事异，\r
所以兴怀，其致一也。\r
后之揽者，亦将有感于斯文。"""@zh,
        """永和九年，\r
歲在癸丑，\r
暮春之初，\r
會于會稽山陰之蘭亭，\r
脩禊事也。\r
群賢畢至，\r
少長咸集。\r
此地有崇山峻領，\r
茂林修竹，\r
又有清流激湍，\r
映帶左右。\r
引以為流觴曲水，列坐其次；\r
雖無絲竹管弦之盛，\r
一觴一詠，亦足以暢敘幽情。\r
是日也，天朗氣清，\r
惠風和暢，仰觀宇宙之大，\r
俯察品類之盛，所以遊目騁懷，\r
足以極視聽之娛，信可樂也。\r
夫人之相與俯仰一世，\r
或取諸懷抱，晤言一室之內；\r
或因寄所托，放浪形骸之外。\r
雖趣舍萬殊，靜躁不同，\r
當其欣于所遇，暫得于己，\r
快然自足，不知老之將至。\r
及其所之既倦，情隨事遷，\r
感慨係之矣。\r
向之所欣，俛仰之間，\r
已為陳迹，猶不能不以之興懷；\r
况修短隨化，終期于盡。\r
古人云﹕「死生亦大矣。」\r
豈不痛哉！\r
每攬昔人興感之由，\r
若合一契，未嘗不臨文嗟悼，\r
不能喻之于懷。\r
固知一死生為虛誕，\r
齊彭殤為妄作。\r
後之視今，亦由今之視昔。\r
悲夫！故列敘時人，\r
錄其所述，雖世殊事異，\r
所以興懷，其致一也。\r
後之攬者，亦將有感於斯文。"""@zh,
        """Yǒnghé jiǔ nián,\r
suì zài guǐ chǒu,\r
mùchūn zhī chū,	\r
huì yú guì jīshān yīn zhī lántíng,	\r
xiū xì shì yě.	\r
Qún xián bì zhì,	\r
shǎo zhǎng xián jí.	\r
Cǐdì yǒu chóng shān jùn lǐng,\r
mào línxiūzhú,\r
yòu yǒu qīngliú jī tuān,\r
yìng dài zuǒyòu.	\r
Yǐn yǐ wéi liúshāng qū shuǐ, liè zuò qícì;	\r
suī wú sīzhú guǎnxián zhī shèng,\r
yī shāng yī yǒng, yì zúyǐ chàngxù yōuqíng.	\r
Shì rì yě, tiān lǎng qì qīng,\r
huìfēng hé chàng, yǎng guān yǔzhòu zhī dà,	\r
fǔchá pǐnlèi zhī shèng, suǒyǐ yóu mù chěng huái,\r
zúyǐ jí shìtīng zhī yú, xìn kělè yě.	\r
Fūrén zhī xiāng yǔ fǔyǎng yīshì,	\r
huò qǔ zhū huáibào, wù yán yī shì zhī nèi;\r
huò yīn jì suǒ tuō, fànglàngxínghái zhī wài.	\r
Suī qù shě wàn shū, jìng zào bùtóng,	\r
dāng qí xīn yú suǒ yù, zàn dé yú jǐ,	\r
kuài rán zìzú, bùzhī lǎo zhī jiàng zhì.	\r
Jí qí suǒ zhī jì juàn, qíng suí shì qiān,	\r
gǎnkǎixìzhī yǐ.	\r
Xiàng zhī suǒ xīn, fǔ yǎng zhī jiān,	\r
yǐ wèi chénjì, yóu bùnéng bù yǐ zhī xìng huái;	\r
kuàng xiū duǎn suí huà, zhōng qī yú jìn.	\r
Gǔrén yún﹕`sǐshēng yì dà yǐ.'\r
Qǐ bù tòng zāi!	\r
Měi lǎn xī rén xìng gǎn zhī yóu,	\r
ruò hé yī qì, wèicháng bù lín wén jiē dào,	\r
bùnéng yù zhī yú huái.	\r
Gù zhī yī sǐshēng wèi xū dàn,\r
qí péng shāng wèi wàng zuò.	\r
Hòu zhī shì jīn, yì yóu jīn zhī shì xī.\r
Bēi fū! Gù liè xù shí rén,	\r
lù qí suǒ shù, suī shì shū shì yì,\r
suǒyǐ xìng huái, qí zhì yī yě.	\r
Hòu zhī lǎn zhě, yì jiāng yǒu gǎn yú sīwén."""@zh-Latn .

