    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/663.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "In \"Music Script, Still Night\", Fung Ming Chip combines calligraphy and music. The characters are transformed but it is still possible to recognize them; although the traditional structure of the columns is not respected, the disposal of the characters is from top to bottom and from right to left. Many strokes are replaced by round dots (which do not belong to the category of strokes used in Chinese writing to compose characters) which recall the form of musical notes. Fung Ming Chip realizes this calligraphy while the music resonates in the air, letting himself be inspired by it. The artwork is harmonious and rhythmic, because it precisely follows the rhythm of the music that inspired it."@en ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
