    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42519> ;
    ns2:P571 "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "This long vertical calligraphy is an example of work in which Fung Ming Chip plays with different dilutions of ink in water, creating stratified effects. The \"script type\" he creates in this work is \"rubbing script\" (ta zi 拓字) that reproduces the effect of rubbing tehnique. The artist wrote the characters on xuan paper with water and put the piece of paper into a pool of ink. The traces of writing instantly revealed themselves. The sentence quoted by Fung Ming Chip is \"我有我在, 息神无奈\", whose meaning is \"I am who I am, Change me no one can\"."@en ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850>,
