    ns1:description "\"Raindrop Script, Heart Sutra\" was created in 2012 by the artist Fung Ming Chip. The source of inspiration is a scene of everyday life: the raindrops falling on the glass of a car. In this artwork, in fact, the artist tried to recreate raindrops on paper: he firstly used a brush full of ink on a plastic sheet, creating droplets on its non-absorbent surface. Then, using a dry brush and the ink droplets left on the plastic sheet, he wrote some lines from the Heart Sutra. Finally, he positioned a sheet of rice paper on the written plastic sheet, transferring the traced content from the plastic to the paper."@en ;
