    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Female Character Writing in a Patriarchal Society (妎、妇、妄、婪...)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the performance \"Female Character Writing in a Patriarchal Society (Fuxi shehui de nu zi shuxie 父系社会的女字书写)\". It consists of some big traditional characters of the famous Chinese dictionary named \"Shuowen Jiezi 说文解字\" realized by Xu Shen (c. 58 – c. 148 CE). These characters are accompained with their explanations written in smaller size. These big characters with female radical have all a negative meaning, for example: \"hai 妎\" (jealous/demanding); \"fu 妇\" (woman/wife); \"wang 妄\" (presumptuous/rash); \"lan 婪\" (be greedy); \"fang 妨\" (harm), \"hun 婚\" (married), \"yin 婬\" (lascivious/licentious); \"ning 佞\" (sycophant/toady); \"du 妒\" (jealous/envy); \"qu 娶\" (take a wife); \"wei 委\" (throw away/cast aside); \"zi 姊\" (older sister) etc. Characters are realized with white ink on a black wall in regular script. In addition, they are realized in non-simplified form and from top to bottom and from right to left, recalling ancient scriptures. In China female discrimination has a very ancient origin. It starts from writing and, consequently, from calligraphy, an artistic practice exclusive to male in China."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
