    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/751.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU VR - Wandering Beyond (《庄子—逍遥游》)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU features the illegible text inscribed by Wang Dongling in the creation of the artwork \"VR – Wandering Beyond\". It is based on a sentence of 14 Chinese characters—\"野马也,尘埃也,生物之以息相吹也\" (Wild stallions, wandering dust, the breath of beings intertwined in the wind)—from the first chapter of the \"Zhuangzi\" entitled \"Wandering Beyond\" (Xiaoyao you 逍遥游). This chapter explores themes of spontaneity, relativism, and the nature of reality. It begins with the tale of Kun, a giant fish that transforms into Peng, an immense bird capable of soaring to extraordinary heights and traveling vast distances—far beyond human reach. This transformation symbolizes the boundless potential of nature and the vastness of the universe, contrasting with the limitations of human existence. Wang Dongling’s calligraphic virtual signs transcend reality through a continuous series of transformations, reflecting Zhuangzi’s philosophy. His art embraces the natural flow of change, rejecting rigid structures in favor of spontaneity and fluidity."@en ;
    ns1:directionality "Free" ;
