    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Shanghai be strong (上海坚强)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of four characters (Shanghai jianqiang 上海坚强).  The first two characters \"上海\" (Shanghai) were painted by Huri in running script (xingshu 行书). The other two characters jianqiang \"坚强\" (fortify, be strong) were painted by Storm (French writer) in regular script (kaishu 楷书). Because of their uniform thickness, maybe painted using a pasting brush or a paint roller, the \"jianqiang 坚强\" characters might also call to mind the great seal script (dazhuanshu 大篆书). Both parts have a thin black outline that grants a tridimensional effect. "@en ;
