    ns1:numberOfCharacters 21 ;
    ns1:relatedUnit <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/92> ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """Afar a row of wild geese fly, \r
Weaving a letter in the sky. \r
What have I done in days gone by? \r
Gazing from the balustrade, \r
Could I weave my way as far as they?\r
(Translator: Xu Yuanchong)\r
"""@en,
        """天际征鸿，\r
遥认行如缀。\r
平生事，\r
此时凝睇，\r
谁会凭栏意。\r
"""@zh,
        """Tiānjì zhēng hóng, \r
yáo rèn háng rú zhuì. \r
Píngshēng shì, \r
cǐ shí níng dì, \r
shéi huì pínglán yì."""@zh-Latn .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/952> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4970> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Drinking on West Lake First Shine After the Rain  (饮湖上初晴后雨)"@en,
        "饮湖上初晴后雨"@zh,
        "Yǐn húshàng chū qíng hòu yǔ"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4115079> ;
    ns2:P2048 "15 m" ;
    ns2:P2049 "33 m" ;
    ns2:P287 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/748> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "2015-01-05"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.inkstudio.com.cn/news/14-event-wang-dongling-calligraphic-artwork-to-commemorate/> ;
    ns2:P88 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q312> ;
    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36020> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/952.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """In January 5, 2015  Wang Dongling  collaborated with Apple to realize this huge calligraphic work for the opening of the Apple Store in Hangzhou near West Lake. The artwork represents a relevant example of the use of calligraphy for commercial purposes. The huge painting covers the exterior façade of the first and largest-in-Asia Apple retail store. In the white space around the red iconic Apple logo, the artist wrote the poem entitled "Drinking on West Lake first shine after the rain" by Su Shi 苏轼 (1037-1101), better known as Su Dongpo 苏东坡, an eminent poet of the Song dynasty (960-1279). The content of the poem praises the rich history of art and culture of the city of Hangzhou. Wang Dongling realized the draft of the work in a lower scale, using brush and ink on paper. This original calligraphic artwork was used as a model to realize the wall adornment of the Apple Store, incorporating the Apple logo in the middle. \r
In this work, Chinese calligraphy highlights the essence of traditional culture,  linked to poetry, literature and art; while the Apple logo embodies an American contemporary commercial empire, based on scientific and technological innovation. The fusion between the calligraphic inscription and the commercial logo shows the successful attempt by Wang Dongling and Apple to integrate technology, culture and modern cross-border trade exchanges in today's Cina. In this occasion, the black Apple logo changed to a vivid red to recall a Chinese traditional seal. The reason of this change is the intention to make the ultra-modern commercial products of the foreign brand more attractive to Chinese consumers. In the commercial video, Wang Dongling expresses his happyness "to reach many people by showing them the power of Chinese ideograms" (from Ink Studio website).  According to Wang, the poem was the most suitable to praise the essence of ancient Chinese culture of the city of Hangzhou.\r
After Wang Dongling's contribution, other traditional Chinese arts have been used as the subject of Apple's advertising campaigns in China. """@en ;
    ns1:hasChineseConcept <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/chinese_red> ;
    ns1:hasChineseVisualElement <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/seal> ;
