        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8686> ;
    ns1:description "Zheng Shengtian is an artist, scholar and curator. He is one of the founders and chief curators of the academic journal \"Yishu: Journal of Contemporary Chinese Art\". Zheng Shengtian is also director of the Asian Pavilion of the Vancouver Art Gallery, director of the Asian Art Archive in America. He was the director of the Oil Painting Department of Zhejiang Academy of Fine Arts. After moving to Canada in 1990, he served as President of the Vancouver Chinese Artists Association, Secretary General of the Leung Kit Wah Art Foundation (Liang Jie Hua Yishu Jixinhui 梁洁华艺术基金会) founded in Vancouver in 1997, and Founding Director of the Vancouver International Centre for Contemporary Asian Art . He has curated important exhibitions such as \"Shanghai Modern\", \"Art and Chinese Revolution\", \"The Wind Rises in Fusang\", as well as the Shanghai and Vancouver Biennales."@en ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Not present"@en ;
