    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q378564> ;
    ns1:description """This visual artwork was realized by Chen Guangwu in 2004 and exhibited on several occasions, such as at the "Boundary of Freedom - Chinese Contemporary Ink towards Europe" (Ziyou de chidu - Zhongguo dangdai shuimo zouxiang Ouzhou 自由的尺度”第五回——中国当代水墨走向欧洲) exhibition held at Ca' dei Carraresi, Treviso, in 2018. \r
“Facsimile Wang Xizhi”  exemplifies Chen Guangwu's commitment to emulating the fluidity and continuity of Chinese characters, conveying them as "visual poetry". By maintaining a continuous line throughout the composition, he captures the essence of Chinese script, which is often perceived as both artistic and poetic. By prioritizing aesthetics over semantics, Chen Guangwu elevates the beauty and form of the characters, therefore he praises the beauty and form of the characters, transcending their literal meaning. Chen Guangwu's dedication to replicate and reinterpret the style and essence (fluidity, rhythm, and grace) of Wang Xizhi's calligraphy  within a contemporary context. """@en ;
