    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1115> ;
    ns2:P941 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/96> ;
    ns1:description "Preface to the Poems Composed at the Orchid Pavilion was realized by Chen Guangwu in 2008. This artwork provides an example of his interactive piece made of a disassemblable and reassemblable puzzle consisting of 2700 wooden blocks, onto which Chen transcribed the the most undisputed classic in the history of Chinese calligraphy,  the 'Preface to the Orchid Pavilion Gathering', written by Wang Xizhi in 353. This reinvention and reinterpretation  in a modern context of Wang Xizhi's famous piece transforms the artwork into an interactive game that captivates the audience, notably the Western audience (as the exhibition is held in Berlin). It serves as an introduction to the contemplation and manipulation of the calligraphic line, challenging viewers to reconstruct its unity without prior knowledge of the underlying meaning or the writing that inspired it (Iezzi 2014, p. 440)."@en ;
