    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/116.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Luo Qi and Collegium Musicum Almae Matris - Musicalligraphy Performance (signs)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is an original transcription of the Italian opera arias played by the Collegium Musicum Almae Matris written by Luo Qi using the Dunhuang musical score system (Dunhuang qupu 敦煌曲谱).  This ancient music notation system consists of 20 tablature-signs, which represent the tablature notations for the four-stringed Tang dynasty pipa (Chinese lute), indicating finger positions and their corresponding pitches. These symbols are simple characters (six are Chinese numerals), radicals or character components/parts. The text is composed of a series of signs derived from the Dunhuang musical score system."@en ;
