    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Broken Celadon (观音)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is the elaborate wildstyle charactering \"GuanYin  观音\" inside the ceramic vase glazed in jade green celadon color placed in the center of the composition. The explosive force of this elaborate wildstyle charactering pushes onto the thin walls of the vase and disintegrates it, representing the forces of modernity  - embodied by the Kwanyin Clan - that break and overcomes tradition. The vase recalls the Jun-type celadons made in China during the Song Dynasty (960 - 1279), considered one of the finest forms of Chinese art. "@en ;
