<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1178> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P144 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/911> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1150070> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1348059>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3055935> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1860>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/running_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1178.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 3 Broken Celadon (泮林革音 + seal)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit is a vertical calligraphic inscription in the lower right-hand corner of the composition. It is a chengyu written in running style (xingshu 行书) and it originates from "Pan shui 泮水" a poem from "The Book of Songs" (Shijing 诗经), China's earliest anthology of poetry. "Pan shui 泮水" is a long narrative poem that extols the military achievements of Duke Xi of Lu in pacifying the Huaiyi tribes. It praises his ability to carry on his ancestors' legacy, subdue the Huaiyi, and accomplish military feats. The poem is composed of eight chapters, each containing eight lines. \r
The chengyu "panlingeyin 泮林革音" affirms that "when we receive positive influences, we can change our old habits" , that seems to be an artistic admonishment made by the crew. The content of the vase represents the real nature of the Kwanyin Clan's art (graffiti), while the traditional art is only its cover (the glaze of the vase): when the power of graffiti smashes that cover, the traditional influences will be transformed into modern art. \r
As usual in traditional calligraphy, next to the calligraphic inscription there is a seal with the name of the crew (KWAN YIN), but opposite to the traditional canons, the seal is in Latin letters and not in archaic characters.  """@en ;
