    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 3 Olympic Beijing (观音)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is written in \"big characters\" (dazi 大字) and in regular-running script (xingkai 行楷). This CWU is composed of only two traditional Chinese characters \"Guan Yin 觀音\", the Chinese name of the crew, that are written vertically (from top to bottom), as usual in Chinese calligraphic works. In the two big characters, the variation of the width of the strokes produced by a skillful use of the spray-painting is a contemporary expedient to create the illusion of being in front of a classical calligraphy written with the ink brush. It is very significant that around the characters there are bamboo and mist, as in the Chinese painting tradition."@en ;
