    ns1:description "The artwork \"Tuo qi xiwang 托起希望 (Raising Hope)\" was made in 2009 in memory of the Sichuan earthquake of 12 May 2008, which claimed approximately seventy thousand victims. The piece is a wild style renderings of the four characters of the title inspired by a chengyu (four-character idiom) that means \"Raising Hope\". The writing style is very edgy and basic, consisting of one or two fill-in colors spread evenly, a single outline, and only occasionally a hint of 3D. The result is somewhat “rigid” and reveals the embryonic state of the ANDC personal stylistic research, centered on the attempt to reshape Chinese writing by imitating American styles."@en ;
