    ns1:description """Alongside a long career as a jazz performer that began in 1982, at the end of the 1990s he began to write and publish classical music compositions. Over 70 recordings see him alongside musicians such as Tony Scott and Paul Bley. He has created around forty soundtracks and theme songs for theatre, short films, cinema and TV, working with many directors including Soldini, Migliarotti and Margherito.\r
For Tutù (by Giacomo Mondadori) he won the award for best soundtrack at the OZU festival; Lino Sabbattini, wins as best film on art at the Asolo Festival and Ainom (Garofalo/Ceva Valla) wins at the Chinese Oscars. But perhaps the most prestigious recognition he obtained was in 1996 thanks to Mario Monicelli who awarded the short film "La Donna della Sua Vita" by Daniela Franco, with his soundtrack.\r
His jazz version of Vivaldi's Four Seasons is included in the 100th issue of the magazine "Suonare News" and wins the Golden Grain of Rice. For many years he has been under exclusive contract with the prestigious publisher Curci, now in its 150th year of activity. In 2011 he created the project "La Strada della Musica" with the ROM orchestra for the Milan Conservatory. His “The flute connection”, a CD where performers such as M. Simeoli, B. Grossi, F. Loi play his compositions, is included in the specialist flute magazine FALAUT.The documentary with his music "O'Mast" again by Migliarotti is screened in London,  New York and Hong Kong; composes and arranges music for LOVE IN SPACE a film (China-HongKong) distributed by FOX also in the USA with Asian stars Angela Baby, Eason Chan and Aaron Kwok\r
In 2013 the Strehler of Milan dedicated him a great celebration for his 30 years of career. The Roma Project becomes Orchestra dei Popoli, opening up to other ethnic groups and counting on the collaboration of guests such as Franco Battiato, in a social opening program desired by the Conservatory and the municipality of Milan who still entrust him with direction and arrangements.\r
In the world of song he has the opportunity to work as an arranger, among others, with Lucio Dalla, Roberto Vecchioni, M. LoCasciulli and Platinette. With Curci he published the abridged version in 4 volumes of "his" 4 Seasons of Vivaldi, 8 volumes on Astor Piazzolla "Easy Piazzolla" and numerous classical pieces for various ensembles. Leonardo Syndrome by M. Margerito with its soundtrack is selected for EXPOO 2015.In 2016 he created a special library for Finale, the most used musical notation program. Cited in various musical books (Diz. del Jazz by A. Mazzoletti, Umbria Jazz a sea of faces, Il Fluto jazz by S, Benini, Il Saxofono ed. Zecchini, etc) He is in the selection of 24 flautists from all over the world of the FALAUT Festival. In 2017 he presented the new project La Mia Napoli with the Musica Oggi orchestra at the Strehler. In the summer he received a prestigious artistic direction at the La Verdi Auditorium: he  carried out a project he had conceived There was many times in Jazz which in 6 concerts accompanies the audience to delve into the music that characterized almost his entire life. On 16 December, again at the La  Auditorium, with the Symphony Orchestra directed by him, with original compositions and very personal arrangements of the Neapolitan song, he celebrates his 35-year career Secondo me, Napoli with Antonio Lubrano. In 2018 he resumed the historic duo Ampio Respiro with Daniela Panetta, working on the documentary About a war, on the war in Lebanon (UK production) released in cinemas in London on 28 November. He wrote the music for the short film by Michael Degani and Alessia Rotondo Who is Jerry Adams, and he himself conducted the LaVerdi Symphony Orchestra in the recording of the soundtrack. The film will be released in 2020. He was entrusted with the concert-event for the tenth anniversary of the LaVerdi Youth Orchestra (92 elements aged 8 to 20): Strong? Very strong! documents the concert and preparation for Il Manifesto against child labor (UN project) from which the DVD/CD C'era Numero Volte il Natale will be born in 2019, also available on all digital platforms. On 4 July of the same year he created a new concert event dedicated to the 50th anniversary of the moon landing entitled Houston we have a... concert writing and conducting the LaVerdi Symphony Orchestra again with the voice of Daniela Panetta and the extraordinary participation of the scientist Amalia Ercoli Finzi; during the concert Luca Santaniello performs the world premiere of a movement of his violin concerto Trip to the Moon. In 2021 he created 20 new variations on the theme of Madness for the guitar of the great concert pianist Giulio Tampalini published by Curci in 2022. In 2021 he created a series of broadcasts on Cinema and Music for Swiss Radio.In 2021 Event for the 100th anniversary of the birth of Astor Piazzolla There was 100 times Astor with the Who is Jerry Adams, (M. Degani and A. Rotondo soundtrack with the Sinfonica de LaVerdi in 2020 wins two awards for best soundtrack: Locarno and Los Angeles International Film Festival.\r
In 2022, for his 40 years of career, he published a volume with two of his treatises with Curci Milano editions: "A new approach to wind instruments writing", a revolutionary concept on wind writing and "Base-7 symmetries in the musical writing system". With a great Christmas event he celebrates his career in a concert with the Milan Symphony Orchestra, children's choir and mixed choir, vocal trio. A staff of 120 members who received enormous public response. In 2023 he is on stage at the Noh Ma Theater with the actress Iaia Forte in a show by Mimmo di Marzio Principessa.""" ;
