    ns1:description """This piece is part of a set of five armchairs by Minaxdo, titled “Yuanyuan Chairs” (Yuanyuan yi 缘圆椅). It is conceived as an individual expression within the broader Yuanyuan Chairs series, embodying the principles of Chinese calligraphy through a singular, self-contained form. Its design translates the movements of the brush — turns, hooks, inclinations, and directional flow — into a continuous structural gesture, where each curve and transition contributes to a sense of controlled fluidity.\r
Rooted in the essence of traditional calligraphy, the armchair presents smooth, restrained lines that evoke the rhythmic balance of running and semi-cursive script. This visual softness is counterbalanced by an inner strength, reflecting the classical notion of fenggu 风骨 — a quiet but resolute structural integrity beneath an elegant surface.\r
The chair’s silhouette recalls a spontaneous semi-cursive composition, yet its construction adheres rigorously to mechanical and ergonomic principles. Handcrafted mortise-and-tenon joints punctuate the form like intentional pauses in brush movement, anchoring the design while preserving its sense of motion.\r
Named “Yuanyuan” (缘圆), meaning “round-perfect edge” or “harmonious connection,” the armchair expresses continuity and balance through its ergonomically shaped teak and rosewood armrests. Drawing inspiration from the Ming-style backed armchair, the Yuanyuan Armchair – Ease achieves a poised equilibrium between dignified proportion, comfort, and the enduring spirit of Chinese literati aesthetics."""@en ;
