    ns1:description "This work was exhibited during the \"First Exhibition of Chinese Modern Calligraphy\" that was held in 1985 at the National Art Museum of China. Su Yuanzhang uses calligraphic forms to mimic the forms of landscape paintings. The name of the work comes from the final two lines of a famous poem by Li Bai entitled \"Zao fa bai di cheng\"早发白帝城 (Through the Yangze River), whose characters make up the landscape. "@en ;
