    ns1:attributedTitle """CWU 1 Women's Writing: A Blank Page (女书)\r
""" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of the text written in one of the four components of Cai Mengxia’s installation "Women's Writing: A Blank Page" (Nüshu: Kongbai zhi ye 女书——空白之页), and specifically on the top right panel. It is inscribed with text in Women's Writing (nǚshū 女书), a unique form of calligraphy historically used exclusively by ethnic Yao women. Originating from the Jiangyong area in Hunan Province, Nǚshū was developed as a secretive script allowing women a private means of communication. In her artwork, Cai Mengxia highlights this localized and gender-specific script to underscore its significance as a medium of expression solely for women. By incorporating Nǚshū into her installation, she not only acknowledges its cultural and historical importance but also elevates its status within the broader discourse of women's writing and artistic expression.\r
It is important to notice that Nüshu became a national-level ICH of China when 'Nüshu Custom' was included in China's National Representative List of Intangible Cultural Heritage in 2006.""" ;
