    ns1:description """ "Godbird Series" (Shenniao xilie 神鸟系列) is one of the three interrelated series of artworks  realized by Luo Qi between 2005 and 2009 , together with the "Godfish Series" (Shenyu xilie 神鱼系列) and the "Flying Fish Series" (Feiyu xilie 飞鱼系列). The works, realized in ink and color on paper, explore a creative reinterpretation of the ancient Chinese characters for "bird" (niao 鸟) and "fish" (yu 鱼).  Each series demonstrates a pictographic return, with a move from rigid adherence to the original character forms to a more fluid and creative interpretation. In the artworks of these three series, Luo Qi emphasizes the visual structure and transformation of the characters. He manipulates the symbols freely, creating diverse representations of "birds" and "fish" that challenge traditional artistic conventions and explore new visual languages. In the first artworks of these series, the analogy with the pictographic forms of the related character is very strong, but then it becomes increasingly tenuous in favour of a greater resemblance to the real images of birds and fish or to their conventional way of being drawn. In the last examples, they turn into compositions of lines that only vaguely recall the shapes of birds and fishes.\r
Therefore, Luo Qi uses the idea of "combinatorial and asymmetric modularity", where variations and irregularities become key principles of creativity, together with a fusion between different levels of representation, such as the archaic forms of the characters, the stylized drawings of real images, the linear abstraction, and the rework of conventional elements.   \r
\r
""" ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/1406_HR.png> ;
