    ns2:P571 "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1407.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "\"Godbird 07-30\" is one of the works included in the \"Godbird Series\" (Shenniao xilie 神鸟系列). In the works of this series, Luo Qi reinterpreted the ancient Chinese character \"bird\" (niao 鸟) , preserving and elaborating  its original shapes to the greatest extent. In \"Godbird 07-30\", there is no longer a strong analogy with the pictographic forms of the related character, and the compositions of lines only faintly suggest the shapes of a bird.  In this work and similarly in all the works of the series, Luo Qi created a childish, archaic drawing writing, in which the characters have been heavily reshaped and contaminated with simple figurative elements. For example, the beak is rendered in red, reminiscent of a seal impression, while green is used for the bird's plumage. This coloration gives the bird an almost fish-like form, evoking connections to the \"Flying Fish Series\" by the same artist. This non-formalized 'writing' is no longer linguistically readable, but visually appreciable, opening itself to universal aesthetic enjoyment. " ;
