    ns1:description "Hua Jun, born in Jiangsu 1970.  He graduated from the China Academy of Art in 1994. He moved to Sweden in 1995, obtaining a Master’s degree from the Royal Swedish Academy of Fine Arts in 2002, and taught Chinese calligraphy at Stockholm University and Royal Academy of Fine Arts in Sweden.  He returned to China in 2006, where he  pursued his PhD at the China Academy of Art (CAA) under the supervision of  Professor Wang Dongling. He is currently professor at China Academy of Art and Deputy Director of the Department of Chinese Painting. Hua Jun works in the field of contemporary Chinese art, whose work spans multiple artistic disciplines, including ink painting, calligraphy. He is also actively engaged in performance art, installation art, photography, printmaking, and design." ;
