<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1462> a ns3:Q184485 ;
    ns2:P1132 1 ;
    ns2:P1476 "The Story of the Mirror (镜子的故事)"@en,
        "镜子的故事"@zh,
        "Jìngzi de gùshì"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P175 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/698> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q378564>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7252>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81938> ;
    ns2:P186 ns3:Q127418,
        ns3:Q171495,
        ns3:Q283,
        ns3:Q618710 ;
    ns2:P2047 "PT30M"^^xsd:duration ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1741> ;
    ns2:P585 "2023-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1767> ;
    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q10871612>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q378564> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1462.jpg> ;
    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/698> ;
    ns1:description "The performance takes place in three different moments. 1) In a room furnished with an old mattress and red gauze, Li Xinmo begins to use red ink (cinnabar ink) to write characters related to pain on the gauze and after on the mattress. These characters are words and poetic verses from Chinese calligraphic tradition and in particular related to the famous calligrapher Wang Xizhi, such as: “Pain penetrates the heart and liver, pain should be helpless” (Tong guan xingan, tong dang naihe 痛贯心肝、痛当奈何), a verse contained in “Letter of Distress and Indignation” (Sangluan tie 丧乱贴)   and “sadness and pain are destroyed” (aitong cui bo 哀痛摧剥) a verse from “Deploring the Death of My Aunt” (Yimu tie 姨母帖).  2) In a second moment, after having sprinkled the mattress with red balloons filled with water (symbol of female ovaries) she begins to break them flooding everything with water. 3) Finally, the artist takes a mirror, breaks it and begins to put pieces of broken glass in her mouth, whispering some moans and words. She is unable to speak clearly, as the pieces of glass could cut her. In this performance, the artist uses key elements that lead her back to the excursus of suffering endured by women who receive sexual abuse: first the pain expressed through calligraphy (symbol of patriarchal power), then the loss of femininity through the symbolic breaking of the ovaries that, by breaking, flood everything “soft” and “comfortable” (like the mattress) that life can offer. Finally, her reflection in the mirror breaks into a thousand pieces, filling her mouth and preventing her from speaking. What comes out is only a silent scream and a few barely audible whispers."@en ;
