        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P19 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1038564> ;
    ns2:P21 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6581097> ;
    ns2:P2561 "Zeit 時間 " ;
    ns2:P27 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148> ;
    ns2:P361 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1494> ;
    ns2:P569 "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1650> ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.instagram.com/z51tiez/> ;
    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q16572> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1507.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """Zeit 時間 is a graffiti artist, in his thirties, whose work is deeply intertwined with themes of time and cultural identity. He uses the tags "時間" (the Chinese character for "time," shijian 时间 in Mandarin) and "zeit" (the German word for "time"). He initially adopted these aliases to obscure his identity when he began his graffiti journey abroad in 2009. His artistic evolution was sparked by his discovery of graffiti through the influential book Spraycan Art during his studies overseas.\r
Currently residing in southern China, Zeit 時間 is engaged with the global graffiti scene and is affiliated with several graffiti crews, including FEK, 2G, STH, and YP. \r
His practice primarily involves the use of spray paint, roller paint, and ink, blending traditional graffiti techniques with influences from Chinese calligraphy—a skill he developed during his childhood. This background in calligraphy significantly shapes his artistic approach, allowing him to explore the dynamic interaction between form, movement, and expression.\r
Zeit 時間's primary goal in creating graffiti is to engage in what he terms "public vandalism" or "art vandalism," aiming to make art accessible to a broader audience. He advocates for artistic disruption that brings creativity directly to the streets, challenging conventional boundaries of art presentation.\r
While acknowledging that the graffiti scene in China is still in its early stages compared to other regions, Zeit 時間 sees the use of Chinese characters as a powerful tool for creating distinctive, culturally integrated graffiti. He believes that Chinese graffiti can incorporate traditional decorative elements and ethnic patterns, setting it apart from Western styles. Although the complexity of Chinese characters may sometimes pose challenges in terms of legibility, he views this as an opportunity for innovation and growth within the graffiti movement.\r
Zeit 時間 is part of a new wave of Chinese graffiti artists contributing to the development of this emerging culture. He collaborates with notable teammates like Donis, Asko, and Wreck, as well as Chinese artists such as 气 (Qi) and 灵丹 (Lingdan), each playing a crucial role in shaping the future of graffiti in China."""@en ;
