    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU Music and Calligraphy (水、止、木、目)" ;
    ns1:description "The characters, which are broken down and created with a pen, are inspired by the inscriptions on oracle bones. These characters are: shui 水 (water) zhi 止 (to/only) mu 木 (wood) and mu 目 (eye). Animal figures can also be glimpsed in the work, such as deer heads. The lines that make up the draft can be both vertical and horizontal, as if to reproduce the movements of the elements of nature."@en ;
