    ns2:P571 "2008-01-13"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/860> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork by Pu Lieping was created during a musical performance held at the Florida Gulf Coast University. Three guitarists, students at the university, performed music by George Gershwin and Edward Rizzo. In response to the music, Pu Lieping painted directly onto a long scroll of paper using brushes of varying sizes dipped in black ink. The resulting calligraphic lines, fine and vibrant, seem to visually echo the rhythm and flow of the music, as though composing a parallel visual score. The artwork becomes a synesthetic dialogue between sound and image, where ink moves to the beat of melody and harmony.\r
This work visually incorporates elements developed in a preparatory sketch made the day before the performance, on January 12. That initial draft, drawn in pen on a piece of Polo Ralph Lauren wrapping paper, featured deconstructed Chinese characters inspired by oracle bone script: shui 水 (water); zhi 止 (to/only); mu 木 (wood) and mu 目 (eye).\r
These characters were reinterpreted and reproduced within the live performance artwork, embedded into the composition as visual and symbolic anchors. Also present are suggestive animal figures—such as deer heads—and gestural lines arranged both vertically and horizontally, evoking the fluid, elemental motion of nature. The work thus becomes a synthesis of musical energy, ancient writing, and natural imagery.""" ;
