    ns2:P571 "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1265> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is realized during the performance “Cursive/Wild Grass”. It was held on 25 February 2006 at the Vision Festival of New York. The performer is Yin Mei herself, accompanied by the music realized by the American jazz multi-instrumentalist Joe McPhee (b. 1939). Yin Mei is dressed in black and is lying on a white paper sheet. She starts to move, snaking and rolling around on the paper. In a second step, she drenches her body in ink, starting to move as before but leaving traces of ink on the paper through her body movements. With her hands and feet, she performs circular and spiral movements, creating both linear and spotty smears of ink, becoming a calligraphic brush. The performance unfolds as a meditative act, where movement, ink, and paper merge in a contemplative expression of bodily calligraphy."@en ;
