    ns1:description "In this demonstrative performance, Wu Wei uses a big dried brush to \"caress\" a naked woman body. In contrast to traditional calligraphy, he doesn't use ink and paper to write characters. The artist makes a critique at the \"conforting pleasantness\" of the traditional Chinese art: the traditional culture is embodied by the brush, which produces a softing and conforting pleasantness on the skin. Through the ostentation of the body and the use of  the brush as a \"tool of pleasure\", Wu Wei wants to provoke a state of shock in order to shake the viewer from the social and existential torpor in which he lives. According to Wu Wei,  Chinese art is still strongly anchored to old styles and traditional tools and methods, so the artist is not free to express himself. The only way to break with the tradition is to overturn traditional tools and methods in a  \"sensual/sexual\" provocative way. "@en ;
