        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1690.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 X-Evolution (X-planned)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is composed of an X combined with a red “TT” seal, which together form the tag “TxT”. The large black X, accompanied by the small red “TT” seal, is set against a yellow background.\r
The X loosely evokes the visual qualities of regular script (kaishu), especially in its straight, upright strokes and relatively controlled structure. Its symmetrical, compact configuration gives the character a stable and somewhat rigid appearance, while the sharp intersections of the strokes introduce a distinctly contemporary, graphic quality. The juxtaposition of the black X with the red seal further recalls the traditional relationship between black calligraphic writing and red seals in Chinese calligraphy, reinterpreted here within the visual vocabulary of graffiti and characteristic of the Straight/Roller style."""@en ;
