<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1739> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns2:P10661 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1285> ;
    ns2:P1476 "DA KAI TONG - Exhibition of Zhang Aiguo (大开通——张爱国书法作品展)"@en,
        "大开通——张爱国书法作品展"@zh,
        "Dà kāitōng——Zhāng Aiguó shūfǎ zuòpǐn zhǎn"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P1640 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1740>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1741> ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q15174> ;
    ns2:P580 "2022-08-30"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2022-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """"Da Kai Tong - Exhibition of Zhang Aiguo Calligraphy" is the title of two exhibitions of artworks by Zhang Aiguo. The first exhibition was held at the Guan Shanyue Art Museum in Shenzhen from August 30 to October 7, 2022. The second exhibition took place at the Shenzhen University Museum from March 10 to 23, 2023. Both exhibitions were curated by Lu Dadong and Cao Yingwang.\r
The meaning of "Da Kai Tong" is "The Great Passage" and refers to an inscription found in a rock carving from the year 63 AD (the sixth year of the Yongping era of the Han dynasty), formally known as "The Rock Inscription of the Opening of the Baoxie Pass by Governor Chu of the Han Dynasty" (Han Chu jun kai tong Banxie dao keshi 汉鄐君开通褒斜道刻石). This inscription is renowned for blending characteristics of two distinct calligraphic styles: the clerical script (lishu) and the seal script (zhuanshu). It is currently preserved in the Hanzhong Museum in Shaanxi Province.\r
""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1736> .

