    ns2:P571 "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.xubing.com/en/work/details/231?year=1999&type=year#231> ;
    ns1:description """This work was realized by Xu Bing in 2002 and belongs to the series 'Landscript' ( Wenzi xiesheng 文字写生, 1999-2013) .  The artworks of this series are also known as 'Read View' (Du fengjing 读风景). The artist uses Chinese pictographic as pictorial elements to arrange a landscape composition: the characters for 'stone' (shi 石) make up images of rocks, the character for 'tree' (mu 木) makes up trees, for 'clouds' (yun 云) clouds, and so on. In this way, Xu Bing transforms visual images of landscapes into linguistic forms and proposes an original approach to 'read a scene'.  \r
In this particular work, the pictographic characters are rendered in a dynamic black ink style and arranged into a traditional Chinese landscape painting (shanshui 山水). The composition presents a river winding through the scene, bordered by rocks and trees along its banks. In the background, hills and mountains rise above the river with forested areas and cultivated fields. """ ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q191163>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
