    ns1:description "This monumental calligraphy was commissioned to Tong Yang-tze  by M+ of Hong Kong in 2020 for the opening of the museum. It was displayed in the Main Hall of the museum together with other four calligraphies by Tong Yang-tze all inspired by the I Ching (Yijing 易经, Book of Changes), an ancient Chinese philosophical text. The title of the artwork, that corresponds to the transcription of its calligraphic text, is in fact a phrase from I Ching selected by the calligrapher. Also the contents of the other 4 calligraphies of this group are phrases from the I Ching. All of them reveal the dynamic between humans, nature and cosmic order and are the artist’s reflection on how ancient wisdom applies to the modern world. " ;
