<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1917> a ns3:Q7725634 ;
    ns2:P1476 "One-Hearted (相思)" ;
    ns2:P1480 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5727902> ;
    ns2:P50 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q313605> ;
    ns2:P571 "0735"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "“One-Hearted” (Xiang Si, 相思) is a brief poem by Wang Wei (王维, 699–761) of the Tang Dynasty (618–907). Although the exact date of its composition is uncertain, it was possibly written in the middle of the 8th century, during the Kaiyuan era (713–741) or the early Tianbao era (742–756). Structurally, the poem is a five-character quatrain, also called jueju (wu yan jueju 五言绝句), consisting of four lines of five characters each, for a total of 20 characters. In this poem, Wang Wei uses red beans as an evocative symbol to express deep longing and affection, highlighting the enduring power of love and remembrance." ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """When those red berries come in springtime,\r
flushing on your southland branches,\r
take home an armful, for my sake,\r
as a symbol of our love.\r
(translation by Witter Bynner )"""@zh,
        """紅豆生南國﹐春來發幾枝。\r
願君多採擷﹐此物最相思。"""@zh,
        """红豆生南国，春来发几枝。\r
愿君多采摄，此物最相思。"""@zh,
        """Hóngdòu shēng nánguó, chūnlái fā jǐ zhī.\r
Yuàn jūn duō cǎi shè, cǐ wù zuì xiāngsī."""@zh-Latn .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1945> a ns3:Q4502142 ;
