        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q911285> ;
    ns2:P2048 "240 cm " ;
    ns2:P2049 """840 cm\r
""" ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1032> ;
    ns1:description "\"Magnified Calligraphy 07909\"  explores the intersection of tradition and abstraction, focusing on the essence of Chinese calligraphy. The artist selects a character from an ancient calligrapher, cutting away its four sides to isolate and magnify the central part by 100 times. Painted in oil on hessian fabric, the piece concentrates the key elements of calligraphy—brushwork, construction, and rhythm—into a visual language that invites the viewer to contemplate the nuances of form and movement. The magnification offers an almost microscopic view, transforming familiar brushstrokes into an abstracted, intricate composition." ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q128115>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
