    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/194> ;
    ns1:description "These conceptual photographs are a set of thirty-six chromogenic prints that attest the performance of Song Dong entitled \"Stamping the Water\". The artist repeatedly stamps the Lhasa River in Tibet with a large wood seal carved with the Chinese character for water (shui 水). The image of the performer is always blacklit while the surrounding nature is enlighted. "@en ;
