    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1959> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork was created during the TENG Ensemble's digital performance entitled: "Heaven, Earth, Mankind and Unity (天地人合)" realized on September 2, 2021 by the TENG company and recorded in the concert hall of the Singapore Chinese Culture Centre. The female calligrapher Grace Chen Liang 陈亮  realized the phrase "The Heart Dances and Leaps" (xin feiwu 心飞舞). \r
These words can be considered a contemporary expression, giving a sense of grounding and relevance in contemporary times. Although the words may appear to not have roots in traditional text, its structure was actually inspired by Han Dynasty’s Liu Bang’s poem “Song of the Great Wind” (Dafeng ge 大风歌).  As Liu Ban uses the three words “The Clouds Rose on High” (yun feiyang 云飞扬), Chen too, took liberties in creating a similar syntax with “The Heart Dances and Leaps” (xin feiwu 心飞舞). """ ;
