    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q840173> ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1959> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork was created during the TENG Ensemble's digital performance entitled: \"Heaven, Earth, Mankind and Unity (天地人合)\" realized on September 2, 2021 by the TENG company and recorded in the concert hall of the Singapore Chinese Culture Centre. The female calligrapher Grace Chen Liang 陈亮 creates the two characters jing guan 静观 (observe calmly/mindfulness) using her left hand on the notes of the piece written by Hua Yanjun, commonly known as Ah Bing 阿炳 (1893 – 1950)   “Reflection of the Moon on Erquan Spring” (Er quan ying yue 二泉映月). The work presents the idea of guidance by “stillness” (jing 静) and “observation” (guan 观) through the hustle and bustle of mankind in modern day. Chen recalls the memories of the Erhu solo, “Reflection of the Moon on Erquan Spring”, to be one of her father’s favourite pieces when she was a child. The fluctuating movements in the piece are profound and philosophical. The listener naturally closes their eyes to find the depiction of mountains, waters, skies, and earth within the music." ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
