    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/square_word_calligraphy> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Art for the People for The Met (Art For The People - Square word calligraphy)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the four English words \"Art For The People\" written in \"Square Word Calligraphy\", that is a system designed by Xu Bing that adapts the English alphabet to the calligraphic forms of Chinese writing. While Chinese characters are made up of several strokes written in the same imaginary square, here each word is made up of its letters written in the same imaginary square. The expression is written from left to right and from top to bottom and sums up one of Mao Zedong's most fundamental views on art that he explained during the famous \"Talks at the Yan'an Conference on Literature and Art” (1942). Reflective also of the artist's personal conviction that Mao's concept of art for the people is universally relevant; the work exemplifies the way in which Xu Bing integrates his particular cultural background and life experience into the international context of contemporary art. " ;
    ns1:directionality "Free",
        "Modern" ;
