    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """"Who transmitted the knowledge from ancient times?"\r
The origins of ancient times were passed down through generations of people, orally transmitted until today.\r
\r
"How can we investigate the pre-formation of the universe?"\r
Modern science attempts to understand the origin and evolution of the universe through methods like the Big Bang theory and observations of cosmic microwave background radiation. Clues are also provided by ancient texts and archaeological findings.\r
\r
"In the primordial darkness, who can fathom it?"\r
The beginning of the universe was a state of extreme chaos and obscurity. High-energy and high-temperature matter filled the surroundings, and plasma prevented light from propagating. Approximately 380,000 years later, the universe cooled down, and light emerged.\r
\r
"How can we recognize the true nature amidst the obscurity?"\r
Scientists use laboratory research and theoretical models to simulate and observe the behavior and interactions of primordial matter in particle physics experiments and cosmology studies. They infer the nature and characteristics of primordial matter and its impact on the early universe. Even though it is intangible, it exists.\r
\r
"Bright and dark alternates, what causes it?"\r
The alternation of brightness during the day and darkness at night is due to the Earth's rotation and revolution. When a certain area faces the Sun due to the Earth's rotation, it becomes bright, while the opposite side experiences darkness.\r
\r
"The harmony of Yin and Yang, what is their origin and transformation?"\r
Yin and Yang rely on each other and transform continuously, forming the operating principles and driving force of all things in the world, as well as the diversity and balance of the universe.\r
\r
"The nine celestial layers, who governs and measures them?"\r
The nine celestial layers represent the highest levels of the universe, governing the creation and operation of all things. Each layer has unique features and inhabitants, playing significant roles in ruling, order, and the dwelling place of deities.\r
\r
"What achievements lie in it, who initiated its creation?"\r
The measurement and calculation of the nine celestial layers are skills of astronomers, used for predicting seasons and creating calendars.\r
By observing the positions, trajectories, and cycles of celestial bodies, they grasp the fundamental structure of the cosmos.\r
According to the Classic of Mountains and Seas (Shan Hai Jing), the nine celestial layers were created by numerous deities working together.\r
\r
"How does it revolve and revolve around?"\r
Celestial bodies revolve around the axis, as if tied to the center with a rope.\r
According to The Book of Jin – Astronomical Records, the heavens are round like an opened canopy, while the earth is like a chessboard.\r
The celestial sphere resembles a canopy with a polar point, and celestial bodies revolve around it like wheels turning around an axis.\r
\r
"Where is the top of the celestial axis?"\r
The top of the celestial axis has no specific location; it is a hypothetical point.\r
\r
"When do the eight pillars appear?"\r
The eight pillars supporting the heavens are fictitious and serve to describe the motion of celestial bodies.\r
\r
"Why is the southeast deficient?"\r
The unevenness in the southeast is due to the celestial canopy rotating at a 36-degree angle.\r
The Earth's equator from rotation and the ecliptic from revolution are not on the same plane, causing the North Pole to be 36 degrees above the ground.\r
The variation of the North Star gave rise to the myth of Gonggong's anger striking the pillar of heaven.\r
Ancient people thus believed that the pivotal star of the North Pole moved to the northwest, placing Mount Kunlun in the northwest as well.\r
\r
"Within the confines of the nine heavens, what is placed and assigned?"\r
The depiction of the nine heavens is based on ancient Chinese astronomical concepts.\r
In reality, the universe is infinite and flat, a three-dimensional space where celestial bodies interact through gravity without boundaries. \r
\r
"There are many corners and crevices, who knows their number?"\r
The number of galaxies and stars in the universe is still a rough estimate in scientific research.\r
\r
"Where does the sky rest?"\r
In traditional Chinese cosmology, the sky, earth, and universe are considered an organic whole with close connections.\r
The sky is above, and the earth is below, linked through the celestial pivot, celestial axis, and celestial balance.\r
\r
"How is it divided into twelve?"\r
The sky is divided into reference systems such as the ecliptic, equator, and celestial axis.\r
The ecliptic serves as a reference plane for the movement of the sun, moon, and planets and divides the sky into twelve segments, known as the zodiac.\r
\r
"Where do the sun and moon belong, and where do the stars assemble?"\r
The sun, moon, and other celestial bodies move along the ecliptic.\r
Additionally, ancient China divided the sky into twenty-eight lunar mansions, with each mansion representing specific constellations or star clusters.\r
This guided agricultural activities, calendar systems, and other practices.\r
The positions and movements of the stars were also used for divination and predictions, closely related to earthly matters.\r
\r
"Emerging from Tang Valley, following Mengji. From brightness to darkness, how many miles does it travel?"\r
The journey of the sun described in myths is legendary and does not align with scientific calculations.\r
According to scientific measurements, the sun travels approximately 15 million kilometers from sunrise to sunset, which is far different from the myth's depiction.\r
In myths, the sun is often regarded as a mysterious existence or controlled by divine creatures, moving along a fixed orbit.\r
Myths typically use expressions like "ten thousand miles" or "ninety thousand miles" to symbolically describe the sun's movement, representing its daily course and the passing of time.\r
\r
"What virtues does the moon possess that it dies and then revives?"\r
The phases of the moon, such as the full moon and new moon, are caused by the changing position of the moon as it orbits around the Earth and the relative positions of the Earth and the Sun.\r
The moon itself does not have its own source of light; its brightness is the result of the sunlight reflecting off its surface.\r
\r
"Where do the dark spots come from, and why is the hare seen on its belly?"\r
The dark spots on the moon, also known as "lunar maria," are visual illusions caused by variations in the surface terrain and angles of illumination on the moon.\r
There are no physical objects present; people perceive shapes like a rabbit or a toad within these spots.\r
\r
"Why does Nuqi have no mate, yet she gives birth to nine sons?"\r
The legend of Nuqi giving birth to nine sons reflects the ancient people's fascination and reverence for the mysteries of life and reproduction.\r
In a matrilineal clan society, women held a higher status, symbolizing the greatness of their reproductive ability and motherhood.\r
\r
"Where does Boqiang reside, and where can we find his benevolent aura?"\r
According to The Classic of Mountains and Seas – Overseas Northern Classic, the wind deity Boqiang, who has the face of a man and the body of a bird, resides in the north.\r
The gentle and pleasant breeze is often associated with blowing from the east, symbolizing the unobstructed flow of the wood element and promoting the growth of all things.\r
\r
"Why does it turn dark and then become bright again?"\r
The terms "heaven's closure," "darkness," "heaven's opening," and "brightness" describe the changes between day and night due to the Earth's rotation and revolution.\r
This metaphor compares the sky to a window in a house, symbolizing the opening and closing of the window for day and night, vividly expressing the natural phenomenon of day and night alternation.\r
\r
"When the constellation Jiao has not dawned, where is the hidden luminous essence?"\r
During the dawn, the sun has not yet risen, and the stars in the eastern sky have not completely disappeared.\r
At this moment, the sun is hidden below the horizon, waiting to rise, while the stars in the east gradually fade, making way for daylight.\r
\r
"Why was Gonggong not entrusted, and why did the teachers not support him? Why were they not worried and did not teach him the proper methods? Why did Chi and Gui not listen to Gun?"\r
The people had high hopes and trust in Gonggong, believing he could solve the flood problem.\r
They considered Gonggong to be highly intelligent and believed he could find a unique way to address the flood disaster.\r
Gonggong imitated the method of a woodpecker and built dikes, moved boulders, and carried soil with its beak, thinking that it would be effective.\r
\r
"To achieve success, why was Emperor not punishing him? Why is he forever confined to Mount Yu, and why has it been three years without implementation?"\r
Despite Gonggong's contributions to flood control, Emperor Yao believed that his actions needed to be punished to uphold the authority of the law and order.\r
The prolonged exile of Gonggong on Mount Yu might have involved political power struggles and conflicts between Gonggong and Shun's supporters, leading to his long-term confinement without release to this day."""@en,
        "Various methods such as gathering wind vegetables, dragging stones, and using windows were attempted to control water flow, but they were unsuccessful. However, Yu the Great successfully managed the floods by using a method of guiding water through nets and pearls. Unlike previous approaches that focused on blocking water, Yu emphasized guiding its flow. His method became a model for flood control, as he directed floodwaters by digging channels and using techniques like gathering wind vegetables to gradually control the floods, allowing the land to prosper and people to live in harmony. Yu is often depicted in a romanticized manner, using an eagle cage as a map and drawing channels with a swipe of his tail. These mythical descriptions add a sense of mystery and imagination to his legendary role in flood control. They highlight his heroic image and extraordinary abilities, elevating historical events to a symbolic level, imbuing them with deeper significance. [...]"@en,
        "鲸采风菜提曳石窗出等方法法理泌水但未成功大禹則采网珠導水流的方法成功治理洪水並用 土地雖往重工握离注重好流方法不同大禹之方陆更我学有敦为让水典範他阙贱汀渠引导洪水挖框生地菜提等透漸控制洪水使土地得以共后樂業禹以鷹籠為圖膳用尾巴劃地闖馨磷渠這種浪漫化之描述腻予了禹语水遏握之神秘和想象力实頸出他的英璀形象与非凡能力将層史事件赋予了挺台丝的亲義 [...]"@zh,
        "Jīng cǎifēng cài tí yè shí chuāng chū děng fāngfǎ fǎlǐ bì shuǐ dàn wèi chénggōng dà yǔ zé cǎi wǎng zhū dǎo shuǐliú de fāngfǎ chénggōng zhìlǐ hóngshuǐ bìngyòng tǔdì suī wǎng zhònggōng wò lí zhùzhòng hǎo liú fāngfǎ bùtóng dà yǔ zhī fāng lù gèng wǒ xué yǒu dūn wèi ràng shuǐ diǎnfàn tā quējiàntīng qú yǐndǎo hóngshuǐ wā kuàng shēngdì cài tí děng tòu jiàn kòngzhì hóngshuǐ shǐ tǔdì déyǐ gòng hòu lè yè yǔ yǐ yīng lóng wèi tú shàn yòng wěibā huà dì chuǎng xīn lín qú zhè zhǒng làngmàn huà zhī miáoshù nì yǔle yǔ yǔ shuǐ è wò zhī shénmì hé xiǎngxiàng lì shí jǐng chū tā de yīng cuǐ xíngxiàng yǔ fēifán nénglì jiāng céng shǐ shìjiàn fùyǔle tǐng tái sī de qīn yì [...]"@zh-Latn ;
