    ns1:description "\"Grain Buds\" is one of the works included in the series \"Brilliant Star\". Grain buds (xiaoman 小满) refers to the eighth solar term in the traditional Chinese agricultural calendar, which divides the year into 24 fifteen-day periods. This particular solar term marks the period when plant seeds are full but not yet fully ripe, occurring between late May and early summer. In this piece, the original photograph taken by Chu Chu at West Lake in Hangzhou is partially obscured by multiple layers of calligraphy and painting. The artist employs cerulean and yellow-gold ink, creating a dynamic explosion of color and energy that enlivens the entire composition.    " ;
