        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q315>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q450> ;
    ns2:P2048 "102 cm (each)" ;
    ns2:P2049 "127 cm (each)" ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1602687>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/221> ;
    ns1:description """This series of photographs attest the three different moments of Zhang Huan's performance entitled "1/2". In the first photograph entitled "1/2 Meat", Zhang Huan is naked and he 'wears' a carcass of raw bovine meat, reminiscent of the armors of ancient Chinese warriors. In the second photograph entitled "1/2 Text", the body and the face of the artist are completely covered by Chinese characters, so that Zhang Huan's ethnicity is literally inscribed on his body. In the third photograph entitled "1/2 Meat + Text",  Zhang Huan 'wears' again the carcass of the raw bovine meat, but this time his  body is completely covered by written characters. \r
To realize Chinese characters on the artist's body, his friend used traditional calligraphic tools, like brush and ink, and the support for their calligraphies is the artist's body instead of paper. The chromatism of these photographs also recalls traditional calligraphy: the black of the ink, and the white and red of the carcass that recalls white paper and  red seal(s). \r
"""@en ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q125191> ;
