<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2314> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1476 "Xu Bing for Louis Vuitton - Customized Hard Suitcase Case for the Four Treasures of the Study (Ink, paper, brush, and ink stone) with “Square Word Calligraphy” Inscription"@en,
        "'英文方块字书法' 的文房四宝特别定制箱"@zh,
        "'Yīngwén fāngkuàizì shūfǎ' de wénfángsìbǎo tèbié dìngzhì xiāng"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P176 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q191485> ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1277> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1094542>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q121916>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7553> ;
    ns2:P2048 "42.6 cm" ;
    ns2:P2049 "64.7 cm" ;
    ns2:P2284 "2.8 million RMB" ;
    ns2:P2386 "23.7 cm" ;
    ns2:P287 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1096> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q47071>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P941 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2318> ;
    ns1:description "The famous fashion house Louis Vuitton collaborated with the renowned contemporary Chinese artist Xu Bing, drawing inspiration from his representative work “Square Word Calligraphy” (Yingwen fangkuai zi shufa 英文方块字书法). By combining the invented character concept from his work “A Book from the Sky” (Tianshu 天书) with the iconic motifs of the LV maison, Xu Bing and the famous fashion house jointly launched a specially designed calligraphy set box in “Square Word Calligraphy”. In May 2016, this work was auctioned by Sotheby’s during a dinner auction in Beijing, fetching a final price of 2.8 million RMB. The custom-made hard case took two years to design and produce. It contains 30 items, including traditional Chinese writing tools (brush, ink, paper, and inkstone) as well as modern instruments such as a tablet. The exterior design of the case is based on the poem “In Ancient Days” (Zai gudai 在古代, 2004)  by the female contemporary Chinese poet Zhai Yongming 翟永明 (b.1955),  along with a note from the author. Xu Bing first translated the text into English, then transformed each English word into a form resembling a Chinese character to write it using his \"Square Word Calligraphy\" method." ;
    ns1:hasChineseConcept <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/junzi> ;
