<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/235> a ns3:Q7725310 ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4970> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Pseudo-Characters Series (虚构文字系列 )"@en,
        "虚构文字系列 "@zh,
        "Xūgòu wénzì xìliè"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/231> ;
    ns2:P580 "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P582 "1986"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/235.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """This series consists of big panels in which Chinese characters are written backwards, overturned, crossed out, mutilated or reconstructed. These characters have been taken away from their original function to play a syntactical part in a sentence. They are detached, synthesized, misplaced, overlapped, miswritten, negated and inverted to create an uncertain world.   \r
In this series, Gu Wenda re-elaborates and deconstructs not only traditional calligraphy and but also traditional landscape ink painting. Instead of mountains, clouds, trees and streams, in fact,  abstract and semi-abstract ink marks float across the page along with similarly abstract, pseudo-Chinese characters. Bessire (2003, 198) affirms that: " Gu's audacious explorations, his new techniques, his elimination of individual brush stroke and unreadable Chinese characters, have allowed him to create a new kind of Chinese ink painting: conceptualized abstract ink painting."\r
The series is composed of several works, each one exploring different compositions of characters. The most important are: “Characters of ‘Still’ Written by Three Men and Three Woman”  (Wo piyue san nan san nu de jing zi 我批阅三男三女书写的静字), “Negative and Positive Characters” (Zhengfan de zi 正反的字), “Misplaced Characters” (Cuowei de zi 错位的字), “Meaningless Characters” (Wuyi de zi 无意的字) and “Modern Meaning of Totem and Taboos” (Tuteng yu jinji 图腾与禁忌). Also works from “The Mythos of Last Dynasties” became part of this series (e.g. “Synthesized Words”, 1985). """@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/235.jpg> ;
