<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2363> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P144 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2059> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1043197>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11660> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/great_seal_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2363.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Dialogue of Heaven: Artificial Intelligence Converses with Qu Yuan (《天问》- seal script)" ;
    ns1:description """CWU 1 consists of excerpts from Qu Yuan’s Questions to Heaven (Tianwen 天问) presented in classical Chinese and written in seal script (zhuanshu). The text reproduces the calligraphic transcription created by Huang Yeda for the installation "Inquiry of Heaven" (2023), preserving both the visual form of the original work and its historical reference to the script traditions associated with the state of Chu. The characters appear in red against a black background, recalling the cinnabar inscriptions and dark surfaces of the original installation while reinforcing the ritual and archaic qualities of the script. Traditional Chinese characters are employed throughout, and the text follows the conventional layout of Chinese manuscripts, being arranged in vertical columns and read from top to bottom and from right to left.\r
Within the structure of the video, the text of Questions to Heaven appears progressively, section by section, serving as the starting point for the subsequent interaction with artificial intelligence. Each passage is displayed on screen after the completion of an AI-generated response (CWU 3), creating a cyclical sequence in which Qu Yuan’s ancient questions and the machine’s contemporary answers alternate throughout the thirty-three-minute duration of the work.""" ;
