    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 A Neon Calligraphy Series: Sotheby's (sotheby's)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the English name of the Sotheby’s corporation, which is written in small yellow Roman neon letters in the upper register of the artwork. It functions as the verbal starting point for Gu Wenda’s “Complex English-Chinese Translation”, first developed for his “Forest of Stone Steles” (1993-2005). From the English name in the top register (CWU 1), the artist transliterates the sounds. of the syllables into Chinese characters (CWU 2).  In the lower register, we find new English translations that Gu created by translating back into English each single character (CWU 3). The Chinese and English texts are written in a modern way, from left to right. The last panel at the right bears a vertical column of linear yellow neon Chinese characters as colophon, Gu shi kai dian 谷氏楷典, followed by Gu’s seal in red neon. The colophon can be translated as ‘Mr. Gu’s canon of regular script’, a reference to Gu’s distinctive style of calligraphy (Cateforis 2010,13). " ;
