<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2487> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1891>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q38> ;
    ns2:P1476 "WRITE Project Logo with Luo Qi Calligraphy "@en ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1094542> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "2021"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P856 <https://writecalligraphyproject.eu/the-project/> ;
    ns2:P88 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q131262> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2487.jpg> ;
    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/84> ;
    ns1:description """This is the logo of the research project "WRITE – New Forms of Calligraphy in China: A Contemporary Culture Mirror" (Grant Agreement No. 949645, 2020‑2026) funded by the European Research Council (ERC) and led by the Department of Interpreting and Translation at the University of Bologna (PI: Prof. Adriana Iezzi). The project aims at analysing how the emergence of new forms of calligraphy in contemporary China is re-defining Chinese cultural identity. \r
The logo embodies a harmonious integration of Chinese calligraphy and Latin script, aiming to present the encouter of Chinese and European cultures. The red character is a calligraphic artwork by the calligrapher Luo Qi, representing the character xie 写, which translates as “write.” In this rendition, Luo Qi reinterpreted an archaic form of xie 写, blending his distinctive style with elements of running script (xingshu 行书). Notably, the upper portion of this character resembles the letter “W,” which inspired the addition of the letters R-I-T-E to complete the word WRITE. In this logo, the dynamic brushstrokes of the artist converge seamlessly with the structured form of digital typography, creating a visual synthesis of traditional artistry and contemporary graphic design, Chinese and English languages, Chinese writing and Latin alphabet, and extensively between Asian and Euro-American writing cultures. The logo was created by D-Sign graphic design agency in close collaboration with the WRITE team. """ ;
