<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2500> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1476 "DRAWSHINE (妆写) Logo"@en,
        "妆写"@zh,
        "Zhuāng xiě"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q10953913>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1207152>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q866081> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3133>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P941 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4211668> ;
    ns2:P973 <https://drawshine.com/> ;
    ns1:description """DRAWSHINE (Zhuangxie 妆写) is  a brand that produces cosmetics in porcelain containers, contains multiple references to Chinese tradition. The left part of the logo explicitly evokes the jade "ruyi 如意", an object historically used as a ceremonial scepter or as an amulet symbolizing power and good fortune, whose flat upper surface was traditionally inscribed with characters. Similarly, the brand logo references this upper portion of the "ruyi" by inscribing the brand name within it, reinterpreting the pictographic form of the character "zhuang 妆" (“to apply makeup” or “to beautify”). Of particular interest is the right-hand component, the “woman” radical (nü 女), which appears mirrored in the left-hand component (qiang 丬), alluding to the world of women’s cosmetics that the logo represents.\r
The allusion to the jade "ruyi", which can also resemble a traditional seal, lends an aura of elegance and refinement to the brand’s products. On the left, the brand name is displayed both in Chinese characters, zhuangxie 妆写 (zhuang 妆: “to apply makeup” or “to beautify”; xie 写: “to write”), and in its English equivalent, Drawshine. The various shades of green in the logo’s background harmonize with the lighter yellow tones of the text and seal, echoing the characteristic color of Celadon porcelain.""" ;
    ns1:hasChineseVisualElement <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/green_celadon_vase>,
        <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/jade>,
