<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2501> a ns1:CalliWritingUnit ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q10953913>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1190910>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7242>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q866081> ;
    ns2:P282 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8201> ;
    ns2:P407 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7850> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/small_seal_script> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 DRAWSHINE Logo (妆)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is placed within the "ruyi 如意" form in the left part of the DRAWSHINE logo.  "Ruyi" is an object historically used as a ceremonial scepter or as an amulet symbolizing power and good fortune, whose flat upper surface was traditionally inscribed with characters. This CWU consists of the character "zhuang 妆"(to apply make-up/to beautify) written in small seal script (xiaozhuan 小篆) . The character is composed of the radical "nü 女" (woman) - on the right, that is rendered through the stylized figure of a woman, and of the left-component "qiang 丬" (piece of wood, half tree trunk, bed), that looks like a mirror in which the woman is looking at herself. this sense of mirroring generates a sense of visual symmetry and reinforcing the thematic focus on femininity. The interplay between these two components transforms the character into a harmonious, balanced form that visually resonates with the aesthetics of traditional Chinese calligraphy, while simultaneously being adapted for contemporary brand design. Conceptually, this CWU embodies the fusion of heritage and modernity, conveying notions of beauty, personal care, and elegance, while serving as a distinctive visual identifier for the DRAWSHINE brand.\r
""" ;
