        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P571 "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P941 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/729> ;
    ns1:description """Qiu Zhijie’s photograph "Light Writing: The Heart Sutra No. 22 (光写书法：心经 22)" features the characters Wuyi shijie 無意識界 [无意识界], translated as “In the Void” or “No Realm of Consciousness,” an excerpt from the Heart Sutra. The photograph was realized in 2005 at the Hebei Quyang Dafotou (Great Buddha Head) of Quyang County (Hebei province).\r
Part of the "Light Writing Calligraphy – Heart Sutra Series", this work is one of fifty-five photographs in which Qiu reimagines calligraphy through light painting, preserving its performative gestures while expanding it into new media.\r
The process is site-specific and nocturnal: light replaces brush and ink, and long-exposure photography captures the unfolding gesture. The resulting images function both as traditional calligraphy and as ephemeral public interventions, shareable via social media, reaching audiences beyond the conventional gallery.\r
Qiu’s practice also engages Buddhist iconography, particularly Buddha Amoghasiddhi, associated with the gesture of courage (Abhayamudra): the right hand raised at chest level with the palm outward, symbolizing the power to dispel fear and cultivate a mind free from resentment, especially envy. Amoghasiddhi is one of the five transcendent Buddhas, embodying victory over obstacles.""" ;
