    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/253.jpg> ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/251> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is the final result of the performance entitled \"Writing the 'Orchid Pavilion Preface' One Thousand Times\" (重复书写一千遍 '兰亭序'). In this performance, Qiu Zhijie decides to devote himself to copying the work \"Lanting xu 兰亭序\" (Orchid Pavilion Preface) composed by Wang Xizhi in 353 AD. Qiu Zhijie repeatedly copies the work a thousand times on the same piece of rice papersheet. Repeatedly writing over his free-hand interpretation of the original, Qiu turns the paper into a saturated black field. By focusing on the process of writing rather than on its literary content, Qiu asserts that the ultimate goal of calligraphic practice is a form of \"written meditation\"."@en ;
