    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2545.jpg> ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2544> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is part of the performance \"Hair Painting Greatwall 2025\" realized by Echo Morgan in 2025 at the Great Wall of China. The artwork consists of black ink marks, lines, and dots applied to canvas using Echo Morgan’s hair as a brush. Many marks are circular or semicircular, while others form dense patches or thin, flowing lines, reflecting the pressure and movement of her body during the performance. The variation in density and layering creates a dynamic, rhythmic surface that records the physical gestures in real time. Monochrome black emphasizes the gestural quality, turning the canvas into a material archive of the artist’s performance and the cyclical, repetitive nature of her movements." ;
