    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P9302 <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/regular_script> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2630.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Eye Charts - Feng's Vector (signs)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU consists of the typeface Feng's Vector (Shiliangfeng 矢量冯), created by Feng Mengbo for the second panel of Eye Charts (2011). Unlike the pixel-based reduction of Feng's Bitmap, this typeface reduces Chinese characters to delicate vector lines generated through mathematical formulas. The reduction process is inspired by stone flowers (shihua 石花), rubbings taken from eroded or damaged steles in which only faint traces of the original inscriptions remain. By digitally reinterpreting these historical fragments, Feng Mengbo preserves their visual memory through artistic remediation while accelerating the natural process of erosion. The resulting characters are stripped to their essential structures and positioned at the threshold between readability and unreadability.\r
The artist explores the notions of distortion and the inversion of reality. In a deliberate paradox, the larger the characters appear, the less legible they become; the smaller they are, the clearer they read. Through this inversion, Feng challenges conventional perception and questions the reliability of visual systems. The artwork thus becomes a meditation on how digital logic, based on quantification, scaling, and code, reshapes our perception between visibility and abstraction.""" ;
