    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/396.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "Best wishes (Ruyi 如意) is an artwork executed in September 2022 by Shao Yan. This artwork belongs to a series of works executed by the artist during September 2022. Inspired by Ming “blue and white porcelain” (Qinghuaci青花瓷), the artist writes the two characters ruyi 如意 on a Chinese porcelain bottle vase (composed of a globular body and a long thin neck), employing a brush and blue ink. The character \"ru\" 如 is written in running script (行书) and also the character \"yi\" 意 is written in running script, but its component parts \"li\" 立 and \"ri\" 日 are written using the seal script forms (zhuanshu zixing 篆书字形). Shao Yan combines the structure of the characters and the shape of the bottle mouth vessel creating a work of unique elegance and beauty. The series is composed of several white vases of different shapes and types (“bottle” vase, “plum” vase, “gourd” vase, “pear shaped” vase, “cylinder” vase etc.) , which are carried out using two distinct tools and techniques: for some of them, Shao Yan writes the characters with a brush while he holds the vase steady with his free hand or he gets help from his assistants. For other works, he uses a syringe to inject the blue ink on the vessels that are located on a rotating base. For the entire collection, Shao Yan writes auspicious words carrying a good-luck meaning and he aims to combine the structure of Chinese characters or the lines and marks formed by the ink jet with the shapes of porcelain vases."@en ;
    ns1:hasChineseVisualElement <http://w3id.org/write/thesaurus/blue_white_porcelain>,
