<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/448> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q42622> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Watching the Sea and Listening to the Waves (观海听涛) "@en,
        "观海听涛"@zh,
        "Guān hǎi tīng tāo"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/450> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q165> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q127418>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q130693> ;
    ns2:P2048 "40 cm" ;
    ns2:P2049 "23 cm" ;
    ns2:P2284 "3000 RMB" ;
    ns2:P287 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/277> ;
    ns2:P38 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q39099> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1088>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns2:P571 "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P856 <https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/Bc84b5OfrHaZVEDz3FJIBw>,
        <https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/wYWOZStxJ0FcjF1etLyr6g> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/448.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """"Watching the Sea and Listening to the Waves (Guan hai ting tao 观海听涛)" is one of the artworks executed in 2015 by Shao Yan. This artwork was exhibited the same year (May 15 – June 7) at the "Calligraphy and Ceramics Art Exhibition" (Shufa taoci yishu zhan 书法陶瓷艺术展) opened in Suzhou at the Ming Art Museum (Ming meishuguan 明·美术馆). The exhibition, called “Between Squares and Circles” (Fangyuan zhejian方圆之间), featured 60 pieces of calligraphy works carried out by three outstanding young and middle-aged calligraphers in contemporary China: Shao Yan, Li Qiang 李强 and Xu Guixun 徐圭逊. The works, as the title suggests, had to present forms and styles similar to circles and squares. The artwork is a cylindrical “maotong” (帽筒) vase in white porcelain. Shao Yan engraved the four characters on the surface of the vessel and then filled in the blue color. The four characters recall the "bird seal script" (niao zhuan 鸟篆), a kind of artistic script in common use during the late Warring States period (475-221 BC). This script is characterized by gently and intricated curved lines decorated with bird designs. In this work, Shao Yan re-elaborates this script drawing birds and fishes in a naïf style, recalling the acquatic scene evoked by the four characters. \r
The work respected the purpose of the exhibition that was not only to show the combination of traditional and modern art, but also to promote Chinese traditional culture. In fact, even though Shao Yan’s work reflected the taste and culture of the present time, it still maintained the true meaning and essence of Chinese characters. """@en ;
