    ns2:P571 "2022-09"^^xsd:gYearMonth ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is created and used for the performance \"Woman 女+ Horse 马 = Mother 妈\", which took place in 2022 at the TJ Boulting of London during \"Love, Celebration and the Road Ahead\", a three-day festival (September, 29 - October, 1st ) to mark the launch of Hettie Judah's book entitled \"How Not To Exclude Artist Mothers (and other parents)\". The artwork consists of white lanterns with different size bound together and enveloping Echo Morgan's body. These lanterns are decorated with various writings, combining Chinese characters with the English language, such as: \"ziyou 自由\" (freedom); \"hai 海\" (sea); \"hao 好\" (good); \"popo 婆婆\" (grandmother); \"shengming 生命\" (life); \"tudi 土地\" (soil); \"tielian 铁链\" (iron chain); \"Can be a good mum and a good artist?\"; \"The Chinese word mum is combined woman 女 + horse 马\"; \"Flying dress\"; \"Mothers are the best in the world if you have one you are precious\"; \"Yellow face wife\", \"Sea Big Ocean like Mother Care\", \"Don’t get greedy. Only harvest for as long as you can hold your breath\", etc. "@en ;
