    ns2:P571 "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "This photograph represents the character \"xin 心\" (heart) made in \"Nüshu 女书\". Artist Jessie Yingying Gong applied LED lights to the body of a dancer who freely performed dance moves. This photograph is part of the Dance Remains Series (舞迹系列) created by the artist Jessie Yingying Gong in 2018, during the six months of the artist residency at the \"Swatch Art Peace Hotel\" in Shanghai. “Dance Remains” is a series of long exposure photographs the artist made of public dancers (both men and women) in various parks around Shanghai in the evening, after asking them to attach LED lights on their bodies while dancing. The artist captured around 80 photographs and in eight of them, the result appears as if dancers are writing an abstract secret language with the movement of their bodies, resembling some characters written in Nüshu 女书, such as \"xin 心 (heart)\"; \"bei 背\" (sadness); \"shui 水\" (water) and \"xiao 小\" (small). This for the artist evokes the times when the female population gathered together to sing songs and do embroidery in the Nüshu village. By combining these photographs with the flowy Nüshu characters, she intends to form a poetic visual compilation of photography and writing."@en ;
