    ns1:description "This figure was designed by Jessie Yingying Gong represents the Chinese character \"xi 喜\" (happiness) written in oracle bone script and made with red color neon light. It is part of the \" New Semiotics Series (新符号学系列)\" starting in 2017 and ongoing, in which Jessie Yingying Gong compares two ancient styles of writing: \"Linear B\", that was a syllabic script used for writing in Mycenaean Greek, the earliest attested form of Greek and \"oracle bone script\", used anciently in China."@en ;
