    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/710.jpg> ;
    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/704> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is produced during the performance \"Sculpure Writing\" in 2018 by Li Xinmo. It consists on the 30-meters long volume of the Fahua Sutra which was hanged in the museum space. Li Xinmo writes Scriptures as a replacement for woman, giving rise to a feminist perspective. In her opinion, Buddha is a symbol of the equality of all living beings, but also transcends gender. Reading and writing Buddhist sutras was her early lesson. The interpretation of the universe and everything in the sutras had an important influence on her thoughts. In her opinion, to become a Buddha is to transcend the existing social shaping, knowledge system and integrate with all things, thus connecting the energy field of the universe."@en ;
