    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/753.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Dance (舞)" ;
    ns1:description """This CWU is part of the Visual Artwork "Dance" (Wu 舞), realized by Wang Dongling in 1989.  The character 'wu 舞', meaning 'dance', is written in a bold cursive script. The strokes of the character are inspired by Graham's physical posture in motion. Wang "dashed off rhythmic ink strokes directly onto the dancer's image that echoed her form and movement. This resonance of movement between world, mind and body, "what the Chinese call qiyun 气韵 (spirit resonance) is the central desiderata for brush and ink painting" (Ink Studio).\r
The aesthetics principle of qiyun refers to the resonance of the breath in the calligraphic line and the inner vitality of the artist, which together give life and movement to the work."""@en ;
