    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Dance (《观公孙大娘弟子舞剑器行》)" ;
    ns1:description "In contrast to the central character Wu 舞 (CWU 1), written in bold and rhythmic ink strokes, the surrounding text (CWU 2) has been rendered in a lively cursive script using an orange-red (vermilion) ink. This chromatic value can be associated more with the palette of a painter than a calligrapher. "@en ;
