    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """Long ago, Zhang Xu saw Aunt Gongsun dance.\r
There was a beautiful woman of the Gongsun clan. When she performed her sword dance, she captivated the entire realm.\r
Spectators crowded like mountains, their faces struck with awe; Heaven and earth seemed to rise and fall in response.\r
Swift as Hou Yi shooting down the nine suns, graceful as imperial dragons soaring through the skies.\r
She approached like thunder gathering its wrath, and departed like rivers and seas gathering calm light.\r
Red lips and pearl sleeves now lie in solitude, yet her students later carried on her fragrance.\r
[…]\r
\r
"""@en,
        """昔张旭见公孙大娘舞。\r
昔有佳人公孙氏，一舞剑器动四方。\r
观者如山色沮丧，天地为之久低昂。\r
㸌如羿射九日落，矫如群帝骖龙翔。\r
来如雷霆收震怒，罢如江海凝清光。\r
绛唇珠袖两寂寞，晚有弟子传芬芳。\r
[…]"""@zh,
        """昔張旭見公孫大娘舞。\r
昔有佳人公孫氏，一舞劍器動四方。\r
觀者如山色沮喪，天地為之久低昂。\r
㸌如羿射九日落，矯如群帝驂龍翔。\r
來如雷霆收震怒，罷如江海凝清光。\r
絳唇珠袖兩寂寞，晚有弟子傳芬芳。\r
[…]"""@zh,
        """Xī Zhāng Xù jiàn Gōngsūn Dàniáng wǔ。\r
Xī yǒu jiārén Gōngsūn shì, yī wǔ jiànqì dòng sìfāng.\r
Guān zhě rú shān sè jǔsàng, tiāndì wèi zhī jiǔ dī'áng.\r
Chù rú Yì shè jiǔ rì luò, jiǎo rú qún dì cān lóng xiáng.\r
Lái rú léitíng shōu zhènnù, bà rú jiānghǎi níng qīngguāng.\r
Jiàng chún zhū xiù liǎng jìmò, wǎn yǒu dìzǐ chuán fēnfāng.\r
[…]"""@zh-Latn .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/803> a ns3:Q7725634 ;
    ns2:P1476 "Dream of the Red Chamber (红楼梦)"@en,
        "红楼梦"@zh,
        "Honglou Meng"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P50 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q182874> ;
    ns2:P571 "1791"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "\"Dream of the Red Chamber\" (Honglou Meng 红楼梦) is a novel composed by Cao Xueqin 曹雪芹 (1710 - 1765) in the middle of the 18th century. One of the Four Great Classical Novels of Chinese literature, it is known for its psychological scope, and its observation of the worldview, aesthetics, life-styles, and social relations of 18th-century China. The intricate strands of its plot depict the rise and decline of a family much like Cao's own and, by extension, of the dynasty itself. Cao depicts the power of the father over the family, but the novel is intended to be a memorial to the women he knew in his youth: friends, relatives and servants. At a more profound level, the author explores religious and philosophical questions, and the writing style includes echoes of the plays and novels of the late Ming, as well as poetry from earlier periods."@en ;
    ns1:hasWikidataResource <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7213376> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/811> a ns3:Q1400264 ;
    ns2:P2561 "Cloud Gate Dance Theatre of Taiwan (云门舞集)" ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q865> ;
    ns2:P453 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/819> ;
    ns2:P527 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/813> ;
    ns2:P571 "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1266> ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.cloudgate.org.tw/en/cg> ;
    ns1:description """Cloud Gate Dance Theatre is a modern dance group based in Taiwan. It was founded in 1973 by choreographer Lin Hwai-min 林懷民 (b.1947). Cloud Gate has performed in Europe, Asia, North America, and South America. The company also spends a lot of its time performing throughout Taiwan and is generally recognised as the country's premier dance organization. In recognition of its importance locally and internationally, on August 21, 2003, Taiwan's government proclaimed the "Cloud Gate Day" and named the street on which the company's office lies "Cloud Gate Lane." This was the first time in Taiwan's history a day and place were named after a living artist or active artistic organization. Its twenty-two dancers receive trainings of meditation, Qi Gong, an ancient form of breathing exercise, internal martial arts, modern dance, ballet and calligraphy. The current director of the company is Cheng Tsung-Lung 鄭宗龍. The twenty-two dancers are: The twenty-two dancers are: CHOU Chang-ning周章佞, HUANG Pei-hua 黄珮華, LEE Ching-chun 李靜君, TSAI Ming-yuan 蔡銘元, CHIU I-wen 邱怡文, LIN Chia-liang 林佳良, SU I-ping 蘇依屏, SUNG Chao-chiun 宋超群, WANG Chibh-hao 汪志浩, WEN Ching-ching 溫璟靜, YANG I-chun 楊儀君, CHOU Wei-ping 周偉萍, KO Wan-chun 柯宛均, LIN Tzu-chun 林姿君, LIU Hui-ling 劉惠玲, SHEN Yi-wen 沈怡效, WONG Lap-cheong 王立翔, YU Chien-hung 余建宏, HOU Tang-li 侯當立, HUANG Mei-ya 黃媺雅, LIN Hsin-fang 林心放and LEE Tzu-chun 李姿君.\r
"""@en ;
