    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/848> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork is produced during the performance \"Desire for Procreation and Life (渴望生命)\" held on August 14, 2010 at the Tap Seac Museum of Art in Macao. Accompanied by a female musician playing the cello, Pu Lieping reflects on the life drive of man and even more of woman, and introduces the element of dance, through a pregnant dancer who accompanies the notes of a cello played by a female musician. The artist writes the four characters \"Shengming zhi yun 生命之韵\" (Rhythm of Life) both on paper and also on the pregnant dancer's white clothes. Through this performance, Pu Lieping tries to interpret Chinese character art through the senses of sight, hearing, and body language."@en ;
