<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1025> a ns3:Q4502142 ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4970> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Li Bai’s 'Drink Alone Under the Moon'; 'Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Sky'  (李白《月下独酌》;《 把酒问天》)"@en,
        "李白《月下独酌》;《把酒问天》"@zh,
        "Lǐ Bái 'Yuè xià dúzhuó'; 'Bǎ jiǔ wèn tiān'"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/748> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q131395>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q165939>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6010868>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7071> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1144689>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q207849> ;
    ns2:P2048 "170 cm" ;
    ns2:P2049 "360 cm" ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q208045>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3142> ;
    ns2:P571 "2019"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1032>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/879> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1025.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """"Li Bai's ‘Drink Alone Under the Moon’; ‘Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Sky’ " is an installation work realized in 2019 by Wang Dongling . The artist used bright red acrylic on a six-fold screen to write two poems of Li Bai 李白 (701-762): "Drinking alone under the Moon (Yue xia duzhuo 月下独酌) and "Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Sky" (Ba jiu wen tian 把酒问天). The artist used his distinctive Chaos Script (luanshu 乱书) on a golden leaf screen measuring 1.7 meters high and 3.6 meters long. The screen, slightly folded, is placed on a stainless steel plate of 1 meter wide and 4 meters long. This arrangement allows the golden screen to reflect, creating a dynamic interplay of mirroring effects that integrates the viewers into the work and invites a continuously shifting dialogue between the artwork and its audience.\r
Wang Dongling had previously used the same  two poems by Li Bai in 2016 for a monumental  hanging scroll in black ink on white paper, measuring  2.75 m × 18.7 m."""@en ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q20437094>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
