        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q985670> ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.caa.edu.cn/gmrx/2019/10y/201910/35086.html> ;
    ns1:description """In 2005, Wang Dongling initiated a series of exhibitions titled "Writing and Non-Writing" (Shu · Feishu 书·非书), held periodically in Hangzhou. These exhibitions bring together Chinese and international artists who explore the possibilities of calligraphic art through various media. Emphasizing innovation, they showcase how calligraphy is integrated into modern life and diverse cultural contexts.\r
The exhibitions are sponsored by the China Academy of Art and the China Federation of Literary and Art Circles (Hangzhou Committee), with organizational support from the Museum of Contemporary Art at the China Academy of Art, the Lanting Calligraphy Association (Hangzhou Committee), and the China Calligraphers Association (Hangzhou Committee). The "Writing Non-Writing" (Shu · Feishu 书·非书) exhibitions have taken place in multiple editions, including 2005, 2010 (tentative), 2015, and 2019, with the latter titled "Writing and Non-Writing: Hangzhou International Modern Calligraphy Festival" (Shu · Feishu: 2019 Hangzhou Xiandai Shufa Yishu Jie 书·非书：2019杭州国际现代书法艺术节)."""@en ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1025>,
