    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1092> ;
    ns1:description """"Chinese Clothes NO.05-D02" (Zhongguo fuzhuang 中国服装NO.05-D02) from the series "Chinese Clothes" was realized by Wang Tiande in 2004. In this work the artist explores the intersection of traditional Chinese clothing motifs and contemporary artistic expression. Wang combines the aesthetics of traditional garments (Hanfu 汉服), with his signature technique involving ink, cigarettes, and incense sticks.  Wang’s layering of ink and paper in the series "Chinese Clothes" obscures individual characters, while the vivid physical traces of the artist assert the primacy of the creative process and the object’s materiality.  Wang developed this method after accidentally dropping ash onto paper while lighting a cigarette in his studio and noticing the resulting perforations. For him, this process resembles "burning" information onto digital drives, which inspired the title of the series. This technique highlights the fragility and vulnerability of the medium, reminding us that much of Chinese culture is preserved through an inherently delicate medium, and that our grasp of past traditions is similarly elusive.\r
\r
"""@en ;
