    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1081> ;
    ns2:P580 "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P582 "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1083.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """The series "Chinese Clothes" (Zhongguo fuzhuang xilie 中国服装系列) is a collection of artworks including clothes crafted by Wang Tiande in 2004.  This collection juxtaposes traditional Chinese garment with contemporary artistic expression, emphasizing burn marks and the artist's use of gestural movements of ink evoking small forests, mountains and other natural elements on traditional Chinese clothes (Hanfu 汉服), such as qipao 旗袍 , made of silk. The main significance of this series consists of inviting viewers to reconsider traditional motifs within a modern context, provoking new ways of contemplation and facilitating a dialogue between past and present, tradition and innovation, reconsidering the Chinese cultural identity and artistic expression. The series consists of several clothes, including Chinese clothes No. 05-D02 (中国服装 No. 05-D02), Chinese clothes No. 04-D01 (中国服装 No. 04-D01), \r
The pieces of the series "Chinese Clothes" are made of silk cloth, burn marks and Chinese ink, and were displayed during the exhibition "Redolent of Incense" held in Vancouver 2005."""@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/1083.jpg> ;
