    ns2:P664 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3649109> ;
    ns1:description """ "Boundary of Freedom - Chinese Contemporary Ink" is an itinerant exhibition organized by Taihe Art Space. The first three exhibitions of the "Boundary of Freedom" series were hosted by Li Xianting, while the fourth exhibition was hosted by Fan Di'an. For the fifth exhibition, Wang Chunchen served as the Chinese curator, and Adriano Màdaro served as the Italian curator. This series of exhibitions reflects the diverse perspectives and practices within contemporary Chinese ink art.\r
The Exhibition "Boundary of Freedom - Chinese Contemporary Ink towards Europe" (Ziyou de chidu - Zhongguo dangdai shuimo zouxiang Ouzhou 自由的尺度-中国当代水墨走向欧洲) is the "fifth  round exhibition" of the series "Boundary of Freedom - Chinese Contemporary Ink" and was held in Ca' dei Carraresi, Treviso-Italy, from the 2nd of June 2018 to the 2nd of July 2018. With this exhibition Ca' dei Carraresi served as a venue for cultural exchanges and dialogues, enhancing visitors' understanding of contemporary Chinese ink art within the European context. A total of twenty-eight artists participated in this exhibition, representing various fields of contemporary Chinese ink with a range of artworks, from traditional ink paintings to experimental and multimedia installations.  Artists can be broadly categorized into three groups: i) artists who demonstrate contemporary calligraphic expressions emerging from elements of Chinese culture and art, such as Wang Dongling 王冬龄, Qiu Zhenzhong 邱振中, Zhang Dawo 张大我, and Chen Guangwu 陈光武; ii) artists who blend Eastern ink aesthetics with Western abstract expressionism, such as Ji Zi 姬子, Liu Zijian 刘子建, Zheng Lianjie 郑连杰, and Hou Shanhui 侯珊瑚; iii) artists who derive their contemporary art from Daoist or Zen Buddhist philosophies, such as Fan Zhou 樊洲, Mao Xiaolang 茅小浪, and Hei Gui 黑鬼, reflecting Taihe Art Space's consistent artistic principle of "harmony in diversity, with quality as the priority" (He er bu tong, pinzhi wei shang 和而不同，品质为尚)."""@en ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1104> .

