    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Joy in bottle (破樊笼 + seals)" ;
    ns1:description """This Calli-Writing Unit is composed of two parts: \r
1) on the left side, there's a red-stamped section containing 16 tag/seals, each bearing the names of the artists who contributed to this collaborative creation: Smer, Max, Seven, Jer, Way Fan, Blood Bro, Ogs, Andc, Spade, Thorn Donis, Goes, Kayo, Neon, Zeb Roc Ski, Abs, and Tpm. Each tag, written in red Latin letters, is encircled to resemble an ancient seal. \r
2) Next to the tag/seals, there's an inscription in bold characters that reads “Pofanlong 破樊笼” (The birdcage has disintegrated), accompanied by a description of the main characteristics of Chinese dragons. This inscription refers to the massive and fierce red Chinese dragon that spans the entire wall. The dragon seems to emerge from the text, “haunting” the wall with its presence. "Pofanlong 破樊笼" translates to "break free from the cage" in English, symbolizing liberation from confinement or limitations, and achieving freedom. In describing the Chinese dragon's main features, the text employs chengyu (four-characters idiomatic expression) such as "summon wind and rain" (hufenghuanyu 呼风唤雨) that metaphorically indicates great power and influence to control or manipulate situations, and the chengyu "wusuobuneng 无所不能"  translates to "omnipotent" or "capable of anything" that describes someone or something with limitless abilities."""@en ;
