    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Joy in bottle (有明自远方来 + seals)" ;
    ns1:description "This Calli-Writing Unit is located in the center of the artwork: on one side, there's an inscription that reads \"You ming zi yuanfang lai 有明自远方来\", followed by a list of the writers’ cities of origin, serving as a modern colophon for these traveling artists. Translated from Chinese, this inscription means: \"Some people come from afar: Beijing, Tongchuan, Chengdu, Yinzhou, Wuhan, Chongqing. Greetings from China.\" This section also includes two red tag/seals: one with the inscription \"Zhongguo 中国 (China)\" and another with the inscription \"hujian 互鉴 (mutual learning)\"."@en ;
