    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1249> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork was created during the performance \"Ferragina – Cerino Heart Sutra : The Music of the Chinese Calligraphy (塞尔维奥&亚历山得罗：心经 - 中国书法的音乐)\" which took place at the Hangzhou Conservatory on October 20, 2016. Silvio Ferragina wrote in not simplified characters and in regular script, the characters that composed the fundamental part of the Heart Sutra, namely: \"Sè bù yì kōng, kōng bù yì sè; sè jí shì kōng, kōng jí shì sè色不異空，空不異色； 色即是空，空即是色\" (Form is no different from emptiness, emptiness is no different from form, form is just such emptiness, emptiness is just such a form). The characters are written from top to bottom and from right to left. The four fundamental characters that emerge are precisely \"色不異空\" which highlight the formulation of the doctrine of \"emptiness\" (or literally: \"emptiness\") or the insubstantiality (or intrinsic non-existence) of all phenomena."@en ;
