    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1307.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "\"Three One Three Ten One\" is one of the artworks included in \"Word Series\" (1988-1989) by Qiu Zhenzhong. In this particular artwork he transcribes the polysyllabic entries—three- and four-syllable compounds— listed under the word  “triangle” (sanjiao 三角) in the Hanyu Da Cidian (Comprehensive Chinese Word Dictionary). Each word begins with the same root but follows a divergent, often unrelated, semantic path. The characters are arranged horizontally with a free spatial disposition, breaking from the vertical structure of traditional calligraphy. By doing so, Qiu Zhenzhong emphasizes the visual rhythm of repetition and the dissonance of disconnected meanings, transforming lexicographic content into a conceptual and spatial artwork." ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850> ;
