    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1425.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "“XL: S 05”  is one of the 25 panels from Feng Mengbo’s “XL” series (2009), presented in the small format (50 x 50 cm). Drawing inspiration from 1-bit pixel art, the series includes \"classical works of brush painting and calligraphy reduced to one-bit form, the smallest amount of information processed by computer software, the most primitive possible code, and silkscreened onto silver-leaf panels\" (Solomon 2010). In “XL: S 05”, the artist transforms the complex calligraphic forms (Chinese characters and seals) of the opening section of \"Cursive Calligraphy of Four Ancient Poems\" (Gu shi si tie 古诗四帖) by Zhang Xu 张旭 (685–759) into an abstract composition of reduced printed black pixels on a surface made of silkscreen print on silver leaf. Using extreme digital reduction, the artist replaces the classical aesthetics of brushstrokes and seals into pixelated forms. This reinterpretation of the methods of ancient literati within the logic of the digital age creates a new visual syntax that, while nearly illegible, retains the essence and spirit (shenyun 神韵) of the original cursive script and bridges the gap between classical Chinese art, digital art, and contemporary media." ;
