    ns1:description """Since 2004 with the on-going project Book from the Ground, Xu Bing have realized texts that everyone in the world can understand using public symbols. The artist emphasize the disconnection between the new generation with new globalized forms of expressions, such as symbols, emojis, memes, etc. In this artwork, Xu Bing translates the "Orchid Pavilion Preface" (Lanting ji xu 兰亭集序) in this visual way displayed through multicolor screen prints on 8 birch wood panels  measuring 145 x 100 x 2.4 cm. As declared in his article in Wechat (2022), "while viewers may not be used to this yet, this unfamiliarity introduces a new "element of thought" to conventional thinking, which is precisely the intention of this artwork. This enables a better understanding of our traditional culture as well as contemporary culture."  Xu Bing also highlights the semiotic relationship between calligraphy and pictographic art, suggesting that they share a common origin in symbolic communication.\r
""" ;
