    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 2 Sound MAP (signs)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the artwork created by Luo Qi during the performance “Sound MAP (Musicalligraphy Augmented Performance)”, that was held on 12 October 2023 at the “International Museum and Library of Music” in Bologna during the opening of the exhibition “Sounds of Ink: Luo Qi and 30 Years of Calligraphyism” (12 October – 5 November 2023). It consists of the translation of the music the artist heard during the performance into concatenations of calligraphic signs inspired by the oldest Chinese musical notation system, the “Dunhuang musical score” (Dunhuang qupu 敦煌曲谱). Most of Dunhuang musical scores are very simple Chinese characters or component parts  characters. The artist reshaped these signs according to his personal and original interpretation and transforming it into a “visual and visible musical score,” strongly rhythmic and dynamic, with an inextricably calligraphic thread. The music that inspired the work was improvisational music played by pianist Giusy Caruso, who was in turn inspired by the calligrapher's gestures. " ;
