    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q60> ;
    ns1:description "Yin Mei was born in the city of Zhenjiang, Jiangsu province. She is a category-defying director, choreographer, and performance artist, now based in New York City. She began her professional career in traditional Chinese dance during the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976), joining a leading regional dance company at the age of thirteen. She was trained in Chinese court and folk dance, Peking Opera, martial arts, Taiji, and other traditional Asian dance forms. Arrived in the USA in 1985, Yin Mei desires to express and discover herself. While studying at New York University, she encounters various forms of contemporary dance, following famous teachers such as Ohad Naharin,  and the modern dance scholar and critic Deborah Jowitt (b.1934).  Since from 1990s, Yin Mei starts to collaborate with a lot of artists to create works and in 1995, she finally creates her company: the Yin Mei Dance."@en ;
