    ns2:P812 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q106371273> ;
    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5826> ;
    ns1:description """IRON, a graffiti artist based in Xi'an, combines his expertise in traditional Chinese calligraphy with contemporary Gothic influences to create a unique style known as "Modern Gothichinese Calligraffiti (Zhongwen Gete Shufa 中文哥特书法)." Graduating from the Xi'an Academy of Fine Arts, IRON has developed a career as both a tattoo artist and a graffiti writer. His work primarily focuses on the fusion of Chinese characters with Western Gothic aesthetics, highlighting the distinct possibilities of Chinese as a language of expression in urban art.\r
IRON began his graffiti journey in 2009, vividly recalling the thrill and nervousness of his first spray-paint experience. His early work was a reflection of youthful rebellion and emotional release. Over time, he honed his technique, not seeing technical skills as the primary challenge but rather as something that evolves with time and practice.\r
His style is defined by its focus on Chinese wildstyle and modern Gothic calligraphy, often incorporating words that convey his current emotions, personal messages, or lines from his favorite poems. For IRON, language serves as both a tool and a cultural bridge, creating links between traditional Chinese characters and the visual elements of Western Gothic styles.\r
He emphasizes that "Chinese graffiti style" is shaped by the cultural and linguistic logic inherent in Chinese characters, which goes beyond mere decorative elements. His approach values thought and creativity, aiming to stimulate both the mind and the visual senses. IRON appreciates the regional variations in graffiti styles worldwide, such as the contrasts between American and European graffiti, and within different areas of the United States.\r
If he were to define his artistic approach, he would label it as "Modern Gothichinese Calligraffiti," emphasizing a style that blends tradition with innovation while highlighting the unique characteristics of Chinese script."""@en ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "School"@en,
        "Self-Taught"@en ;
    ns1:hasTag "IRON"@en,
        "鐵"@zh,
        "Tiě"@zh-Latn .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1687> a ns3:Q17514 ;
    ns2:P1476 "X-Evolution"@en ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1685> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q12559209>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q170406>,
