<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1743> a ns3:Q7725310 ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8686>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q90> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Digital (数码)"@en,
        "数码"@zh,
        "Shùmǎ"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1081> ;
    ns2:P580 "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description """The inspiration for the creation of the series of works titled "Shuma" (2002-ongoing) originated from the theme of the exhibition “Zero: Material Art Exhibition” (Ling: cailiao yishuzhan 零·材料艺术展) held in Paris in the autumn of 2002.  While smoking in his studio, the artist accidentally dropped cigarette ash onto a sheet of rice paper, which slowly burned by the residual heat. The resulting burns left traces that revealed additional patterns. Wang, then, started to explore the expressive and desctructive potential of fire as a tool for mark-making in an entire series of works, titled "Digital", in which ink and burns interact to create layered compositions. \r
Each work of this series typically consists of two or more sheets of xuan paper layered one atop the other. The bottom sheet is inscribed with Chinese characters and fragmented legible texts. These inscriptions may include both Chinese characters and Latin letters in a multilingual text order with inverted orientations or flipped structures of characters and letters, creating a multilingual visual field. In some cases, there is an  incorporation of Chinese landscape painting elements (shanshui hua 山水画). The upper sheet is made of semi-translucent paper, on which an inscription using cigarette ash or incense is made, echoing calligraphic strokes. This second layer is overlapped on the first layer revealing "flickering glimpses of the inked and uninked surfaces that are otherwise only dimly visible below" (Hearn 2014: 61) creating an expressive interplay of light and shadow, enriching the ink's depth and the transparency of the characters. The title "Shuma" translates to "digital" and reflects how the various layers convey diverse visual information, in a similar way to the gathering and transmission of data in digital systems. \r
According to the artist, this process "resemble that of burning information onto DVDs and digital divres ― hence the title of this series. Appropriately, each work is identified using letters and digits that resemble a serial number or computer code to give the date, format, and number within the series. Thus, Digital No. 02HP01-03 may be read as 2002: hanging paintings one through three" (Hearn 2014: 61).\r
In the exhibition "Tiande Remanufacturing" (Tiande zai zhizao 天德再制造), the curator Zheng Shengtian 郑胜天 , through an analysis of numerous historical allusions, explored the cultural background to illustrate the power of words and the religious consciousness associated with the incineration of written paper.""" ;
    ns1:includesArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1744> .

