    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Sound MAP  (水墨声音)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the long scroll written by the calligrapher Luo Qi during the musicalligraphy performance title “Sound MAP (Musicalligraphy Augmented Performance)”, that was held on 12 October 2023 at the “International Museum and Library of Music” in Bologna during the opening of the exhibition “Sounds of Ink: Luo Qi and 30 Years of Calligraphyism” (12 October – 5 November 2023). This CWU is composed of the four characters \"shuimo shengyin 水墨声音\" (Sounds of Ink), that represent the Chinese title of the exhibition. The artist wrote the characters from left to right using his personal style, that is a creative mix of running script (xingshu 行书) and a particular form of clerical script (lishu 隶书) used during the Han dynasty (206 BC -220 AD). During the execution, the scroll came directly out of the piano and the characters represent a visual translation of the sounds produced by the instrument. "@en ;
