    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/943> ;
    ns1:description "This artwork was created during the concert entitled \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会)\", an event commissioned by the Chinese government to honour the Summer Olympic Games. To honour this partnership, Li Binquan realizes the phrase “Yingguo Zhongguo youyi wangguchangqing 英国中国友谊万古长青” (Britain-China Friendship will Last Forever) together with the Professor Roger Mason (b.1941) : the first part “Yingguo Zhongguo youyi 英国中国友谊” (Britain-China Friendship) was written by Roger Mason, while the second part “wangguchangqing 万古长青” (will last forever) was written by Li Binquan."@en ;
