    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1925> ;
    ns2:P941 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/187> ;
    ns1:description "From December 12, 2018, to March 29, 2019, Song Dong’s “Writing Diary with Water” (1995-2012) has been on view at the Aspinwall House in Kochi (India) as part of the Kochi-Muziris Biennale. An extension of the earlier series of the same name, “Writing Diary with Water” is housed in a glass structure surrounded by the greenery of Aspinwall House’s gardens. Inside, paintbrushes are stored in containers of water, all coloured and of different sizes and shapes. Visitors are invited to dip their paintbrushes in the water and move them freely along the translucent wall. Over time, each visitor’s trace gradually fades, until it disappears. The work, according to the artist, is about the “inherent impermanence” of the world."@en ;
