    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns1:description """Zeng Laide was born in 1955 in Pengxi, Sichuan Province. He is currently a national first-class artist, vice president of the National Academy of Painting of China, executive director of the Calligraphy and Seal Cutting Institute, and a member of the Academy's Art Committee. He is also a council member of the China Calligraphers Association and its Education Committee chairman, as well as president of the World Chinese Business Painting and Calligraphy Institute. After studying under calligrapher Hu Gongshi 胡公石 (1912－1997) in the 1980s, Zeng developed a unique style that blends tradition with innovation, combining Chinese calligraphy with Western and Japanese artistic influences.\r
Zeng Laide is known for experimenting with new forms of expression, blending calligraphy with other art forms, such as music. His works have attracted significant international attention, with exhibitions in museums and galleries both in China and abroad, including a major exhibition entitled "The Music of Ink at the British Museum" held in London in 2005 (see the archive). His creations are known for the bold use of the brush and ink, giving them strong visual impact and modern expression.""" ;
