    ns1:description "This artwork is part of the series \"Material Immaterial - City\". This series depicts city centers in the distance that can be seen fading into a foggy atmosphere. On this background Chu Chu incorporates calligraphy using black ink and colorful acrylic paint on photographs using Italo Calvino's “Invisible Cities” and Western poems translated into Chinese as content of the texts. In this particular piece, Chu Chu uses  black ink and white acrylic to write the Chinese translation of Percy Bysshe Shelley's \"Ode to the West Wind\". " ;
