    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2088.jpg> ;
    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Retranslation & Rewriting of Tang Poem no.1 (《相思》)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU consists of the poem \"Xiangsi 相思\" (One-Hearted) by  Wang Wei (699-759) from the Tang Dynasty (618-907). The reading of \"Retranslation & Rewriting of Tang Poem no.1\" begins with this poem, inscribed in the right section of the stele in Chinese characters, following the traditional direction from top to bottom and from right to left. In this poem, Wang Wei uses red beans as an evocative symbol to express longing and affection, highlighting the enduring power of love and remembrance. The poem is then translated into English (CWU 2). " ;
