    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 3 Retranslation & Rewriting of Tang Poem no.1 (晚作詩來...)" ;
    ns1:description "Starting from the English translation (CWU 2) of Wang Wei's poem \"One-Hearted\" (CWU 1), the artist transliterates the syllabic sounds back into Chinese. For example, “when” is transliterated into one single Chinese characters wan  晚 (\"dusk\"), selected for it phonetic proximity to the English word. This CWU occupied the stele's central section and represents the main content of the artwork due to both its central position and the larger scale of the characters. The other CWUs appear both to the right and to the left of this central text. The overall meaning diverges completely from both the original poem by Wang Wei and its English translation." ;
    ns1:directionality "Traditional" ;
