    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2356.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "\" Water of Lake Tai\" is a conceptual work by Wang Nanming. It addresses social and ecological issues in China.  The artist realized \"Water of Lake Tai\" in 2007 to record water pollution at Lake Tai, the third biggest freshwater lake in China separating Jiangsu and Zhejiang provinces. The work consists of sheets, which were drown in the green water of Lake Tai.  The artwork  was exhibited during \"Ta Yin Drought: Wang Nanming Solo Exhibition\" (2012) and it belongs to Wang's uncompleted Ecological Trilogy (Shengtai zuopin sanbu qu 生态作品三部曲)." ;
