<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2585> a ns1:DecorativeAndAppliedArt ;
    ns2:P1071 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1867> ;
    ns2:P1476 "Emptiness (無)"@en,
        "無"@zh,
        "Wú"@zh-Latn ;
    ns2:P179 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2582> ;
    ns2:P180 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3074482>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q546054>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6498317>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q67932942> ;
    ns2:P186 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q231250> ;
    ns2:P287 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/148> ;
    ns2:P462 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23445> ;
    ns2:P571 "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P608 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/150> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2585.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """The dress titled “Emptiness" (Wu 無) is realized by Tsai Yi‑Fen as part of the "From Ink to Apparel III" exhibition held in Taipei in 2018. The concept for this piece derives from the Chinese character  wu 無 (emptiness/non‑being) and translated into a garment that embodies both visual and philosophical meaning. \r
The design abstracts the flowing strokes and rhythmic energy of calligraphy into structural lines and contours, using silhouette and textile movement to evoke space and void. The bodice features a rigid, woven framework reminiscent of a net or grid, enveloping the shoulders and torso. Its architectural interlacing suggests three-dimensional calligraphic knots, while the off-shoulder cut balances the density of the upper structure. The skirt, composed of long black threads akin to fringe or filamentary fibers, cascades to the floor and beyond, generating a liquid, ethereal effect. Threads extending from the arms echo the gestures of calligraphy in motion, imparting a sense of spatial expansion even in stillness. Constructed from glossy, slightly rigid fibers—likely synthetic or treated to preserve length and movement—the bodice emphasizes texture and three-dimensionality through corded details and raised knots. A subtle red accent at the wrist introduces chromatic contrast to the predominantly black and gray palette.\r
Ultimately, “Wu 無” functions as wearable art rather than conventional ready-to-wear. The interplay between a structured, architectural upper section and flowing, ethereal fringes creates a poetic, theatrical effect, visually translating the concept of emptiness and spatial extension while engaging in a dialogue between Chinese calligraphy and contemporary fashion."""@en ;
