<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2597> a ns3:Q215627 ;
    ns2:P106 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3501317> ;
    ns2:P21 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6581072> ;
    ns2:P2561 "Polly Ho 何善恒" ;
    ns2:P27 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8646> ;
    ns2:P361 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2599> ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2595> ;
    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8646> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2597.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """Polly Ho is a Hong Kong–based fashion designer and co-founder of the brand Loom Loop, whose practice focuses on the reinterpretation of traditional Chinese textile culture within contemporary fashion design. She studied Arts and Design at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University and later continued her education at the University of Central England in Birmingham. Her work is characterized by a research-driven approach that combines heritage craftsmanship, historical fabrics, and experimental garment construction. A central aspect of her design methodology is the translation of cultural and artistic references—such as calligraphy, textile history, and material techniques—into three-dimensional forms worn on the body.\r
Educated in design in Hong Kong and the United Kingdom, Polly Ho has developed an interdisciplinary practice that moves between fashion, material research, and cultural preservation. Through Loom Loop, she has been particularly engaged in revitalizing traditional silk fabrics and artisanal processes, integrating them into modern silhouettes and conceptual collections. """@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/2597.png> ;
    ns1:isDesignerOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2589> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2599> a ns3:Q1400264 ;
    ns2:P2561 "Loom Loop 碌祿" ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8646> ;
    ns2:P527 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2597> ;
    ns2:P571 "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2595> ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.loom-loop.com/> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2599.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """Loom Loop is a Hong Kong–based fashion label founded in 2014 by designers Polly Ho and Andy Wong. The brand was established with the aim of integrating traditional Chinese textile heritage with contemporary fashion design, developing collections that reinterpret historical materials and artisanal techniques through a modern design perspective.\r
A key aspect of Loom Loop’s identity is its focus on the use and revitalization of Canton silk, also known as gambiered silk, a traditional fabric historically produced in the Guangdong region. By incorporating this material and other heritage textile processes into contemporary garments, the brand seeks to preserve and promote Chinese textile culture while adapting it to current fashion contexts and global audiences.\r
The name of the brand reflects this conceptual approach: “loom” refers to the weaving loom used in textile production, while “loop” evokes the construction process of garments and the cyclical relationship between tradition and innovation. Through this framework, Loom Loop positions craftsmanship, material research, and cultural continuity as fundamental elements of its design methodology.\r
Over the years, the brand has presented its collections on international platforms, including major fashion events and showcases promoting Hong Kong designers abroad. Through these initiatives, Loom Loop contributes to the global dissemination of contemporary fashion practices rooted in East Asian textile traditions."""@en ;
