    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/526> ;
    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/549> ;
    ns1:description """This performance takes place at the "17th Macau International Live Art Festival (MIPAF)" (Di shiqi jie Aomen guoji xianchang yishu jie 第十七届澳门国际现场艺术节 - MIPAF) on January 7, 2023. Wu Xixia and a red humanoid mannequin are kneeling facing each other, covered by a red cloth. When the cloth is lifted, the artist begins to write with a brush the white characters "human" (ren 人) and "art" (yishu 艺术) on the mannequin to "give life" to it, announcing the beginning of the confrontation. To the sound of the drums, the artist "stabs" the mannequin with the brush, leaving traces of white and red ink on the object. Each time Wu Xixia hits the mannequin, laser beams are projected onto the artist's back, until both the mannequin and the artist's body are covered with marks. At that point, the cloth is replaced and the "fall" of both sides (subject and object) marks the end of the confrontation.\r
The humanoid mannequin is an inanimate object created by industrial civilization and modern technology, while the living person represents humanity, identity, role, creation, etc. The dynamics of the act of "punching each other" through this game of parts represents the confrontation between living and non-living beings. Both sides are kneeling towards each other, in an equal position, just to represent that at the end there is no winner."""@en ;
