    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/648> ;
    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/651> ;
    ns1:description "This performance took place in 2008, when Sun Ping organized a “subversive” (dianfu xing 颠覆性) calligraphy and a workshop called “I Don’t Know” (Wo bu zhidao 不知道). On this occasion, the calligrapher Sun Ping asked his collaborator Luo Shan 罗姗 to use her vagina to “hold the brush” (zhibi 执笔) and write on paper. The content of this calligraphy is the “Orchid Pavilion Preface” (Lanting Xu 兰亭序) written in 353 by Wang Xizhi (303-361). The “vagina font” calligraphy (“Bi- ti” shufa “Bi- 体” 书法) concepted by Sun Ping 孙平 is a new way of interpreting calligraphy, using a brush specially created to be inserted into the female vagina. This type of brush is made by installing a type of sexual tool on top of the classic Chinese calligraphy brush. The installed mechanism prevents the brush from falling from the lower part of the body during the writing process. Luo Shan inserts the tool into the vagina and writes calligraphy through the movement and the tone of the lower body. When writing, the brush movements produce pleasure. Luo Shan is often half-naked and wears particular masks or costumes, as well as various accessories. "@en ;
