    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/769.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "\"Filling the World with Love\" is an iPad-based work created in 2021 by Wang Dongling and represents one of the first Chinese calligraphic works using iPad digital technologies. In this digital piece, the artist uses an Apple Pencil to transcribe the lyrics of the famous song \"Rang shijie chongman ai 让世界充满爱\" (Fill the World with Love) by Guo Feng 郭峰 (b. 1986) over a detail of the Mona Lisa image by Leonardo da Vinci. Guo Feng is a prominent Chinese pop singer and composer active since the 1980s, and the song, released in 1986, became an emblematic hymn to peace and collective harmony in post-Mao China. The combination/juxtaposition of the lyrics from one of the earliest Chinese pop songs, a hymn to universal peace, with a famous Western painting functions as a manifesto of intercultural unity, articulating art as a shared aesthetic language across traditions and cultures. The work also reflects a shift in the medium of calligraphic practice. Instead of ink, brush, and paper, the artist employs a tablet interface and a digital pen. These technological devices reinforce how Chinese calligraphy, and its aesthetic logic, can articulate meaning even within the digital age."@en ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850>,
