    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 3 Cursive - Multiple Projected Traditional Calligraphies (unknown)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the dancing performance \"Cursive\". It is a series of traditional calligraphies projected as a slideshow in the background during the various performances of the dancers: calligraphies by Wang Xizhi 王羲之 (303–361), Huai Su 怀素 (737–799), Zhang Xu 张旭 (fl. 8th century) and other famous masters of past dynasties are presented to the audience in large scale, merging with the movements of the dancers in the foreground floor. According to the video of the performance, in total there are about twenty-one frame changes of traditional calligraphic works projected throughout the ballet. "@en ;
