    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 4 Cursive ( 《离骚 》)" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the dancing performance \"Cursive\". It is a freeze frame calligraphy which was projected during the performance. It consists of a beitie 碑帖 (a rubbing of an inscribed script on stone) of the white cursive words on a black background reproducing the poem entitled “Li Sao 离骚” (Encountering Sorrow) realized by Mi fu 米芾 (1051–1107). This is an ancient Chinese poem from the anthology Chuci traditionally attributed to Qu Yuan 屈原 (c. 340 – 278). "@en ;
