    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/741> ;
    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1589> ;
    ns1:description """This performance took place on January, 13 2008 at the Florida Gulf Coast University, during the inauguration of the exhibition “I Am in It: Contemporary Chinese Art Expression” (Zi you wo zai: Zhongguo dangdai yishu biaoxian 自有我再：中国当代艺术表现). The band composed of three guitarists students of the Gulf Coast University of Florida, play the music from the repertoire of George Gershwin and Edward Rizzo.  Pu Lieping writes on a roll of paper with brushes of different sizes and soaked in black ink. The calligraphic lines are almost very thin and "vibrate" to the sound of the music during execution, almost as if they were creating a musical score.\r
On January 12, 2008 Pu Lieping, the day before the performance, inspired by the music composed by the three students of the Gulf Coast University in Florida, made a preparatory draft on a wrapping paper from the Polo Ralph Lauren brand. The characters, which are broken down and created with a pen, are inspired by the inscriptions on oracle bones. These characters are: shui 水 (water) zhi 止 (to/only) mu 木 (wood) 目 (eye). Animal figures can also be glimpsed in the work, such as deer heads. The lines that make up the draft can be both vertical and horizontal, as if to reproduce the movements of the elements of nature."""@en ;
