    ns2:P580 "2017-08-12"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P582 "2017-11-12"^^xsd:date ;
    ns1:description """"Wang Dongling: The Bamboo Path" (Wang Dongling: Zhu jing 王冬龄：竹径) was held in August 2017 at the OCT-Contemporary Art Terminal (OCAT) Shenzhen Pavilion (OCAT深圳馆艺术个展), in Halls A and B of OCAT Loft in Shenzhen.  The exhibition consisted of three distinct parts:\r
- Hall A featured an immersive installation with 201 five-meter-tall green bamboo stalks inscribed with Wang Dongling's calligraphy. The warehouse-shaped space was transformed into a bamboo grove, lending the exhibition its title.\r
- Hall B showcased a large-scale calligraphy work in "chaos script" on paper (8.4 x 5.5 m). The artist vertically inscribed excerpts from poems by Ruan Ji and Ji Kang, creating a piece that, when displayed on the wall, resembled a majestic waterfall. Also in Hall B, Wang exhibited 100 pieces of ink abstraction along with a video documenting his calligraphic process.\r
Throughout the exhibition, bamboo served as the primary medium for Wang's calligraphic expressions. Additionally, transparent propylene panels inscribed with white acrylic paint were interspersed among the bamboo stalks. This interplay between calligraphy and bamboo invited viewers to experience a dynamic dialogue between art and nature as they wandered through the grove."""@en ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/910> .

