    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q956> ;
    ns1:description """Chen Guangwu is a prominent Chinese artist. Born in Guangxi, 1967, Chen's artistic journey began at a young age, driven by a passion for traditional Chinese art forms. Trained at the [Name of Academy], Chen's artistic vision merges traditional calligraphy with contemporary sensibilities, resulting in dynamic and expressive artworks that push the boundaries of the art form. Chen Guangwu's artworks have been exhibited extensively both in China and internationally, garnering acclaim for their innovation and artistic vision. Through a diverse range of materials and techniques, from traditional ink brushwork to experimental digital methods, Chen creates compositions that captivate viewers and challenge conventional perceptions of Chinese calligraphy. His works often feature abstract and experimental elements, exploring concepts of movement, space, and form within the realm of calligraphic expression.\r
Chen Guangwu's innovative exploration of repetition, layering (overwriting, rewriting), and deconstruction forms the core of his creative process. The essence of Chen's artworks can also be divided into these three main categories (Iezzi 2014, p. 439-440): i) the repetition of a single character until space saturation, ii) the layering of different words overlaid, and iii) the breakdown of characters into their component parts, followed by their multiple reiterations. """@en ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "School"@en ;
