    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1250.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "Silvio Ferragina created the Heart Sutra work on 10 panels made of rice paper. The work was created in Milan in 2016 to be used as a backdrop for the performance performed with Alessandro Cerino entitled: \"Heart Sutra – The Music of Chinese Calligraphy: Brush and Flute Musicalligraphy Project (中国书法的音乐: 心经)\" which took place at the Hangzhou Conservatory. The characters are all those of the Heart Sutra, 268 in total and are made in seal script. The four fundamental characters that emerge very large are precisely \"sè bù yì kōng 色不異空\" which highlight the formulation of the doctrine of \"emptiness\" (or literally: \"emptiness\") or the insubstantiality (or intrinsic non-existence) of all phenomena."@en ;
