    ns2:P170 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1096> ;
    ns2:P580 "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "Xu Bing has designed a calligraphic system known as \"Square Word Calligraphy\" (Yingwen fangkuaizi shufa 英文方块字书法) or \"New English Calligraphy\" (Xin Yingwen shufa 新英文书法), in which English (or other languages) words are visually reconfigured to resemble Chinese characters. Like a linguistic hybridizer, the artist combines Chinese calligraphy with English writing to create a new “species”. However, this system differs from the nonsensical characters in \"Book from the Sky\", which generate feelings of suspicion and confusion in the viewer. In contrast, when encountering Square Word Calligraphy, these tensions are quickly resolved through the recognition that the work contains “real” (readable) text. Through this process, Xu Bing effectively introduces a novel Eastern art form into the Western cultural sphere. It transcends conventional distinctions between Chinese and English, reshaping conceptual and perceptual norms and challenging the very foundation of cognition. After developing this lettering system, Xu Bing extended the project into an installation format, modeling it on adult literacy classes within the exhibition space. He also added a textbook, an instructional video, and practice sheets, replicating pedagogical materials used in classroom environments." ;
