    ns1:description "Zhu Qingsheng was born 1957, Zhenjiang, Jiangsu Province, China. He is an influential art historian, critic, and artist. He holds a PhD from Heidelberg University and is the President of the International Association of Art History (CIHA). He is a Professor at Peking University, where he also directs the Center for Visual Studies (CVS) and the Han Art Institution (HAI). Additionally, he serves as Editor of the Annual of Contemporary Art of China and leads the \"Chinese Modern Art\" initiative. His work bridges the fields of art history, curation, and contemporary Chinese art." ;
