    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1633> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork was created during the first part of the performance "Sound MAP (Musicalligraphy Augmented Performance)" held on October 12, 2023 at the International Musuem and Library of Music in Bologna during the opening of the exhibition “Sounds of Ink: Luo Qi and 30 Years of Calligraphyism” (12 October – 5 November 2023). This artwork is composed of two parts: in the first part the artist wrote the four characters of the Chinese title of the exhibition (shuimo shengyin 水墨声音 "sounds of ink") using his persoanl style, while in the scond part he translated the music he heard during the performance (played by the pianist Giusy Caruso)  into concatenations of calligraphic signs inspired by the oldest Chinese musical notation system, the “Dunhuang musical score”. The result is a visual and visible musical score, strongly rhythmic and dynamic, with an inextricably calligraphic thread.\r
"""@en ;
