    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/635> ;
    ns1:description "“I” (Wo 我) is one of the first calligraphic performances realized by Wu Xixia in Macau. During this performance, the artist is inside an airtight inflatable sphere symbolizing the female uterus. In the inner part of the sphere, she starts to write with red ink and in regular script some labels of society’s goodwill and malice towards women, such as: “whore” (biao zi 婊子); “old maid” (lao chunü 老处女); “good wife and loving mother” (xian qiliang mu 贤妻良母); “green tea bitch” (luchabiao 绿茶婊); “teenage girl” (yunü 玉女); “white lotus” (bailian hua 白莲花), etc.  As a female, she has been questioning her gender, and the social labels she writes about are an attempt to reconcile herself with her gender identity. Wu Xixia reflects on various questions about her life, such as: “Who are women? And who am I? Is my gender determined by birth or is it given by society? There is a womb here, but where is the ‘mother’?”. For Wu Xixia, this performance represents a meditative act of reconciliation with herself, as well as a way to metaphorically return to the peace of the maternal womb. "@en ;
