    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/526> ;
    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/639> ;
    ns1:description "This performance was held in 2021 in Macau, in front of a building called “Darling”. The building was covered with red ribbons, which spread all the way to an airtight inflatable ball where Wu Xixia is “trapped”. She stars writing expressions such as: “jiu jiu wo 救救我” (help me); “qiuqiu ni 求求你” (I beg you); “bie sha wo 别杀我” (don’t kill me); “bie S wo 别S我” (don’t fuck me), etc. with red ink inside the hermetic sphere. During the performance, passers-by, especially men, took photos with various poses and angles nearby. In this “public act”, the female body transforms into an object of desire and “objectification” through the male gaze. For over 40 minutes, the artist lies still on the ground, inviting the audience's scrutiny while she begins to write down pleas for help. Red colour serves as a symbol of judgment, and the red ribbon represents the tangible reality of the female body being observed. The building covered with red ribbons symbolize the existing and massive examination of the female body. The artist wraps the red ribbon of the building on the inflatable ball, representing the current situation of women who are looking at fearlessly and pursuing physical freedom, but it is still difficult to escape from the scrutiny. In the past, the female body has always been hidden. Nowadays, with the awakening of female consciousness, women break free from the shackles and turn from invisibility to openness and fearless publicity. In this transition, the female body is no longer a private and invisible object but exposed to the public eye. This performance aims to arouse people’s attention to the predicament of women breaking “free from physical examination” (wuwei shenshi 无畏审视)."@en ;
