    ns2:P664 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1034>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1071> ;
    ns1:description """The exhibition "Shu Fei Shu — 2010 Hangzhou International Modern Calligraphy Art Exhibition" opened at the China Academy of Art Museum. \r
This exhibition, led by artists from the Modern Calligraphy Research Center at the China Academy of Art, marked its second edition. The title "Shu Fei Shu" (书非书), meaning "Calligraphy as Non-Calligraphy," indicated its cross-disciplinary nature, blending calligraphy with other art forms like fashion, installation, sculpture, and architecture. Featuring works by 100 renowned artists from 14 countries and regions, including the United States, Japan, France, Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan, the exhibition showcased innovative approaches to traditional calligraphy. Over 100 pieces incorporating calligraphic elements spanned various fields, including calligraphy, painting, fashion design, architecture, music, and dance. It challenged conventional definitions of calligraphy, demonstrating its limitless possibilities in modern life.""" ;
    ns1:exhibitedArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1428>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2002> .

