    ns1:description """"Eye Charts" consists of two large panels featuring optometric-style charts composed of characters using two newly-designed computer fonts, named "Feng's Bitmap" (Dianzhenfeng 点阵冯) and "Feng's Vector" (Shiliangfeng 矢量冯). In the first one the characters are pixel-based reduced, while in the second one they are reduced to gentle lines based on vectors and mathematical formulas. The reduction of characters is based on 'stone flowers' (shihua 石花). These 'stone flowers' are rubbings made from eroded or damaged steles that show white marks where the stones or inscriptions had been before, often rendering the characters illegible. Feng Mengbo chose to revive the stone flowers to preserve them in an artistic digital remediation. Adopting digital tools to accelerate the aging process of characters of stone rubbings, the artist reduces the fonts to their most essential forms, placing them on the edge between readability and unreadability.  \r
The artist explores the notions of distortion and the inversion of reality. In a deliberate paradox, the larger the characters appear, the less legible they become; the smaller they are, the clearer they read. Through this inversion, Feng challenges conventional perception and questions the reliability of visual systems. The artwork thus becomes a meditation on how digital logic, based on quantification, scaling, and code, reshapes our perception between visibility and abstraction.""" ;
