<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2530> a ns3:Q1400264 ;
    ns2:P2561 "Biface Graphy 双面书法" ;
    ns2:P276 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148> ;
    ns2:P453 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/367> ;
    ns2:P527 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/100>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/361> ;
    ns2:P571 "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns2:P800 <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/370> ;
    ns1:description """Biface Graphy is an artistic collective and calligraphic practice founded by Zhang Qiang and Lia Wei. Operating between calligraphy, performance, and installation, the collective develops projects ranging from performative writing sessions to large-scale spatial and landscape interventions.\r
Rooted in the Literati tradition as a shared mode of practice, Biface Graphy conceives calligraphy as a relational process rather than a linguistic one. The two artists write simultaneously on opposite sides of a vertically suspended, translucent scroll, using brushes and ink. The resulting script is intentionally unreadable and emerges from the interaction of gestures, pressure, and movement rather than from premeditated characters.\r
The scroll and its supporting structure function as an abstract “machine” that generates a continuous visual language, where form and content coincide. Over time, the collective’s practice evolved toward greater fluidity and spontaneity, giving rise to an emergent shared language shaped by mutual awareness and performative interaction.\r
Through the “Open Scroll” installations, Biface Graphy extends calligraphy beyond the studio into architectural and natural environments, redefining it as a spatial, performative, and collective art form.""" ;
    ns1:isCalligrapherOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/367> .

