    ns1:description """In this performance Qiu Zhijie writes  inversely ten poems from the Tang Dynasty (618-907). The poems are written from left to right and from bottom to the top. Every stroke order is also written inversely.\r
Playing a video of the performance backward, the poems are erased as they are written, turning calligraphy into an "anti-calligraphy". The video is part of an installation where the ten calligraphies of the Tang poems  written on paper hung on the wall of the exhibition room, create a paradoxical relationship with the video."""@en ;
