    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/100> ;
    ns1:description """In this four-hour performance, Zhang Qiang writes on sheets of paper and on geometric shapes made of white chalk. The artist is seen from behind and never looks at where he paints, while the female British counterpart named Sophia Huist conveys the artist's movements. She moves the paper or objects on which Zhang Qiang is working, thus shattering, or deconstructing his work. After being used for the performance, these geometric shapes will be also used for an installation. The performance is accompanied by a recorded traditional Chinese music played with the guqin 古琴 (a plucked seven-string Chinese musical instrument). \r
About the performance, Zhang Qiang says: "The aim of this performance is looking for our spiritual, entire, honest and beautiful language. I don't know if I have this ability or not, but I try looking for it together with painters all over the world. This is not a work for only one person, this is a humanity work". (Barrass 2002: 256-259)\r
This performance is part of the series "Zhang Qiang's Traceology A/B Model (Zhang Qiang zongji xue  A/B moxing 张强踪迹学 A/B 模型, 1990-2000). """@en ;
