    ns1:description "These artworks (n. 51, 52 and 53) are created during the performance \"Free Cloud Calligraphy (云自在书)\". In this performance, Zhang Qiang creates the so-called \"Blinded Calligraphy\" (mang shu 盲书): looking away, the artist holds up an ink-soaked brush, creating traces of ink while the female counterpart Ding Feifei 丁斐斐 moves a sheet of paper or silk over his head, as if to simulate the movement of clouds in the sky. "@en ;
