    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/522> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork is created during the performance "Writing the Orchid Pavilion Preface One Time (Shuxie Lanting Xu yibian 书写兰亭序一遍)" held in Macau in 2021.  It is an airtight plastic sphere on which Wu Xixia writes inside the “Orchid Pavilion Preface” composed by Wang Xizhi 王羲之 (303–361) in 353. During the writing process, the different forms of the twenty zhi 之 characters present in the poem, which have always been praised and imitated by all Chinese calligraphers, were replaced with visible red ink male phalluses. The character zhi 之, as a symbol of order, represents the "authority" (quanwei 权威).\r
This artwork then became part of the installation held in Beijing in 2021 called "Her Mountain" (Ta shan 她山) in which Wu Xixia creates a "mountain of blood" full of symbols linked to childbirth and the female womb (such as some foetuses lying in red wedges) to talk about gender issues in contemporary society."""@en ;
