    ns1:description "This is the artwork realized during the performance \"I\" (Wo 我) and then leaving as an installation in the exhibition space where the performance was held. This artwork was then used as part of the installation \"Her Mountain\" (Ta shan 她山) exposed in Beijing in 2021 in occasion of the \"Wu  Xixia Personal Art Exhibition\" (Wu Xixia ge zhan 吴析夏个展 - December 6 to 20, 2021) at the Song Yang Art Museum (Song Yang meishu guan 宋洋美术馆). In this artwork, Wu Xixia reconciles personal identity and gender and carries out a reflection on women and herself, writing the labels of society’s goodwill and malice towards women with red ink, such as \"whore\" (biao zi 婊子) \"old maid\" (lao chunu 老处女), \"good wife and loving mother\" (xian qiliang mu 贤妻良母), \"green tea bitch\" (luchabiao 绿茶婊), \"teenage girl\" (yunu 玉女), \"white lotus\" (bailian hua 白莲花), etc. She answers questions such as: \"Who are women? And who am I? Is my gender determined by birth or is it given by society? There is a womb here, but where is the \"mother\"?\". Having been rejected by her family at the time of her birth as a female, she has been questioning her gender throughout her formative years, and the social labels she writes about are an attempt to reconcile herself with her gender identity."@en ;
