    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/730.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """Commissioned by Hermès and developed in collaboration with Fu Qiumeng Fine Art, this piece from the “Les Poèmes du Mandarin” collection by Hermès is a white ceramic plate featuring the full text of Li Bai’s poem "Invitation to Wine" (Jiang jin jiu 将进酒)  written by Fung Mingchip in non-simplified characters. The calligraphy is rendered in subtle shades of black and grey with delicate platinum accents to evoke the effect of freshly applied, wet ink, and punctuated with small red seals carved by the artist. The calligraphy was first created freehand on traditional rice paper and later digitally adapted by the design studio to fit the ceramic surface. The writing reflects a personal style inspired by xingkai (semi-cursive script), reinterpreted on a reduced and carefully controlled scale. The strokes are exceptionally delicate, at times resembling fine hatchings, giving the script a highly unconventional and experimental quality compared to traditional calligraphic norms. The composition transforms each character into a visual rhythm, highlighting both the expressive potential of the brush and the artist’s innovative approach to classical Chinese calligraphy.\r
The plate is presented inside Hermès’ iconic square orange box, emphasizing the combination of classical Chinese poetry with the brand’s contemporary luxury aesthetic. The subtle, almost ethereal quality of the calligraphy, together with the pristine white ceramic, transforms the functional object into a work of art, highlighting both the beauty of the literary text and the innovative approach to calligraphy."""@en ;
