    ns1:derivesFrom <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/878> ;
    ns1:description "This visual artwork is a digital calligraphic piece by Wang Dongling, created with the technical support of Gao Lu. It was realized for the Retrospective Exhibition “From Inception: Wang Dongling 60 Years of Calligraphy” (Hangzhou, 2021). The title and the content derive from the first chapter of the Zhuangzi,  titled “Wandering Beyond\" (Xiaoyao you 逍遥游). This text has been written several times by the artist, but in this work it is rendered for the first time through the Virtual Reality technology. Wang Dongling merges his distinctive \"Chaos Script” (luanshu 乱书) with digitally generated brushstrokes, which are continuously emerge, interwine, and dissolve. As Gao (2021, 350) notes, \"the 'chaos' of 'Chaos-Writing' consists in its penetrating through calligraphy's state of torpor with the power of confusion and disorder, in its focus on the essence of the inner structure and 'openness' of writing itself, in bringing back to life the original, generative power of calligraphy.\"  This  work represents a three-dimensional trace of embodied gestural movements, rather than a fixed inscription. Traditional calligraphic materials and tools such as paper, ink, and brush are replaced by digital and technological tools, producing virtual and immaterial brushstrokes that expand calligraphy into spatial experience. It is important to note that the artwork is not authored solely by the calligrapher, as in pre-digital  practices. Instead, it emerges through collaborative processes involving engineers and technical producers. The work therefore exemplifies distributed authorship and the hybridization of artistic and technological expertise."@en ;
