    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/750> ;
    ns1:description """The digital artwork entitled "Virtual Reality Calligraphy: Wandering Beyond" was created by Wang Dongling for his retrospective exhibition, titled “From Inception: Wang Dongling 60 Years of Calligraphy (从头开始 ——王冬龄书法艺术60年)”. The artist uses a full-body motion capture system (quanshen dongzuo buzhuo xitong 全身动作捕捉系统), consisting of a motion capture suit (mo-cap suit), to create a digital work in augmented reality. This wearable device records the body movements of the person, which are converted  into data by the system.  In particular, Wang uses motion-capturing gloves to capture the body movement trajectory of his writing.  Gao Lu 高路, Professor at the China Academy of Art, generated several videos adopted different parameters to create videos with different colors and sizes of Wang's calligraphy. The writing of this VR visual artwork is based on the first chapter of Zhuangzi, "Wandering Beyond" (Xiaoyao you 逍遥游), written in the artist's iconic Chaos Script (luanshu 乱书).  In this style, lines of no more or hardly legible characters cross each other in a three-dimensional space . The final video rendering present a highly dynamic visualization of the text, conveying a strong sense of vitality and movement.\r
\r
Within the exhibition “From Inception: Wang Dongling 60 Years of Calligraphy", the videos showing the digital artwork "Virtual Reality Calligraphy:  Wandering Beyond " form part of an installation, that also includes mirrors and the monumental calligraphy work " Wandering Beyond: I" (Yi xie "Xiaoyao you" 一写《逍遥游》，ink on paper) realized by the artist in 2003.   This calligraphic work represents the artist's first large-scale calligraphic transcription of the text "Zhuangzi - Wandering Beyond", measuring 7,5 x 12,5 meters. In addition to this piece, Wang Dongling repeatedly engaged with the same text through multiple iterations, including: Wandering Beyond : II (Er xie "Xiaoyao you" 二写《 逍遥游》, ink on paper, 7,5 ×10 m, 2003); Wandering Beyond: III (San xie "Xiaoyao you" 三写《逍遥游》, ink on paper, 7,3 ×17,85 m, 2011); "Wandering Beyond" in Chaos Script (Xiaoyao you《逍遥游》, ink on paper, 3,65 x 4,32 m, 2015). \r
\r
"""@en ;
