    ns2:P571 "-0800"^^xsd:gYear ;
    ns1:description "The \"Classic of Poetry\" (Shijing 诗经), also known as the \"Book of Odes\" or \"Book of Songs\", is the oldest existing collection of Chinese poetry. It contains  305 works composed between the 11th and 7th centuries BCE. Traditionally regarded as one of the \"Five Classics\", it has been studied and memorized by scholars in China forsover two millennia. The Classic of Poetry is also a rich source of chengyu (four-character classical idioms), which remain part of both literary and everyday language in modern Chinese. Since the Qing dynasty (1644-1912), its rhyme patterns have been analysed for the reconstruction of Old Chinese phonology. "@en ;
    ns1:hasWikidataResource <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q465108> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/927> a ns3:Q184485 ;
