        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q943> ;
    ns2:P571 "2018-05-19"^^xsd:date ;
    ns2:P88 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q111020673> ;
    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/1212.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork, created from May 19 to 21, 2018, at the Berlin Mural Fest ‒ one of the world’s most prestigious international graffiti festivals ‒ stands as a monumental achievement by the ABS crew alongside numerous international graffiti artists. The piece shows a striking composition that blends traditional and modern elements. The lower section is dominated by intricate lettering/charactering and tags, highlighted in yellow, representing the crew's distinctive style and each member's unique contribution. Above, a fierce dragon is depicted in classical iconography: with a crocodile head, catfish-like whiskers, a mane, deer horns, and a sinuous, snake-like body. The dragon is shown spitting fire onto sea waves, from which inscriptions emerge, swirling amidst flames. Further adding to the piece's depth are various calligraphic inscriptions in Chinese characters, often accompanied by reproductions of Chinese seals bearing the names of the artists, sometimes in Latin letters. These elements infuse the artwork with cultural richness and artistic complexity, making it a standout example of contemporary graffiti. \r
In addition to the long red dragon and the yellow tag pieces, this huge masterpiece is also composed of several elements (from left to right):\r
1)a red-stamped section containing 16 tag/seals, each bearing the names of the artists who contributed to this collaborative creation: Smer, Max, Seven, Jer, Way Fan, Blood Bro, Ogs, Andc, Spade, Thorn Donis, Goes, Kayo, Neon, Zeb Roc Ski, Abs, and Tpm. Each tag, written in red Latin letters, is encircled to resemble an ancient seal.\r
2) An inscription in bold characters that reads “Pofanlong 破樊笼” (The birdcage has disintegrated), accompanied by a description of the main characteristics of Chinese dragons, which are said to “summon wind and rain (hufenghuanyu 呼风唤雨) and are omnipotent (wusuobuneng 无所不能)". This inscription refers to the massive and fierce red Chinese dragon that spans the entire wall. The dragon seems to emerge from the text, “haunting” the wall with its presence.\r
3) An inscription that reads "You ming zi yuanfang lai 有明自远方来", followed by a list of the writers’ cities of origin, serving as a modern colophon for these traveling artists. Translated from Chinese, it means: "Some people come from afar: Beijing, Tongchuan, Chengdu, Yinzhou, Wuhan, Chongqing. Greetings from China." This section also includes two seals: one with the inscription Zhongguo 中国 (China) and another with hujian 互鉴 (mutual learning).\r
4) The phrase "Joy in Bottle" (the title of the work), alongside Joybo’s tag/seal.\r
5) A bottle spills water, flooding the bottom of the piece, with numerous puppets inside.\r
6) The inscription "Erlingyiba 二零一八 (2018)", marking the date of creation.\r
While refining their technique, the ABS crew maintains their signature wild style, now more complex and enriched by international collaborations. The piece incorporates various wildstyle tags, distinct elements of Chinese culture (dragon, calligraphy, seals), Chinese writings and inscriptions (ranging from simple names to profound statements), and animated puppets that bring dynamism to the composition. The artwork’s creation involved a larger group of about ten writers, showcasing the crew’s ability to collaborate across cultural and national boundaries. The setting in Berlin's prestigious Mural Fest underscores the artwork’s global impact and recognition within the international graffiti scene. \r
In essence, this graffiti artwork by the ABS crew at the Berlin Mural Fest exemplifies their artistic evolution and prowess in blending traditional Chinese elements with contemporary graffiti techniques. It represents a harmonious fusion of cultural heritage, individual creativity, and collaborative spirit on a global stage."""@en ;
