        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2047> ;
    ns1:description "Digital No08-CH01, CH02 is a pair of works consisting of two standard-size, vertically orientated works (265 x 66 cm) and two miniature works (59,7 x 20.3 cm) realized by Wang Tiande in 2008.  Each work consists of two layers of paper – the top layer carries imagery and words created by burn marks, which is superimposed on another layer that carries other calligraphic marks. The artist writes calligraphies onto xuan paper and then enriches the images with cigarette burns, in a meditation on the precarious relation between permanence and fleeting efflorescence, between the material and the immaterial, between tradition and contemporaneity (Kuo 2010: 58). As in the other works of the \"Digital series\", there is no discernible content:  characters are intentionally devoid of specific meaning. The artist asserts that in the digital age, people are overwhelmed by a flood of information, often feeling compelled to interpret specific content, which leads on the contrary to a confusion of indistinct and fragmented information. By abandoning the normal process of reading, the artwork creates an intentional and inactive mode of communication—a purely artistic language of calligraphy. This results in a new aesthetic experience that deliberately diverges from the traditional standards of calligraphy, while the absence of content grants these works a more independent visual expression." ;
    ns1:hasArtworkType <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22669850>,
