    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2077.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """“Zhuangzi – On the Equality of Things/Tangerine” is composed of two parts: 1) the photograph of a tangerine in a state of decomposition that is overwritten with a calligraphic inscription (2010-2015), and 2) a calligraphic work where the different concentration of the ink in written characters suggests the form of the tangerine in the original photograph (2013).  In this second part of the work, all traces of photography disappear and are replaced by small characters tightly arranged in vertical columns and in cursive style. The opposition that arises from observing first the photographic work and then the calligraphic work makes clearer the sense of materiality and immateriality of matter recalled by the artist in the "Material Immaterial" series. As the title suggests, Chu Chu writes parts of the chapter from the "Zhuangzi" entitled “Discourse on the Equality of All Things”  (Qiwulun 齐物论). This text, through parables and allegories, explains how reality is dense with relativism and the human tendency to separate the world into categories (e.g., right vs. wrong). Through this text, Chu Chu reflects on the way we observe things and approach them.\r
This work is part of the series “Material Immaterial - Fruit” (2010-2015) that in 2012 with the addition of calligraphy evolved into another sub-series titled "Equality of things - Fruit".""" ;
