    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/240.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """This artwork  was originally part of a series entitled "Yishi de wangchao 遗失的王朝" (The Mythos of Lost Dynasties Series, 1983-1998). In this series,  Gu Wenda invents a new form of writing, based on the ancient seal-script characters, but these new characters are meaningless. Exploring the loss of meaning of writing, Gu Wenda reduces writing to a mere sign.\r
"Synthetized Words" was exhibited for the first time in 1985 during  the "Group Exhibition of the New Traditional Painting of Hubei Province" (Hubei guohua xinzuo yaoqing zhan 湖北国华新作请展), held at the Wushang Exhibition Center in the city of Wushang. On that occasion,  the work was presented as part of a series entitled "Mythos of Lost Dynasties - Tranquility Comes from Meditation" (Yishi de wangchao  - Jingguan de shijie 遗失的王朝 - 静观的世界 ) composed of five oversize hanging scrolls. These five artworks then have become part of the series entitled "Pseudo-characters Series" (Xugou wenzi xilie 虚构文字系列). The five artworks of the series feature characters hovering over or within surreal "splashed ink" landscapes or cloudscapes. This artworkk represent the center scroll of the series and it is composed of a single invented ideograph suspended over a landscape. The full ideograph is unreadable, but the three cursive-script components (yi 易, shen 申, shi 示 ) may be interpreted as the character for “unobstructed” (chang 畅 ) and that for “spirit” (shen 神). While Gu’s overriding purpose may have been to subvert the semantic function of calligraphy, his creation of a “new” symbol embodying the notion of an unfettered spirit is a powerful emblem of his wish to escape cultural stereotypes.\r
The arrangement of this work with one invented character suspended over a landscape established the pattern for most Gu Wenda's later works in the "Mythos of Lost Dynasties Series", such as "Form A: Flying Pseudo-Characters in Landscape" (1996-1997, total of 9 works), "Form D: Flying Pseudo-Seal Scripture in Landscape (1996-97, total of 9 works), "Form E: Flying Pseudo-Seal Script above Landscape" (1997-1998, total of 11 works), and "Form G: Flying Pseudo-Running-Standard Script in Clouds" (since 1998, total of 16 works). In the first of this series, there is an artwork very similar to "Synthesized Words" entitled "#A-2 Free Expression". \r
\r
"""@en ;
