    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/434> ;
    ns1:description """In this performance, Zhang Qiang introduces the new concept of “conceptual clothing” (guannian fuzhuang 观念服装) (Zhang 2017: 61-62). This is the first time that Zhang Qiang uses dresses for his "Traceology performances". For this performance, Zhang Qiang collaborates with Zhao Jingyu 赵泾羽, a Beijing fashion designer specializing in western styles who makes dresses for him out of white calligraphy paper. Her creations are put on by the professional model Cao Rui 曹蕊, who assists Zhang Qiang in his art by allowing him to paint on the paper dresses she is wearing. \r
A fundamental condition that emerges here is the "dressing up women's self" (nuxing ziwo de zhuang ban 女性自我的妆扮) (Ibid.). Cao Rui is no longer a passive model; rather, the collaboration unfolds naturally, grounded in a principle of parallelism. In the performance, the female performer, Cao Rui, wears garments designed by the female fashion designer Zhao Jingyu. Together, they form the female counterpart—a creative partnership in which both creation and performance coexist. The male counterpart, Zhang Qiang, through his performative writing, likewise embodies both roles simultaneously. As a result, the entire performance organically develops into a compelling exploration of “gender difference” (xingbie chayi 性别差异) (Ibid.)."""@en ;
