    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/385.jpg> ;
    ns1:description """The series begins in 2002 and ends in 2018. Zhang Qiang realizes collaborative performances of "Action Writing" (xingwei shuxie 行为书写). The artist experiments performances with both female artists' naked bodies and/or clothes made by fashion designers. In the second case, the female counterparts decide the design and material of the clothes they will wear.  Very often the clothes are made with a type of traditional silk called juan 绢, as a reference to the ancients: Chinese paintings before the Yuan dynasty, in fact, were painted on silk.\r
This series has three main features: \r
1. During the performance,  Zhang Qiang does not look at the counterpart's body, so the female counterpart has only the lens of the camera in front of her body. The artist's hand is in constant motion and holds a brush dipped in ink. The female counterpart constantly feels the existence of the "other" from the writing on her body through the brush. At the same time, since there is no direct gaze scrutinizing her body, she can ignore or even forget the existence of the "other" at any moment. During this process, approaching or avoiding the body will lead to distinct and unexpected movements.\r
2. The places of these performances are similar to "study spaces", with artificial lights, different scenarios and backgrounds.\r
3. The cooperative women are basically students of Academies of Fine Arts. These girls are immersed in the process of modern visual education and have fashion sensitivity, so they make unusual and personalized clothes. \r
This series has a subcategory called "Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/X Model" (Zhang Qiang zongji xue baogao A/X moxing  张强踪迹学报告 A/X 模型, 2013 - 2018). The A/X series is more experimental and "free" than the "A/C" series, because it puts more emphasis on the initiative of female collaborators.\r
The "Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/X Model"  consists of about thirteen "free performances" (ziyou xingwei 自由行为) . These performances place greater emphasis on the concepts and initiatives of the counterpart. For example in the performance entitled "Zhang Qiang Traceology Report A/X 7 (Zhang Kaini) [张强踪迹学报告A/X 7 (张凯妮）模型]", Zhang Kaini, the female counterpart, pays close attention to express her thoughts during the performance.  \r
\r
"""@en ;
