    ns1:calligrapher <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/100> ;
    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/516> ;
    ns1:description """In this performance, Zhang Qiang creates the so-called "Blinded Calligraphy" (mang shu 盲书): looking away, the artist holds up an ink-soaked brush, creating traces of ink while the female counterpart Ding Feifei 丁斐斐 moves a sheet of paper or silk over his head, as if to simulate the movement of clouds in the sky. However, as Ding Feifei points out, Yunshu 云书 is a work that Ding Feifei conceived and created together with Zhang Qiang, while Mang shu 盲书 is a work that Zhang Qiang conceived independently, inviting women to work with him. In fact, all materials and techniques used are chosen by Ding Feifei, who thus becomes a full-fledged collaborator and creator of the experimentation.\r
The performance lasts about half an hour (excluding the preparatory work). During the performance, relaxing background music is played. The music consists on various tracks collected in NetEase Cloud Music (Wangyi yun yinyue 网易云音乐), a freemium music streaming service famous in China. The performance produces three artworks in total (n. 51, 52 and 53)."""@en ;
