    ns1:description """These artworks are created during the performance Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/J 5 (Zhang Qingzhi) Model - The Divine Brush comes to Jingde [张强踪迹学报告 A/J 5 (张青枝) 模型 - 神来景德之笔]. It consists of about a dozen blue and white ceramic objects, with different shapes and sizes. At the time of decoration, a gray colored glaze (you liao 釉料), a material particularly used for Chinese ceramic painting, is diluted in water and then applied on ceramics. After entering the kiln and firing it, the color of the ceramic object turns into blue. For some glazes, it happens that there is no color difference before and after firing. In this case, the graze used has turned into a blue colour.\r
On the pottery there is also a "red sign" representing the two charaters of the female counterpart's name "青枝" (Qingzhi). """@en ;
