    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 1 Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is performed during the concert event Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会) and consists of the phrase in Chinese characters “Yingguo Zhongguo youyi wangguchangqing英国中国友谊万古长青” (Britain-China Friendship will Last Forever) created by the calligrapher Li Binquan together with the Professor Roger Mason (b.1941) : the first part “Yingguo Zhongguo youyi 英国中国友谊” (Britain-China Friendship) was written by Roger Mason, while the second part “wangguchangqing 万古长青” (will last forever) was written by Li Binquan."@en ;
