    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the concert entitled \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会)\", an event commissioned by the Chinese government to honour the Summer Olympic Games. It  consists of the characters realized by Li Binquan, composing the poem “Prelude to Water Melody” (Shui diao ge tou · mingyue jishi you 水调歌头 · 明月几时有) by Su Shi (1036-1101), who wrote these lyrics while he was drunk and missing his younger brother (Su Zhe) on the Mid-Autumn Festival of the year Bingzhen (1076)." ;
