    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 4 Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the concert entitled \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会)\", an event commissioned by the Chinese government to honour the Summer Olympic Games. It consists of the characters realized by Li Binquan reproducing the poem “Drinking Alone Beneath the Moon\" (Yue xia duzhuo 月下独酌) by Li Bai, a poem about loneliness and companionship, and the way alcohol blurs the line between the two." ;
