    ns1:attributedTitle "CWU 5 Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells" ;
    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the concert entitled \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会)\", an event commissioned by the Chinese government to honour the Summer Olympic Games. It consists of the characters realized by Li Binquan reproducing the poem “Qinyuan Spring · Snow” (Qinyuan Chun · Xue 沁园春·雪) written during the “Die Libelle, Polka-Mazurka”, by Josef Strauss and composed by Mao Zedong during the Eastern Expedition in 1936." ;
    ns1:hasBackgroundColour <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q23444> ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicLine true ;
    ns1:hasSignificance "Meaningful writing" ;
    ns1:isUnitOf <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1812>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/943> ;
    ns1:madeUsingTool <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q614467> ;
    ns1:numberOfCharacters 300 ;
    ns1:relatedUnit <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1796>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1799>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1801>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1809>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1816> ;
    ns1:transcriptionAndTranslation """My country’s northern scenery:\r
A thousand li encased in ice,\r
Ten thousand li of swirling snow.\r
The noble Wall surrounded on both sides\r
By only blank totality.\r
The Yellow River’s epic stretch\r
Locked into place, its torrents stilled.\r
The mountains, dancing silver snakes,\r
The highlands, charging elephants,\r
Triumphantly competing with the heavens’ lofty height.\r
And come a clear day,\r
The land adorned with sunlight, draped in white,\r
Seduces all who bear its sight.\r
 \r
That wondrous view, so dear and tender all at once,\r
Moved countless heroes, bowing from their waists, to pay their due homage.\r
Alas, for Zheng of Qin and Wu of Han\r
Grasped not the art of poetry,\r
While Zong of Tang and Zu of Song\r
Had not virile minds nor forms.\r
A generation’s pride and joy,\r
The fierce and mighty Genghis Khan,\r
Knew only how to shoot the condors up above the steppes.\r
They are but history,\r
For those who seek a greater figure yet\r
Must look toward this age alone."""@en,
        """北国风光，\r
千里冰封，\r
万里雪飘。\r
望长城内外，\r
惟余莽莽；\r
大河上下，\r
顿失滔滔。\r
山舞银蛇，\r
原驰腊象，\r
欲与天公试比高。\r
须晴日，\r
看红装素裹，\r
分外妖娆。\r
 \r
江山如此多娇，\r
引无数英雄竞折腰。\r
惜秦皇汉武，\r
略输文采；\r
唐宗宋祖，\r
稍逊风骚。\r
一代天骄，\r
成吉思汗，\r
只识弯弓射大雕。\r
俱往矣，\r
数风流人物，\r
还看今朝"""@zh,
        """Běiguó fēngguāng, \r
qiānlǐ bīng fēng, \r
wànlǐ xuě piāo. \r
Wàng chángchéng nèiwài, \r
wéi yú mǎngmǎng; \r
dàhé shàngxià, \r
dùn shī tāotāo. \r
Shān wǔ yín shé, \r
yuán chí là xiàng, \r
yù yǔ tiāngōng shì bǐ gāo. \r
Xū qíng rì, \r
kàn hóngzhuāng sù guǒ, \r
fèn wài yāoráo. \r
Jiāngshān rúcǐ duō jiāo, \r
yǐn wúshù yīngxióng jìng zhéyāo. \r
Xī qínhuánghàn wǔ, \r
lüè shū wéncǎi; \r
táng zōng sòng zǔ, \r
shāo xùn fēngsāo. \r
Yīdài tiānjiāo, \r
chéngjísīhán, \r
zhǐ shí wān gōng shè dà diāo. \r
Jù wǎng yǐ, \r
shù fēngliú rénwù, \r
hái kàn jīnzhāo"""@zh-Latn .

