    ns1:description "This CWU is part of the concert entitled \"Chinese Calligraphy, Music, and Dance Concert at Sadler's Wells (萨德勒之井中国书法、音乐和舞蹈音乐会)\", an event commissioned by the Chinese government to honour the Summer Olympic Games. It consists of some characters realized by Li Binquan representing some excerpts from “A Tale of Two Cities” (Shuangchengji 双城记) by the English writer Charles Dickens (1812-1870) written in Chinese. One example is: “It was the best of times, it was the worst of times” (in Chinese “Na shi zui meihao de shidai, na shi zui zaogao de shidai 那是最美好的时代、那是最糟糕的时代”)."@en ;
