    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/534> ;
    ns1:description """This performance takes place on February 1st, 2002 at the "Great Exhibition Court" of the London British Museum in occasion of the "Brushes with Surprise: The Art of Calligraphy in Modern China Exhibition" (Jingren zhi bi—xiandai Zhongguo shufa zhan 惊人之笔—现代中国书法展). In this performance, Zhang Qiang writes on clothes previously realized by himself. Zhang Qiang used a roll of silk (a type of silk called juan "绢") then folded it in half and created a slit in the middle, asking the models (Rachel and Claire Portal) to wear it. Zhang Qiang, looking away from the female counterparts  realizes calligraphic traces on the models' bodies and clothes. At the end of the performance, the "traced" clothes were exhibited in the museum.\r
A similar performance entitled "Zhang Qiang's Traceology Report A/C 4 Model - Enchanting Golden Wings (Zhang Qiang zongji xue baogao A/C 4 moxing - Jin yu yaorao 张强踪迹学报告A/C 4 模型 - 金羽妖娆)” was held the day after this performance (February 2nd, 2002) at the same place, with two models named Claire Portal and Zhai Teng 斋藤.""" ;
