    ns1:description "This performance took place on 30th May 2013, during the Exhibition “Splashed Ink at Venice - The performance of 'Vagina Font' Chinese Calligraphy: 'L’Internationale' and 'The Way of the Brush'” (Mo sa Weinisi - ji “b- ti” shufa biaoyan: “Guojige” yu “bimo zhi dao” shufa biaoyan ji 墨洒威尼斯 - 记 “bi - 体” 书法表演: 《国际歌》与《笔墨之道》书法表演记) in occasion of the “55th Venice Biennale Parallel Exhibition Chinese Independent Art Exhibition - Unseen Voices” (“Di 55 jie Weinisi shuang nian zhan pingxing zhan Zhongguo duli yishu zhan - weiceng chengxian de shengyin” 第55届威尼斯双年展平行展中国独立艺术展 - 未曾呈现的声音). In this performance, Sun Ping wears a white t-shirt with the black Chinese character meng 夢 (Dream) written in traditional form. Sun Ping assists his collaborator Luo Shan as she executes calligraphy using a brush dipped in red and black ink inserted inside her vagina. Luo Shan is half naked and wearing a red nightgown and a carnival mask (probably a tribute to the famous Venice carnival). Her movements attempt to reproduce Chinese characters, but finally result in a set of signs and dots. At the end of the performance, all the remaining ink was poured onto the exhibition board. The two artists stretched their hands upwards, in a gesture of sending fuck off."@en ;
