    ns1:description """Wang Nanming is a contemporary Chinese artist known for his contributions to ink painting and calligraphy. He was born in 1962 in Jiangsu Province, China. Wang Nanming is recognized for his innovative approach to traditional Chinese art forms, particularly in the realm of ink painting and calligraphy, blending traditional techniques with modern interpretations and incorporating elements of contemporary life and global influences.\r
Wang Nanming is known as one of the most critical voices in contemporary Chinese art criticism due to his sharp critique. He is both an interpreter and promoter of concepts such as "avant-garde art," "post-avant-garde art," and "Metavant-garde" (Geng qianwei yishu 更前卫艺术). At the same time, Wang is also an artist who integrates his thoughts and ideas into his creative practice. After creating the series "Balls of Characters" from 1989 to 1992, Wang's artistic direction shifted towards issues concerning art and society, which have been continuously presented in his work. His artworks have been exhibited widely both in China and internationally. In 2017 Wang Nanming was appointed as new Director of Himalayas Museum in Shanghai."""@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/788.png> .

