    ns1:description """Wang Yong, born in 1976 in Xuzhou, Jiangsu Province, currently resides in Beijing. He is a representative artist of the "New School of Beijing" (Xin jing pai 新京派) and of "Ten Ink" (Shi mo 十墨). Wang Yong holds an academic position at the Art Research Institute of the New Beijing School and serves as General Secretary of the New Beijing School. He is also a member of the "Hudson Artists Association" in New York and participates as a guest artist at the "Hudson International Art Exchange" and "Visiting Centre" in New York. His works are part of the collections held by the  Ferrari Group in Italy and various other institutions in China and internationally. He has published monographs such as "The New Beijing School - New Art by Seventeen Artists from China". In the realm of Chinese contemporary art, Wang Yong is reknowned for his "Hidden Ink" (Yin mo 隐墨).  In 2011, he named his works "Hidden Ink," using Zen (chan 禅) as a methodology and applying Zen approaches to contemplate and address issues.\r
"""@en ;
