    ns1:description """The exhibition "From Inception: Wang Dongling 60 Years of Calligraphy"  was held at the Zhejiang Art Museum in Hangzhou from 16 October to 14 November 2021. This retrospective exhibition included iconic artworks by Wang Dongling and represented the his largest solo exhibition. The exhibition was divided into four parts: Calligraphy (Shu 书), Writing (Fei shu 非书, Not-Calligraphy),  Chaos-Writing (Luanshu 乱书), and From Inception (Cong tou kaishi 从头开始). In particular, the four sections were structured as follows: \r
Part 1,  "Calligraphy" occupies two exhibition halls (5, 6). The first hall (Hall No. 6) features "Wandering Beyond: I, II, III" (2003) and other iconic hanging scrolls written using four traditional calligraphic scripts. The second hall (Hall No. 5), titled "Scholar's Snow Cave" (Shutang xuedong 书堂雪洞), presents small-sized works in regular script and big-sized works in cursive script, encompassing different calligraphic genres and materials such as handscrolls, album leaves, tablet inscriptions, screens, etc. This section showcases Wang Dongling's immersion and training in the calligraphic tradition and first examples of experimentation. \r
Part 2, "Writing (Fei shu 非书, Not-Calligraphy)" is composed of the installation "The Bamboo Path" (2017) situated in the gallery's glass-ceilinged corridor, and the section titled "Fantasy Land of Calligraphy" (Shulin Huanjing 书林幻境) in Hall No. 4. This section consists of colored album and newspaper leaves (i.e. "Dance" Wu 舞, 1989), abstract ink paitings (i.e. "Dark (Heaven) and Yellow (Earth)" Xuan huang 玄黄, 1998, and "Brush Array" Bi zhen tu 笔阵图, 2007), and writings made of white acrylic on transparent panels (i.e. "More than White” Fei bai 非白, 2013).\r
Part 3, "Chaos-Writing" (Luanshu 乱书, Entangled Calligraphy) is dedicated to Wang Dongling's Chaos Script (luanshu 乱书), including the installation "Drink Alone under the Moon, Raise a Wine Glass to Ask the Sky by Li Bai" (2019),   the iPad work "Filling the World with Love" (2021), "Wandering Beyond Chaos Script" (2015) and many other hanging scrolls and artworks realized by Wang Dongling using Chaos Script.\r
Part 4, “From Inception" (Cong tou kaishi 从头开始) featured collections of documents illustrating the artist's six-decades-long artistic exploration, in both its traditional and modern forms. \r
The exhibition "From Inception: Wang Dongling 60 Years of Calligraphy"  was sponsored by the Publicity Department of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (Zhejiang Province Committee),  the Hangzhou Municipal People’s Government,  the Ministry of Culture and Tourism (Zhejiang Province), China Federation of Literary and Art Circles (Zhejiang Province), Chinese Calligraphers Association (CCA), China Academy of Art (CAA) and Xiling Society of Seal Arts (XSSA). The organizers included the School of Chinese Painting and Calligraphy Art of CAA and Lanting Calligraphy Association."""@en ;
