    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/370> ;
    ns1:description """This Biface Graphy writing session was held at the "Venice Academy of Fine Arts", in occasion of the 2018 "Ink Art Week - Ink Riders (Yu mo 驭墨) Exhibit Vernissage". \r
In this "Biface Graphy" writing session, a scroll hangs vertically in-between the two artists Zhang Qiang and Lia Wei. The brushes thus not having to compete for a same surface, each one being able to freely occupy a whole side of the paper. The script is realized with calligraphic brushes and ink; it is not readable, but constructed through the interaction of the two brushes writing simultaneously, conscious of each other’s movement.\r
During the performance, the Italian cellist Paolo Santi played classical music on the cello, accompanying the writing session and contributing to the atmosphere of the moment.\r
At the end of the performance, the fifty meters long scroll is hung in the center of the room."""@en ;
