        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1517>,
        <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/1557> ;
    ns2:P856 <https://www.instagram.com/yellow_peril_crew/> ;
    ns1:description """Yellow Peril (YP) is one of the most important crews of the so-called “New Era of Chinese Graffiti” (2020-2024) in mainland China.  Yellow Peril, in Chinese Huanghuo 黄祸, was founded with the goal of promoting graffiti written in various Asian languages and includes members from all over the world. In China it is challenging to identify which writer belongs to which crew because crews are not confined to a single city and maintain friendly relations, but currently Yellow Peril seems to be composed of:\r
- Exas / Lingdan 灵丹 (fat_spoon_x)\r
- Zatou 杂投 / Zato\r
- Zeit / Shijian 時間 (z51tiez)\r
- Qizi 漆仔\r
- Baitekuai 百特快 / Batman \r
- Paradise / Tianguo 天国 (female?)\r
- Funk\r
- Elvis / Mao Wang 猫王 (Elvis Presley),\r
- Reset / Chongqi 重啟 / Qiren  奇人 (reset_swg)\r
- Dongbay 東北 (northeast)\r
- Meimeng (?).\r
The foundation of this crew is related to the Black Lives Matter protests in 2020. Following the death of George Floyd, Exas,  a writer from Beijing, decided to start Yellow Peril. He wanted to create a crew dedicated to supporting graffiti in Asian writings, and the timing seemed proper. He explained that since he listened to rap music and consumed other forms of Black culture, he wanted to do something to support the Black community. The Yellow Peril, originally a xenophobic term used to refer to Asian immigrants, had been reclaimed by activists during the 1960s civil rights movement and was aligned with Black power movements like the Black Panthers."""@en ;
    ns1:hasArtisticCollectiveType <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q11964195> .

<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/814> a ns3:Q215627 ;
