    ns2:P937 <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8686> ;
    ns1:description """Wang Tiande, born in Shanghai in 1960, is a contemporary Chinese artist. He graduated from the Chinese Painting Department at the Zhejiang Academy of Fine Arts (now the China Academy of Art; CAA) in 1988 and later earned his doctoral degree in the Calligraphy Department. He currently serves as a professor and dean at the Art and Design Department of Fudan University in Shanghai.\r
Wang Tiande's approach is the reimagination of traditional Chinese script and painting and his use of unconventional materials and techniques. One of his notable methods involves burning xuan paper with incense or cigarettes, creating unique textures and layers that add depth to his pieces. Wang's art explores the delicate balance between permanence and impermanence, material and immaterial, tradition and modernity. His innovative "Digital" series, inspired by his residency in Paris in 2002, merges contemporary art influences with his love for traditional ink techniques. In this series, he paints landscapes and calligraphies on xuan paper and enhances them with cigarette burns, blending painting and calligraphy in a rich and complex form. Wang's work has earned international acclaim and is featured in prestigious collections such as the Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Museum of Fine Arts in Boston, and the British Museum. Through his unique artistic vision, Wang continues to push the boundaries of traditional Chinese art."""@en ;
