    ns1:createsArtwork <http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/807> ;
    ns1:description """This performance took place at the Yulan Grand Theatre of Dongguan, on November, 25, 2017. In this performance, Pu Lieping together with other two calligraphers Wang Xiaoming 王晓明 and Wang Yong 王勇, painted in black ink the names of the “Twelve Beauties of Jinling” (Jinling shi’er chai 金陵十二钗) of the work “Dream of the Red Chamber” (Honglou Meng 红楼梦), a novel composed by Cao Xueqin 曹雪芹 (1710 - 1765) in the middle of the 18th century. On the notes of three traditional instruments such as the guqin 古琴 (a seven-stringed plucked instrument), the erhu 二胡 (a two-stringed bowed instrument) and the hengdi 横笛 (bamboo flute), played respectevely by Wang Kexun 王可逊, Ouyang Mingqiao 欧阳铭桥 and Liu Hanchao 刘汉超 the three calligraphers painted, on six different panels, the names of: Lin Daiyu 林黛玉, Xue Baochai 薛宝钗, Jia Yuanchun贾元春, Jia Tanchun 贾探春, Shi Xiangyun 史湘云, Miaoyu 妙玉, Jia Yingchun 贾迎春, Jia Xichun 贾惜春, Wang Xifeng 王熙凤, Jia Qiaojie 贾巧姐, Li Wan 李纨 and Qin Keqing 秦可卿.  \r
The music played by the musicians are the three most famous songs created for the tv series inspired by the novel in the ‘80: Daguan honglou大观红楼 (A Grand View of the Red Chamber), Honglou xuqu 红楼序曲 (Dream of the Red Chamber Overture) and Zang hua yin 葬花吟 (Song of Flower Burial). At first, all three calligraphers use black ink to complete their creation later by filling everything using the colours blue, green, brown, orange and red. """@en ;
