    sch:thumbnailUrl <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/thumbs/2076.jpg> ;
    ns1:description "Chu Chu (b. 1975) is a female artist whose holistic worldview is expressed through the union of photography, calligraphy and painting. Chu Chu is a prolific artist whose creative process is based on constant observation of the world, inner and outer, where feelings and thoughts originate. The latter are the preparatory engines for the creation of innovative works in which photography and calligraphy combine highlighting tangibility through the portrayed image, the imperceptibility of feelings through the use of ink and the instantaneousness of time with photography.  Originally from Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province, she has been exposed to the world of art from an early age. She learned painting from her father, who was a sculptor and a cartoonist. At the age of seven, she began the study of calligraphy. During the period of her doctoral research, she was supervised by the calligrapher Wang Dongling. Chu Chu is currently a professor at the China Academy of Art and Zhejiang University and a researcher emeritus of the Sanshou Calligraphy Society. Her background is not limited to the field of art, but she is familiar with literature, philosophy and poetry, which she incorporates into her works. She has exhibited her works at several solo exhibitions dedicated in China and abroad, particularly in the United States and Japan, but also in Germany and France (e.g. Art Basel, Frieze Art Fair, and Paris PHOTO)." ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Academic"@en,
        "Self-Taught"@en ;
    ns1:image <https://cloud.ditlab.it/public.php/dav/files/b49pfgPgPXNDFtc/2076.jpg> .

