    ns1:description "Qiu Zhenzhong was born in Nanchang, Jiangxi Province in 1947. He graduated with a Master of Arts degree from the Zhejiang Academy of Fine Arts (now China Academy of Art) in 1981. He is Professor of Calligraphy at the China Academy of Fine Arts (CAFA) in Beijing. He also serves as Director of the Center for Comparative Research on Calligraphy and Painting at CAFA and Director of the Orchid Pavilion School of Calligraphy in Shaoxing. He is Vice President of  Pan Tianshou Research Association and a member of the Chinese Calligraphy Expert Committee of the China National Museum of Art (NAMOC).  In 2008 he was appointed as consultant for Chinese calligraphy and painting at the Opening Ceremony of the Beijing Olympic Games. He is recognized as one of the leading figures in Chinese modern calligraphers. He has held numerous solo exhibitions in China and internationally. Major exhibitions include The First Four Series – Calligraphy by Qiu Zhenzhong (Zuichu de si ge xilie: Qiu Zhenzhong shufa zuopin zhan 最初的四个系列——邱振中书法作品展) at the National Art Museum of China (1989) and a solo show (Qiu Zhenzhong shufa zuopin zhan 邱振中书法作品展) at Galerie Saint-Légar in Geneva, Switzerland  (1996). He is also the author of numerous influential publications on the theory and practice of Chinese calligraphy." ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Academic"@en ;
