    ns1:description "Gu Wenda, born in 1955 in Shanghai, is a Chinese artist known for his conceptual ink art. He graduated from the Shanghai School of Arts in 1976 and received a Master of Fine Arts from the China Academy of Art (CAA) in 1981. Gu Wenda gained international recognition in the mid-1980s for his first exhibition in Xi'an, where he introduced his invented calligraphic characters, a hallmark of his work. After moving to the USA in 1987, he became a full-time artist and has since created influential pieces that blend his Asian heritage with global themes." ;
    ns1:hasCalligraphicTraining "Academic"@en .

