    ns1:description """Wu Xixia was born in 1993. She is an installation artist and designer, Co-founder of Macau Kun Studio and Kun Art &Culture (Zhuhai Hengqin). She graduated in Master of Fine Arts from the University of Massachusetts Dartmouth, her study focus on feminist philosophy, and she is currently studying for a PhD in Fine Arts (Theory of Art History) at the Macao University of Science and Technology. PhD. Her study focuses on "Performance Arts in Gender philosophy, and thesis" specifically regarding the "Non-maleness in the Symbolic Order: Phallocentrism and the Castrated Third Sex". Her works mainly use sociology and gender philosophy as raw materials to create performance art and installation art.\r
In 2022, "Non-Fountain" - Xixia Wu Solo Exhibition (Wu quan - Wu Xixia zuopin zhan 毋泉 - 吴析夏作品展) was held at the Oriental Foundation in Macao; in 2021, "Her Mountain" (Ta shan 她山) - Xixia Wu  Solo Exhibition (Wu Xixia ge zhan 吴析夏个展) was held in Beijing 798 Art District Songyang Art Museum; in the same year, "Transmutation" (Shanbian 嬗变) - personal exhibition was held in Zhuhai city (Guangdong). The performance art piece "Writing the Orchid Pavilion Once Time" (Shuxie Lanting Xu yibian 书写兰亭序一遍) has attracted widespread attention across various platforms; the work "Nativity Aphasia" (Dan· shiyu 诞·失语) was selected for the Lisbon Biennale in Portugal; "The Secret of the Body" (Shenti de mimi 身体的秘密) was selected for the Gwangju International Biennale (Korea) in occasion of the eighth exhibition of the YAA Asian Young Artists Nomination and "Plastic Girl " (Su nu 塑女) was selected for the 4th Lishui International Photography Festival 2021. In 2022 Wu Xixia was selected as one of the 100 most noteworthy young artists on Douyin. His works have been exhibited at Soprafina Museum of Art in Boston (USA); Virginia Spetco Museum of Art (USA); Umass Museum of Art (USA), New Bedford Art Museum (USA); Macau Visual Art Joint Exhibition; Macao Oriental Foundation; Macau MGM; Guangzhou Poly World Trade Center Expo; Guangzhou Yi Cube Museum of Contemporary Art; Zhuhai Unbounded Art Museum and other places."""@en ;
