    ns1:description """Silvio Ferragina is an Italian calligrapher actively involved in the panorama of contemporary experimental Asian calligraphy. He studied Chinese calligraphy for more than ten years and he took part in lots of calligraphic exhibitions around the world, especially in China, Korea, Japan, United States, Egypt, Switzerland and Italy. In addition to an artistic production of classical inspiration, his works consist of calligraphic paintings, calligraphic sculptures, calligraphic multimedia installations, live multimedia performances, and other experimental calligraphic forms. He is involved in the so-called “contemporary calligraphic movement”, which aims at a worldwide modernization of calligraphic art. In recent years, he devoted himself to an extremely ambitious project called “musicalligraphy” project that aims at combining calligraphy and music to create something new between the two. By matching "fundamental calligraphic strokes" to "musical notes”, he arrives at the transformation of a Chinese character into a corresponding musical melody, that sometimes is transposed into a “musicalligraphy” performance.\r
\r
"""@en ;
