    ns1:description """Luo Qi is an internationally renowned Chinese calligrapher and professor at the China Academy of Art in Hangzhou.  Born into a family of intellectuals, he studied calligraphy since he was a child and then he graduated from the Academy of Fine Arts of China in 1986. He has always been involved in the modern calligraphic movement aiming at a radical trasformation and hydridization of calligraphic art. He is the founder and the highest representative of “Calligraphyism,” the most significant post-modern calligraphy movement that emerged in China in the early 1990s. He is also the founder and the director of two important Chinese cultural institutions: the “Calligraphyism Research Center” (Shufazhuyi yanjiu zhongxin 书法主义研究中心) and the "Luo Qi International Contemporary Art Museum" (Luo Qi guoji dangdai yishuguan 洛齐国际当代艺术馆). Currently, he lives and works between Hangzhou (China) and Lisbon and frequently travels to Italy. \r
He works as the editor of several specialized journals, the curator of international exhibitions, and the author of countless texts about art and calligraphy. He is Executive Editor of the Belt and Road Cultural Journal of China’s Silk Road Art (Guangxi Publishing Group), Project Consultant of the International Conference on Portuguese Chinese Cultural Studies (University of Aveiro, Portugal), Founder of AAmA International Exhibition and AhA Asian Humanities and Arts Exhibition. Luo Qi has participated in numerous exhibitions worldwide, showcasing his works in prestigious institutions such as: Louvre, Accademia di Brera, Palazzo Ducale di Genova, United States National Gallery of Art, Tokyo Art Museum, National Art Museum of China, Brussels Modern Art Museum, Seoul Art Museum, ecc. His works are preserved within numerous museums and art galleries and have been auctioned by Sotheby's for tens of thousands of euros. Throughout his extensive career, he has received a numerous awards and recognitions both in China and abroad.""" ;
