<http://wendang-project.github.io/data/item/2635> a ns3:Q464980 ;
    ns1:description """Dedicated to the evolution of contemporary Chinese calligraphy, this exhibition explored new directions and expressions within the art form. Organized in collaboration with the Civic Museums Department of Bologna, the exhibition represented the final outcome of the research project “WRITE – New Forms of Calligraphy in China: A Contemporary Culture Mirror”, coordinated by the University of Bologna and funded by the European Research Council (ERC).
The exhibition explores the transformation of calligraphy into new artistic languages capable of reflecting the cultural and social changes of contemporary China. More than an aesthetic practice, calligraphy (shufa) has always been one of the deepest forms of artistic and intellectual expression in Chinese culture. Every mark becomes a visible manifestation of vital energy (qi), transforming gesture, rhythm, and emotion into form. Today, this millennia-old tradition is being reinterpreted through new languages, materials, and media.
Divided into four thematic sections—visual arts, graffiti, decorative and applied arts, and performance arts—the exhibition presented works ranging from abstraction to the pictographic, from invented and illegible calligraphies to experiments created with unconventional materials and tools. With more than 40 artists and over 55 works, it was the first exhibition of its kind in Europe."""@en ;
